// Multi-Level Record Speaking — mock testlar, namuna javoblar, rasmlar
window.SPEAKING={"mocks":[{"id":"b2t1","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":1,"p11":[{"q":"Have you ever bought clothes online?","a":"Yes, I actually shop online quite often. It's super convenient and saves a lot of time, especially when I'm too busy to go to the mall. I do check the size chart carefully though, because returning things can be a hassle. Sometimes the quality is surprisingly good, and other times it's a bit of a letdown. I also enjoy reading customer reviews—they help me decide what's worth buying. Overall, online shopping has become a go-to option for me."},{"q":"What is your favorite color?","a":"My favorite color is navy blue. It's such a classy and versatile shade-it works well for both casual and formal wear. I feel calm and confident whenever I wear it. It also goes well with other colors, so it's easy to match. I guess I've liked it since I was a teenager. It just suits my personality, I think."},{"q":"Do you use computers?","a":"Absolutely, I use computers every single day. They're essential for my work, studies, and even entertainment. I mainly use a laptop, which is portable and efficient. Whether it's sending emails, designing something, or watching videos, my computer is my main tool. I'd honestly feel lost without it. It's become such a huge part of daily life."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t1_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"The images depict two different work-life scenarios showcasing professional and personal multitasking. My initial impression suggests these scenes represent contrasting workplace dynamics - the first image showing a collaborative office environment, while the second portrays a work-from-home situation with parental responsibilities. In the first photo, multiple individuals are gathered around a computer, appearing engaged in a productive team discussion with positive body language and shared focus. The workplace seems professional, with individuals dressed in business attire and working closely together. The second image reveals a working mother balancing professional tasks with childcare, simultaneously managing a phone call and working on a laptop while her child is nearby."},{"q":"Which do you think is better for working in teams: working in an office or from home?","a":"Honestly, I think working in an office is better for teamwork. Face-to-face interaction makes communication smoother and helps build stronger relationships. It's easier to brainstorm and solve problems when everyone's in the same space. Remote work can feel isolating and sometimes causes delays. Of course, it depends on the type of work, but for collaboration, the office has the edge. Still, a hybrid model might offer the best of both worlds."},{"q":"Do you think companies save money if employees work from home?","a":"Yes, I do think companies save a significant amount when staff work remotely. They can cut down on expenses like office rent, electricity, and daily supplies. Plus, some studies show remote employees are even more productive. That means higher output with fewer overhead costs. However, they might need to invest more in tech and security. Overall, it's a cost-effective model for many businesses."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t1_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a time when you pursued an ambitious goal.","How did this experience change your understanding of ambition?","What impact does ambition have on people's lives and society as a whole?"],"a":"A couple of years ago, I challenged myself to become fluent in English within one year. At the time, it sounded a bit crazy, especially because I had a full-time job and very little free time. But I'd always wanted to speak English confidently, so I made a plan and stuck to it. I watched English series without subtitles, listened to podcasts while commuting, and practiced speaking every day—even if it was just talking to myself in the mirror. I also joined an online speaking club, which really boosted my confidence. It took a lot of discipline, and honestly, there were times I wanted to quit. But in the end, I reached my goal, and it felt incredibly rewarding. That experience completely changed how I view ambition. Before, I used to think ambition meant chasing something huge—like becoming rich or famous. But now I think real ambition is personal. It's about setting a goal that scares you a little, and then pushing yourself every day to get there. I realized that ambition doesn't have to be loud—it can be quiet, steady, and still life-changing. I think ambition plays a huge role in both individual lives and society. Ambitious people often inspire others, create change, and drive progress. At the same time, if ambition isn't balanced with patience and well-being, it can lead to stress or even burnout. But when it's healthy, it motivates people to grow, take risks, and improve—not just for themselves, but for their families, communities, and even the world. So I really believe ambition, when guided by purpose, can make a big difference."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t1_3.jpg","topic":"Countries should invest more in renewable energy sources.","for":["reduces dependence on fossil fuels","long-term economic benefits","more cost-effective and efficient"],"against":["xpensive initial investment in infrastructure","weather-dependent and unreliable.","challenging to transition without disrupting economies"],"a":"Well, this is definitely a hot topic these days! When I think about countries investing more in renewable energy, I see both clear benefits and some legitimate challenges.\n\nLooking at the advantages first, reducing dependence on fossil fuels is probably the most obvious one. I mean, we all know fossil fuels are finite resources that will eventually run out, right? By shifting to renewables like solar, wind, and hydropower, countries can secure their energy independence and not be at the mercy of oil-producing nations or volatile energy markets.\n\nThere are also substantial long-term economic benefits to consider. Initially, yes, the investment might seem high, but over time, renewable energy typically pays for itself. In my hometown, they installed solar panels on public buildings five years ago, and they're already seeing significant savings on energy bills. Plus, the renewable energy sector creates tons of\n\nnew jobs - from manufacturing solar panels to maintaining wind farms.\n\nI've also read that renewables are becoming more cost-effective and efficient every year. The technology keeps improving while costs keep dropping. Ten years ago, solar panels were way more expensive than they are now, and they're much more efficient today too.\n\nOn the flip side, I can't ignore some of the challenges. The initial investment in infrastructure is indeed expensive. Building wind farms, solar arrays, and upgrading power grids requires massive upfront capital that many countries, especially developing ones, might struggle to afford.\n\nAnother issue is reliability – renewable energy sources can be weather-dependent and sometimes unpredictable. When the sun isn't shining or the wind isn't blowing, you need backup systems. My cousin in Denmark tells me that even though they have lots of wind power, they still need conventional power plants for those still, cloudy days.\n\nThe transition also presents economic challenges. Moving away from fossil fuels needs to be managed carefully to avoid economic disruption in regions heavily dependent on coal mining or oil production. Many communities rely on these industries for jobs and local economies.\n\nIn conclusion, while there are certainly hurdles to overcome, I personally believe the long-term benefits of investing in renewable energy outweigh the short-term costs and\n\nchallenges. With careful planning and gradual implementation, countries can navigate the transition effectively and build more sustainable energy systems for future generations."},"words":[{"en":"Convenient","uz":"Qulay"},{"en":"Hassle","uz":"Qiyinchilik / Tashvish"},{"en":"Letdown","uz":"Ko'ngilsizlik / Umidsizlik"},{"en":"Go-to","uz":"Doimiy tanlov / Ishonchli variant"},{"en":"Classy","uz":"Nafis / Did bilan tanlangan"},{"en":"Versatile","uz":"Ko'p funksiyali / Har xil holatga mos"},{"en":"Match (well)","uz":"Yaxshi mos kelmoq"},{"en":"Portable","uz":"Oson ko'chiriladigan / Portativ"},{"en":"Efficient","uz":"Samarali"},{"en":"Essential","uz":"Zarur / Muhim"},{"en":"Multitasking","uz":"bir vaqtning o'zida bir nechta ishni bajarish"},{"en":"Collaborative","uz":"hamkorlik qiluvchi, jamoaviy"},{"en":"Productive","uz":"samarali, unumli"},{"en":"Body language","uz":"tana harakati, tana tili"},{"en":"Balancing","uz":"muvozanatlashtirish, bir nechta majburiyatni boshqarish"},{"en":"Brainstorm","uz":"fikrlar almashinuvi orqali g'oyalar yaratish"},{"en":"Isolating","uz":"ajratilgan, yolg'iz his qiladigan"},{"en":"Expenses","uz":"xarajatlar"},{"en":"Overhead costs","uz":"umumiy xarajatlar"},{"en":"Cost-effective","uz":"tejamkor, samarali narxli"},{"en":"Challenge oneself","uz":"O'ziga sinov qo'yish"},{"en":"Fluent","uz":"Ravon so'zlaydigan"},{"en":"Stick to (a plan)","uz":"Rejaga qat'iy rioya qilmoq"},{"en":"Boost confidence","uz":"Ishonchni oshirmoq"},{"en":"Discipline","uz":"O'zini boshqarish / intizom"},{"en":"Rewarding","uz":"Qoniqarli / mamnuniyat bag'ishlovchi"},{"en":"Life-changing","uz":"Hayotni o'zgartiruvchi"},{"en":"Drive progress","uz":"Taraqqiyotni harakatga keltirmoq"},{"en":"Burnout","uz":"Charchash / ruhiy charchoq"},{"en":"Guided by purpose","uz":"Maqsad asosida boshqariladigan"},{"en":"Dependence","uz":"bog'liqlik"},{"en":"Finite","uz":"cheklangan"},{"en":"Securing","uz":"ta'minlash"},{"en":"Substantial","uz":"sezilarli, katta"},{"en":"Efficiency","uz":"samaradorlik"}]},{"id":"b2t2","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":2,"p11":[{"q":"What is your town like?","a":"My town is pretty peaceful and laid-back, with a friendly atmosphere. It's not too crowded, so life here feels more relaxed. We've got some charming cafes, tree-lined streets, and a few scenic parks. Although it's small, it's well-developed and has everything you really need. I think it's a great place to unwind and escape the chaos of big cities."},{"q":"Who is your favourite sports person?","a":"I'd say my favourite sports person is Serena Williams. She's incredibly talented and has dominated tennis for years. I admire her determination and mental strength — she never gives up easily. Plus, she's a role model who inspires millions with her confidence and resilience. Watching her play is always thrilling."},{"q":"How often do you use the internet?","a":"Honestly, I use the internet every single day. It's essential for almost everything — work, staying connected, and even relaxing. I usually browse news, stream videos, or scroll through social media. It's become second nature to me. I can't imagine my routine without it now."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t2_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What can you see in these pictures?","a":"These images showcase different aspects of leisure time, contrasting a social picnic gathering with a solitary moment of personal freedom and adventure. I imagine that while the group in the first image is sharing stories and laughter over a summer picnic in the park, the solo traveler in the second image is experiencing a profound moment of liberation at sunset after completing a challenging hike to this scenic beach location. The picnic scene radiates warmth and companionship, with fresh food and casual attire suggesting a spontaneous gathering among close friends."},{"q":"Why do many people want to spend time alone?","a":"Many people want to spend time alone to recharge and reflect on their thoughts. Being by oneself can offer peace and quiet, which helps to relieve stress. For some, it's also an opportunity to focus on personal hobbies or passions without\n\ndistractions. Alone time allows individuals to escape from the pressure of social interactions, helping them to regain clarity and boost their creativity or productivity."},{"q":"When was the last time you hung out with friends?","a":"The last time I hung out with friends was just a few days ago. We went to a local café and spent hours catching up on life, chatting about everything from work to personal plans. We had a great time over coffee and enjoyed each other's company. It was refreshing to just relax and have some fun together, especially after a busy week. Hanging out with friends always helps to recharge my energy."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t2_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about something you did in your life that was a success.","How did this success impact your life and the people around you?","What role do hard work, talent, and opportunity play in achieving success?"],"a":"One of the biggest successes in my life was starting my own small business a couple of years ago. It began as just a side hustle — I was selling handmade items online, mostly to friends and family. But with time, I started getting more orders, and eventually, I turned it into a full-time job. At first, I had no clue if it would work out, but I stayed consistent, kept improving, and really listened to my customers. This success changed a lot in my life. Financially, I became more stable and even helped support my family. Emotionally, it gave me a huge confidence boost. My friends and people\n\naround me also felt inspired, and a few of them even started their own projects after seeing my journey. It's honestly such a good feeling to know that something I built from scratch is now making a difference. When it comes to success, I think it's a mix of hard work, talent, and opportunity. Hard work is non-negotiable — you've got to put in the hours. Talent definitely helps, especially if you're in a creative field. But sometimes, even if you have both, you need the right opportunity — maybe someone believing in you or just being in the right place at the right time. So it's really about the balance of all three, and not giving up when things get tough."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t2_3.jpg","topic":"Fast Food Restaurants Should Display Calorie Counts","for":["Helps people make informed dietary choices","Encourages healthier eating habits","Could reduce obesity rates"],"against":["Might not significantly affect eating habits","Can create anxiety around food choices","Focuses too much on calorie count, not on nutritional value"],"a":"So, the question is whether fast food places should show calorie information on their menus, right? It's actually something I've thought about whenever I grab a quick bite somewhere.\n\nLooking at the advantages first, I think transparency is really important when it comes to what we eat. When restaurants display calorie counts, consumers can make more informed choices about their meals. Like, I've personally been shocked sometimes when I realized that a seemingly harmless salad actually had more calories than a burger because of the dressing! This kind of information empowers people to align their food choices with their dietary goals. There's also the potential long-term benefit of reducing obesity rates, which is a major public health concern in many countries. When people consistently make lower-calorie choices, it could contribute to healthier weight management across the population.\n\nOn the flip side, there are some valid concerns about displaying calorie information. Research has shown that these displays might not significantly change eating habits for many people - we often eat fast food for convenience or taste, not nutrition. And honestly, sometimes we just want to enjoy our food without thinking about the numbers. Another issue is that calorie displays can potentially trigger anxiety around food for some people, especially those with eating disorders or unhealthy relationships with food. Finally, focusing solely on calories oversimplifies nutrition - a 300-calorie item with protein and fiber is very different from a 300-calorie sugary drink, but the calorie count doesn't reflect that nutritional difference.\n\nIn conclusion, while I generally support calorie displays for the sake of transparency, I think they're just one piece of the puzzle. The ideal approach would be to provide comprehensive nutritional information in a way that educates rather than shames consumers. Maybe restaurants could highlight their healthier options without making people feel guilty about occasional indulgences. After all, being informed is important, but so is having a healthy relationship with food."},"words":[{"en":"Laid-back","uz":"xotirjam, bemalol"},{"en":"Charming","uz":"jozibali"},{"en":"Scenic","uz":"manzarali"},{"en":"Unwind","uz":"dam olmoq, yengillik his qilmoq"},{"en":"Dominate","uz":"ustunlik qilmoq, hukmronlik qilmoq"},{"en":"Determination","uz":"qat'iyat"},{"en":"Resilience","uz":"chidamlilik, bardoshlik"},{"en":"Thrilling","uz":"hayajonli"},{"en":"Essential","uz":"zarur, muhim"},{"en":"Second nature","uz":"odat tusiga kirgan, tabiiy holga aylangan"},{"en":"Leisure","uz":"Bo'sh vaqt"},{"en":"Gathering","uz":"Yig'ilish"},{"en":"Libertation","uz":"Ozodlik"},{"en":"Radiates","uz":"Tarqatadi, yaltiraydi"},{"en":"Companionship","uz":"Do'stlik, birgalikda bo'lish"},{"en":"Spontaneous","uz":"O'z-o'zidan yuzaga kelgan"},{"en":"Recharge","uz":"Zaryad olish"},{"en":"Distractions","uz":"Chalg'ituvchi narsalar"},{"en":"Refreshing","uz":"Yengillashtiruvchi, tetiklantiruvchi"},{"en":"Side hustle","uz":"qo'shimcha daromad manbai"},{"en":"Consistent","uz":"barqaror, muntazam"},{"en":"Confidence boost","uz":"o'ziga ishonchni oshirish"},{"en":"Built from scratch","uz":"noldan yaratmoq"},{"en":"Non-negotiable","uz":"muqarrar, muhokama qilinmaydigan"},{"en":"Financially stable","uz":"moliyaviy jihatdan barqaror"},{"en":"Inspired","uz":"ilhomlangan"},{"en":"Creative field","uz":"ijodiy soha"},{"en":"Right place at the right time","uz":"qulay fursatda to'g'ri joyda bo'lish"},{"en":"Not giving up","uz":"taslim bo'lmaslik, voz kechmaslik"},{"en":"Transparency","uz":"oshkoralik"},{"en":"Empowers","uz":"kuch-quvvat beradi, imkoniyat yaratadi"},{"en":"Align (with goals)","uz":"maqsadlar bilan mos kelmoq"},{"en":"Obesity","uz":"semirib ketish (semizlik)"},{"en":"Public health concern","uz":"jamoat salomatligi uchun tashvish"},{"en":"Trigger (anxiety)","uz":"tashvishga sabab bo'lmoq, qo'zg'atmoq"},{"en":"Eating disorders","uz":"ovqatlanish buzilishlari"},{"en":"Oversimplifies","uz":"haddan tashqari soddalashtiradi"},{"en":"Indulgences","uz":"zavq olishlar, o'ziga ruxsat bergan lazzatlar"},{"en":"Healthy relationship with food","uz":"ovqatga nisbatan sog'lom munosabat"}]},{"id":"b2t3","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":3,"p11":[{"q":"Tell me about your first teacher. My first teacher was a kind and patient woman who made learning fun. She had this amazing ability to explain things in a way that made even the toughest subjects feel easy. I remember how she always encouraged me to ask questions and express","a":"my thoughts freely. Her approach to teaching was very personal, and I felt comfortable in her class. She inspired me to love learning and helped me develop a lot of confidence early on."},{"q":"Do you live in a house or a flat?","a":"I live in a flat, and I absolutely love it! It's located in a quiet area, which gives me peace of mind. The flat is cozy, with a modern design and a lot of natural light. The best part is that it's close to all the essential places like shops and transport, which makes life much easier. I enjoy the simplicity of living in a flat, as it requires less maintenance compared to a house."},{"q":"What do you like to do in the evenings?","a":"In the evenings, I love unwinding by reading a good book or watching a series. It's the perfect way to relax after a busy day. Sometimes, I go for a walk if the weather is nice, just to clear my head. I also enjoy cooking dinner and trying out new recipes. Evenings are my time to recharge, so I usually avoid anything too stressful."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t3_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"The images show a contrast between healthy eating habits and socializing with food. In my view, the first image depicts a woman preparing or enjoying a fresh salad in a kitchen with vegetables around her, while the second image shows friends gathering to eat what appears to be fast food or casual meals together. The group in the second image appears to be enjoying the social aspect of dining, with their focus on conversation and connection rather than the nutritional content of their meal."},{"q":"What are some of the biggest challenges people face in maintaining healthy eating habits?","a":"One of the biggest challenges is the fast-paced lifestyle many people lead. With busy schedules, it's easy to opt for quick, unhealthy food options. Another issue is the lack of awareness about proper nutrition, which can lead to poor food choices. Additionally, unhealthy food is often more affordable\n\nand accessible than fresh, nutritious options, making it harder for people to prioritize their health. Finally, cravings and emotional eating can also undermine healthy habits, as people sometimes turn to comfort food instead of making balanced choices."},{"q":"How can we make sure everyone has access to enough healthy food?","a":"To ensure everyone has access to healthy food, it's important to address both affordability and availability. Governments could provide subsidies for nutritious food and support local farmers to make fresh produce more accessible. We should also raise awareness about nutrition and promote cooking education so people can make healthier meals at home. Community gardens or food banks could play a role in providing fresh food to those in need. Collaboration between organizations and governments is key to solving this issue on a larger scale."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t3_2.jpg","qs":["Describe the time when you tried to do something but failed.","How did you feel about the situation?","What lessons can be learnt from failure?"],"a":"One experience that stands out for me was when I tried to run a half-marathon. I had been preparing for several months, training intensely and focusing on improving my stamina. I felt optimistic as race day approached, thinking I was fully ready for the challenge. However, when the day came, I faced unexpected difficulties. About 15 kilometers into the race, I started feeling completely exhausted and couldn't keep up with my pace. My legs felt like they were made of lead, and I hit a mental block that made it difficult to keep going. Ultimately, I had to drop out of the race, which was a huge setback for me after all the hard work I'd put in. At first, I was deeply disappointed. I had set high expectations for myself, and not finishing the race felt like I had\n\nfailed. I also felt a little embarrassed, especially when I had to explain to my friends and family that I couldn't make it. But as I reflected on it more, I began to accept the situation. I realized that sometimes, things don't go as planned, and that failure is a part of growth. In the end, it wasn't the end of the world, and it allowed me to reassess my approach to future challenges. The initial feeling of failure eventually turned into a determination to improve for next time. Failure offers us valuable lessons, like the importance of resilience—the ability to bounce back after setbacks. It also teaches you to manage your expectations better and not be too overconfident. I learned that failure isn't something to fear but rather an opportunity to grow and learn more about yourself. For me, it highlighted areas where I could improve, like pacing myself and recognizing my limits. The experience also showed me that perseverance is crucial in overcoming challenges, even when things don't go according to plan. Ultimately, failure doesn't define you; it's just a temporary hurdle on the path to success."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t3_3.jpg","topic":"Books Are Better than Movies for Storytelling","for":["Provides more detail and depth to the story","Encourages imagination and creativity","Books offer a personal interpretation"],"against":["Movies can visually bring stories to life","Quicker and more accessible than reading a book","Easier to share and discuss with others"],"a":"Well, I've been thinking about this whole book versus movies debate, and honestly, it's quite fascinating. Both have their merits, but I'd like to share my thoughts on why each has its strengths and weaknesses when it comes to storytelling.\n\nStarting with books, I think one of the biggest advantages is the incredible detail and depth they provide. When you're reading a novel, you get to explore characters' thoughts, motivations, and backstories in a way that's often impossible in a two-hour film. For instance, when I read \"The Great Gatsby,\" I was immersed in Fitzgerald's beautiful descriptions and nuanced character development that the movie adaptation just couldn't fully capture.\n\nAnother major plus for books is how they spark your imagination. When you're reading, your mind creates this personal theater where you visualize everything yourself. This makes the experience uniquely yours - my mental image of\n\nHarry Potter probably looks quite different from yours, and there's something special about that personal interpretation that movies simply can't replicate.\n\nOn the flip side, movies definitely have their own powerful advantages. The visual medium can bring stories to life in spectacular ways. Seeing the breathtaking landscapes of Middle Earth in \"The Lord of the Rings\" films creates an immediate impact that might take pages of description in a book. The combination of visuals, music, and sound effects creates this immersive experience that can be truly captivating.\n\nMovies are also much more accessible for many people. Not everyone has the time or inclination to sit down with a 500-page novel, but most can manage a two-hour film. This accessibility makes storytelling available to wider audiences, which is definitely valuable in our busy modern lives.\n\nLastly, films tend to be more social experiences. It's easier to get friends together to watch and discuss a movie than to coordinate reading the same book. This shared experience creates opportunities for immediate reactions and discussions that books often don't provide in the same way.\n\nIn conclusion, while I personally tend to prefer books for their depth and imaginative qualities, I think both mediums have their place in storytelling. It really depends on what you're looking for in your experience - the detailed, personalized journey of a book or the visually stunning, accessible nature of film."},"words":[{"en":"Patient","uz":"sabrli"},{"en":"Encouraged","uz":"rag'batlantirilgan"},{"en":"Confidence","uz":"ishonch"},{"en":"Personal","uz":"shaxsiy"},{"en":"Cozy","uz":"qulay"},{"en":"Natural light","uz":"tabiiy yorug'lik"},{"en":"Essential","uz":"zarur"},{"en":"Unwinding","uz":"dam olish"},{"en":"Recharge","uz":"tiklanish"},{"en":"Stressful","uz":"stressli"},{"en":"Contrast","uz":"Farq"},{"en":"Socializing","uz":"Ijtimoiylashish"},{"en":"Nutritional","uz":"Oziqlanish"},{"en":"Awareness","uz":"Xabardorlik"},{"en":"Accessibility","uz":"Mavjudlik"},{"en":"Affordability","uz":"Arzonlik"},{"en":"Subsidies","uz":"Subsidiyalar"},{"en":"Collaboration","uz":"Hamkorlik"},{"en":"Emotional","uz":"Emotsional"},{"en":"Balance","uz":"Muvozanat"},{"en":"Preparing","uz":"tayyorlanish"},{"en":"Optimistic","uz":"optimistik"},{"en":"Exhausted","uz":"charchagan"},{"en":"Mental block","uz":"ruhiy to'siq"},{"en":"Setback","uz":"tormozlanish, orqaga qaytish"},{"en":"Disappointed","uz":"hafsalasi pir bo'lgan"},{"en":"Embarrassed","uz":"uyalmish"},{"en":"Reassess","uz":"qayta baholamoq"},{"en":"Improve","uz":"yaxshilamoq"},{"en":"Perseverance","uz":"sabr-toqat"},{"en":"Fascinating","uz":"Hayratlanarli"},{"en":"Merits","uz":"Fazilatlar"},{"en":"Motivations","uz":"Motivatsiyalar"},{"en":"Nuanced","uz":"Nozik"},{"en":"Immersed","uz":"Botilgan"},{"en":"Interpretation","uz":"Tafsirlash"}]},{"id":"b2t4","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":4,"p11":[{"q":"Who do you get on best within your family?","a":"I'd say I get on best with my older brother. We've always been pretty close. We have similar interests, like sports and movies, so we can spend hours talking about them. He's also the one I turn to when I need advice because he's usually very level-headed. Growing up, we had a lot of fun together, whether we were playing games or just hanging out. I think what makes our relationship so strong is the fact that we can talk about anything without judgment."},{"q":"Do you do much exercise?","a":"Yes, I try to stay active as much as possible. I'm not someone who spends hours at the gym, but I make sure to do something every day. I usually go for a run in the mornings or hit the gym a few times a week. I also enjoy swimming, which I find to be a great full-body workout. Exercise has become a part of my routine because it helps me feel energized throughout the day. Plus, it's a good way to clear my mind and reduce stress after a long day."},{"q":"Have you ever given anybody flowers?","a":"Yes, I have! I gave flowers to my mom on her birthday last year. She absolutely loved them. I remember picking out the most vibrant bouquet I could find, full of her favorite flowers. It was a simple gesture, but it meant a lot to her. I think giving flowers is a nice way to show someone you care, especially if they've had a tough time or need a little cheer. It's a small thing, but it can make a big difference in brightening someone's day."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t4_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"The images show a contrast between traditional in-person shopping and modern online shopping methods. I believe the first image depicts two women enjoying a shopping trip together at a mall or shopping center, carrying bags and smiling, while the second image shows someone browsing clothing options on a mobile shopping app from the comfort of their home. Online shopping, as shown in the second image, offers convenience and efficiency, allowing people to browse countless options without the constraints of store hours or travel time."},{"q":"Is it easier to compare products online or in a supermarket?","a":"I personally find it easier to compare products online. The convenience of browsing through different websites at once makes it a lot simpler. You can quickly check prices, reviews, and specifications without walking around or waiting for help. Additionally, online platforms often have comparison tools that\n\nlet you see multiple products side by side. In a supermarket, while you can physically check items, it's much harder to get the same level of detail and variety in a short amount of time. So, for me, online comparison is definitely more efficient."},{"q":"Do you trust the quality of products more when shopping online?","a":"I'd say it depends on the product. For some items, like electronics or books, I tend to trust the online reviews and product descriptions more. I can get a good sense of the quality by reading other customers' experiences. But when it comes to things like fresh food or clothes, I'm a bit more cautious. I prefer to see and touch the items in person to make sure they meet my expectations. So, while I trust online shopping for certain products, I'm still a little skeptical when it comes to others. Overall, I think online shopping has come a long way, but there are still some areas where I prefer traditional shopping."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t4_2.jpg","qs":["Describe an achievement that you consider a personal success.","How did this success influence your approach to future goals?","How does the definition of success vary between cultures or individuals?"],"a":"One achievement I consider a personal success was completing a marathon last year. It wasn't just about finishing the race, but it was about pushing my limits and proving to myself that I could achieve something that seemed impossible at first. I had to train for months, work through injuries, and stay focused despite the challenges. When I crossed the finish line, I felt an immense sense of pride and accomplishment. It showed me that with dedication, even the toughest goals are achievable. This success definitely changed how I approach future goals. Now, I'm more confident in setting challenging goals for\n\nmyself, and I know that persistence is key. I also learned that progress isn't always linear, and sometimes setbacks can be part of the journey. I don't rush things anymore; I take the time to plan and prepare better, but I keep pushing forward, even if things don't go as planned. As for the definition of success, it really varies from person to person and culture to culture. For some, success might mean financial stability or professional recognition, while for others, it's about personal happiness or building strong relationships. In some cultures, success is more about collective achievement and family, whereas in others, individual success and self-reliance are emphasized. So, I think it's important to understand that success isn't a one-size-fits-all concept—it's something deeply personal and subjective."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t4_3.jpg","topic":"Parents should have the right to choose their child's school curriculum.","for":["Parents have a fundamental right to ensure their children receive an education that aligns with their values.","It encourages diversity in education, allowing for specialized or alternative learning methods.","It empowers parents to have more control over their child's future and academic success."],"against":["Standardized curriculums ensure equality and consistency across schools.","Parents may not always be informed enough to make the best decisions for their child's education.","Allowing too much choice could create inequality between schools and hinder social integration."],"a":"So, I've been thinking about this debate on whether parents should have the right to choose their child's school curriculum, and honestly, it's quite a tricky topic with valid points on both sides.\n\nTo start off, I believe there's a strong case for parents having input into their children's education. After all, parents do have this fundamental right to ensure their kids receive an education that aligns with their family values and beliefs. I know several families who chose alternative schools specifically because they wanted their children to learn in an environment that reinforced their cultural or religious perspectives, and that choice really mattered to them.\n\nAnother advantage is the diversity it brings to education. When parents can choose different curricula, we end up with\n\nspecialized programs like Montessori, language immersion, or arts-focused education that might better suit certain children's learning styles.\n\nHaving this control also empowers parents to be actively involved in shaping their child's future. When parents can influence curriculum choices, they tend to be more engaged in their child's education overall, which research consistently shows benefits academic outcomes.\n\nHowever, there are some significant drawbacks to consider. Standardized curricula exist for good reasons – they ensure all kids get a consistent education regardless of where they live.\n\nThere's also the question of expertise. While parents know their children best emotionally, they might not always have the educational background to determine what academic content is most important or developmentally appropriate.\n\nPerhaps the most concerning potential consequence is inequality. If we allow too much parental choice, we might end up with vastly different educational standards between communities, which could widen social divides rather than bringing kids together with shared knowledge and experiences.\n\nIn conclusion, while I understand the desire for parental control, I think the ideal approach is probably somewhere in the middle – a strong standardized core curriculum with some flexibility for schools and parents to customize certain aspects of education."},"words":[{"en":"Level-headed","uz":"salim fikrlash"},{"en":"Energized","uz":"quvvatlangan"},{"en":"Vibrant","uz":"jonli, rang-barang"},{"en":"Judgment","uz":"hukm"},{"en":"Routine","uz":"odat"},{"en":"Clear my mind","uz":"ongimni tozalash"},{"en":"Reduce stress","uz":"stressni kamaytirish"},{"en":"Gesture","uz":"imo, harakat"},{"en":"Cheer","uz":"xursand qilish"},{"en":"Brightening","uz":"yorqinlashtirish"},{"en":"Contrast","uz":"Farq"},{"en":"Convenience","uz":"Qulaylik"},{"en":"Efficiency","uz":"Samaradorlik"},{"en":"Specifications","uz":"Texnik xususiyatlar"},{"en":"Comparison","uz":"Taqqoslash"},{"en":"Cautious","uz":"Ehtiyotkor"},{"en":"Skeptical","uz":"Shubhali"},{"en":"Experience","uz":"Tajriba"},{"en":"Traditional","uz":"An'anaviy"},{"en":"Preferences","uz":"Afzalliklar"},{"en":"Achievement","uz":"Yutuq"},{"en":"Limits","uz":"Chegaralar"},{"en":"Dedication","uz":"Bag'ishlanish"},{"en":"Accomplishment","uz":"Natija"},{"en":"Persistence","uz":"Mustahkamlik"},{"en":"Linear","uz":"Chiziqli"},{"en":"Setbacks","uz":"To'siqlar"},{"en":"Progress","uz":"Rivojlanish"},{"en":"Recognition","uz":"Tan olish"},{"en":"Subjective","uz":"Subyektiv"},{"en":"Curriculum","uz":"o'quv dasturi"},{"en":"Fundamental","uz":"asosiy"},{"en":"Empowers","uz":"kuchlantiradigan"},{"en":"Thrived","uz":"gullab-yashnadi"},{"en":"Standardized","uz":"standartlashtirilgan"}]},{"id":"b2t5","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":5,"p11":[{"q":"What is your town like?","a":"Well, my town is quite peaceful and charming. It's not too big, but it has all the essentials — nice cafés, cozy parks, and friendly neighbors. I'd say it has a laid-back vibe, which makes it perfect for unwinding after a hectic day. The air is cleaner than in big cities, and people here are pretty down-to-earth. Honestly, it's easy to feel at home here."},{"q":"Who is your favourite sports person?","a":"I'd say Serena Williams, without a doubt. She's not just insanely talented but also incredibly resilient. Watching her dominate the tennis court is honestly inspiring. Her determination and mental toughness set her apart. Plus, she's been a role model for so many young athletes, including me."},{"q":"How often do you use the internet?","a":"I use the internet every single day — probably more than I should! Whether it's for work, studying, or just scrolling through social media, it's become a big part of my routine. I also watch a lot of videos and listen to podcasts online. It's super convenient, though sometimes I wish I could unplug more often."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t5_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What can you see in these pictures?","a":"Looking at these pictures, I can see two different dining experiences - one showing a woman eating alone at a restaurant, while the other depicts a lively family meal at home. I guess, in the first image, a young woman is savoring a meal by herself in what seems to be an upscale establishment. The solitary diner appears to be completely immersed in her meal, cutting her food with precision and focus, suggesting a moment of personal enjoyment or perhaps a brief respite from a busy day. In contrast, the family setting radiates conviviality, with what looks like the father playfully using food items as glasses while the mother and children react with evident amusement."},{"q":"Do you prefer dining with family or alone?","a":"I definitely prefer dining with my family. There's something special about sharing a meal together—it's a time to chat, laugh, and enjoy each other's company. It makes the experience much more enjoyable and meaningful. Eating alone can be\n\npeaceful, but it doesn't have the same warmth or connection. Plus, family meals are a great way to stay close and create lasting memories. So, I try to make it a point to dine with my family as often as possible."},{"q":"When was the last time you gathered with family to dine?","a":"The last time we gathered for a family meal was just last Sunday. It was a casual get-together at my parents' house. We cooked a big meal and spent the afternoon chatting and catching up. It was a lovely time to relax and bond, especially since everyone has such busy schedules. We usually try to do this every couple of weeks, and it's always a highlight of the month."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t5_2.jpg","qs":["Describe a book that seriously impact you.","How did the book make you feel when you first read it?","Has this book influenced your other reading choices, or shaped your taste in literature?"],"a":"One book that seriously impacted me was \"The Alchemist\" by Paulo Coelho. I read it for the first time when I was going through a period of self-reflection and looking for direction in my life. The story of Santiago, the young shepherd who sets out on a journey to find his \"Personal Legend,\" really resonated with me. It's a simple story, but it's filled with profound lessons about following your dreams, listening to your heart, and embracing the journey, not just the destination. When I first read it, I felt a sense of peace and motivation. It made me think about my own life and whether I was truly pursuing what I loved or simply going along with what others expected of me. It was one of those books that made me stop and reflect deeply, almost like a wake-up call. The way Coelho blends elements of adventure, spirituality, and philosophy in a story that's both easy to read and thought-\n\nprovoking really stuck with me. I think it was the first book that made me understand how literature can go beyond just telling a story—it can inspire change in the reader. After reading \"The Alchemist,\" I became more interested in books that explore self-discovery and personal growth. It made me gravitate towards philosophical novels, books on mindfulness, and even poetry. I started seeking out works that challenged me to think differently about life, to question my assumptions, and to explore deeper meanings in everyday experiences. In a way, it shaped the way I approach books today—I'm less interested in pure entertainment now and more drawn to works that make me think, reflect, or change in some way. The influence of this book also changed the way I read. I became more intentional in my choices, looking for books that had an emotional or intellectual impact on me rather than just books to pass the time. It made me realize how powerful literature can be in shaping your thoughts and perspective on life. Even now, I often return to it when I need some inspiration or just want to reconnect with that sense of purpose and possibility it gave me when I first read it."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t5_3.jpg","topic":"Everyone Should Have a Hobby","for":["Provides a healthy way to relieve stress","Encourages creativity and personal growth","Can build new skills and knowledge"],"against":["Not everyone has the time or resources","Some hobbies can be expensive or risky","Can become an obsession if not balanced"],"a":"preparation\n\nWell, I've been thinking about whether everyone should have a hobby, and I believe this is quite an interesting topic to discuss.\n\nOn the one hand, hobbies definitely provide a healthy outlet for stress relief. After a long day at work or school, doing something you genuinely enjoy can help clear your mind and boost your mood. I've noticed this myself – whenever I feel overwhelmed, spending even just half an hour on my favorite activity makes a world of difference to my mental state. Hobbies also encourage creativity and personal development in ways that our regular jobs or studies might not. They allow us to express ourselves without the pressure of being perfect. Plus, through hobbies, we can build valuable skills and knowledge. For instance, someone who enjoys woodworking might develop\n\npractical skills that could even become useful professionally someday.\n\nOn the other hand, I have to acknowledge that not everyone has the luxury of time or resources to pursue hobbies. Many people are juggling multiple jobs or family responsibilities, making it difficult to carve out personal time. It's a bit privileged to assume everyone can afford this luxury. Another drawback is that some hobbies can be quite expensive or even risky. Photography equipment costs a fortune, and hobbies like rock climbing or motorsports carry physical risks that not everyone is comfortable with. I should also mention that hobbies can sometimes become unhealthy obsessions if not balanced properly. I've seen friends who became so consumed by their interests that other important aspects of their lives suffered.\n\nIn conclusion, while I think hobbies offer tremendous benefits for stress management, personal growth, and skill development, I understand they're not accessible or beneficial for everyone in the same way. Perhaps instead of saying everyone \"should\" have a hobby, it's better to say everyone deserves the opportunity to explore interests that bring them joy, in whatever capacity fits their life circumstances."},"words":[{"en":"Peaceful","uz":"Tinch"},{"en":"Charming","uz":"Jozibali"},{"en":"Laid-back","uz":"Xotirjam"},{"en":"Down-to-earth","uz":"Sodda"},{"en":"Resilient","uz":"Bardoshli"},{"en":"Dominate","uz":"Ustun bo'lmoq"},{"en":"Mental toughness","uz":"Ruhiy barqarorlik"},{"en":"Routine","uz":"Kundalik tartib"},{"en":"Convenient","uz":"Qulay"},{"en":"Unplug","uz":"Internetdan uzoqlashmoq"},{"en":"Savoring","uz":"ta'mini his qilmoq"},{"en":"Upscale","uz":"yuqori darajali"},{"en":"Immersed","uz":"berilib ketgan"},{"en":"Respite","uz":"nafas olish imkoniyati"},{"en":"Conviviality","uz":"dilkashlik"},{"en":"Connection","uz":"Aloqa"},{"en":"Lasting","uz":"Doimiy, uzoq davom etadigan"},{"en":"Resonated","uz":"ta'sir qildi"},{"en":"Reflection","uz":"o'zini tahlil qilish"},{"en":"Personal Legend","uz":"shaxsiy afsona"},{"en":"Profound","uz":"chuqur"},{"en":"Motivation","uz":"rag'bat"},{"en":"Gravitate","uz":"tortilmoq"},{"en":"Self-discovery","uz":"o'zini anglash"},{"en":"Mindfulness","uz":"hozirgi paytda bo'lish"},{"en":"Intentional","uz":"maqsadli"},{"en":"Reconnect","uz":"qayta bog'lanish"},{"en":"Outlet (for stress)","uz":"chiqish yo'li"},{"en":"Overwhelming","uz":"haddan tashqari ko'p/og'ir"},{"en":"Carve out (time)","uz":"vaqt ajratmoq"},{"en":"Privilege","uz":"imtiyoz"},{"en":"Drawback","uz":"kamchilik"},{"en":"Consumed (by interest)","uz":"qiziqish bilan band bo'lmoq"},{"en":"Tremendous","uz":"juda katta"}]},{"id":"b2t6","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":6,"p11":[{"q":"Tell me about a typical weekend for you. On weekends, I usually unwind by catching up on sleep and spending quality time with friends or family. I often go for a walk in the park or explore a new café. Sometimes, I binge-watch a series if the weather's gloomy. It's a good chance to","a":"recharge before the busy week kicks in. I try to keep things spontaneous and relaxing."},{"q":"What do you usually eat for breakfast?","a":"I usually keep it simple but nutritious. A bowl of oatmeal with fresh fruit and a cup of green tea is my go-to. Occasionally, I treat myself to an omelet or avocado toast. I avoid heavy foods in the morning since I like to start my day feeling light and energetic. Breakfast really sets the tone for the day."},{"q":"What do you do to stay healthy?","a":"To stay healthy, I try to maintain a balanced diet and stay active. I hit the gym a few times a week, and I also walk a lot instead of taking the bus. I drink plenty of water and make sure I get enough sleep. Mental health is just as important, so I take breaks and do some mindfulness exercises. It's all about consistency, really."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t6_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b2t6_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"Looking at these pictures, I can see two very different scenarios involving photography - one casual and self-directed, the other professional and structured. I guess, in the first image, a young woman is taking a selfie outdoors while holding a takeaway coffee cup, The woman in the pink dress radiates spontaneity and lightheartedness as she captures her own image, perhaps for social media, with natural daylight illuminating her cheerful expression. In contrast, the studio scene conveys a more deliberate atmosphere, with the subject striking a thoughtful pose while the photographer meticulously adjusts their equipment to achieve the perfect shot."},{"q":"Do you prefer taking a selfie or regular photo?","a":"I'd say I prefer taking a regular photo. While selfies are fun and convenient, regular photos often capture a more natural moment and allow for better composition. You can also include more people in the shot, which makes it more meaningful,\n\nespecially during special occasions. Selfies can sometimes feel a bit forced, whereas a candid shot with others can tell a richer story. So, I go for regular photos whenever possible."},{"q":"When was the last time you took a photo of yourself?","a":"The last time I took a photo of myself was last weekend when I was out with friends. We were at a café, and I snapped a quick selfie to capture the moment. It wasn't anything too fancy, just a fun shot to remember the day. I don't take selfies often, but when I do, it's usually during an enjoyable outing or event."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t6_2.jpg","qs":["Describe a cultural or family tradition that you celebrate.","How does this tradition bring your family closer together?","Has this tradition influenced your values or outlook on life in any way?"],"a":"One of the most special family traditions we celebrate is New Year's Eve. Every year, our family gathers at my grandparents' house, and it's always filled with warmth, laughter, and a lot of food. The night begins with a big family dinner where everyone contributes a dish, usually something that has been passed down through generations. After dinner, we play games, share stories from the past year, and even create resolutions for the new year. Just before midnight, we all go outside to light sparklers and watch fireworks. It's a tradition that has been in our family for as long as I can remember, and it really brings us closer together. This tradition makes us feel connected, not just to each other, but also to our roots. It reminds us of our shared history and the importance of family bonds. Even though we all have our own busy lives, this event is something we prioritize, and it creates a sense of continuity. It's a time when everyone comes together, no matter where we are or what we're doing in our personal lives. I think this tradition has influenced my outlook on life in a big way. It has taught me the value of family, unity, and taking the time to celebrate small moments together. It also reminds me of the importance of gratitude and reflecting on the year gone by. As I've grown older, I've learned to appreciate these moments even more. It's easy to get caught up in daily routines, but these traditions remind me to slow down, appreciate what I have, and focus on what truly matters: the people we love."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t6_3.jpg","topic":"Fast Food Should Be Heavily Taxed","for":["Discourages unhealthy eating habits","Raises funds for healthcare and nutrition programs","Promotes awareness of better dietary choices"],"against":["Affects low-income families more than others","Could hurt businesses and lead to job losses","People should have the freedom to choose their diet"],"a":"Well, this is definitely a hot topic these days. I'm going to discuss whether we should put heavy taxes on fast food, looking at both sides of the argument.\n\nWhen it comes to supporting this idea, there are several compelling points. First, higher taxes could discourage unhealthy eating habits, which might help tackle the growing obesity crisis we're facing. I mean, if a burger suddenly costs twice as much, I'd probably think twice before ordering it regularly. Also, the money raised through these taxes could fund healthcare and nutrition programs, essentially using the problem to pay for its own solution. That seems pretty smart, right? And let's not forget that these taxes might raise awareness about healthier dietary choices, pushing people to consider what they're eating more carefully.\n\nOn the flip side, there are serious concerns about this approach. The most troubling issue is that these taxes would hit\n\nlow-income families the hardest, since they often rely on fast food as an affordable option. It seems unfair to make life even more expensive for people who are already struggling financially. There's also the economic impact to consider – these taxes could harm fast food businesses and potentially lead to job losses in an industry that employs millions of people. And finally, many argue that people should have the freedom to choose their own diet without government interference through taxation – it feels a bit like overstepping boundaries.\n\nIn conclusion, while taxing fast food might help improve public health, we need to carefully consider the social and economic consequences. Perhaps a better approach would be combining moderate taxation with better education and making healthy food more affordable and accessible for everyone."},"words":[{"en":"Unwind","uz":"Dam olish"},{"en":"Quality time","uz":"Mazmunli vaqt"},{"en":"Binge-watch","uz":"Ketma-ket ko'p serial ko'rmoq"},{"en":"Recharge","uz":"Quvvat yig'moq"},{"en":"Spontaneous","uz":"O'z-o'zidan yuz beradigan"},{"en":"Nutritious","uz":"To'yimli"},{"en":"Go-to","uz":"Doimiy tanlanadigan narsa"},{"en":"Balanced diet","uz":"Muvozanatli ovqatlanish"},{"en":"Mindfulness","uz":"Ongli xotirjamlik"},{"en":"Consistency","uz":"Barqarorlik"},{"en":"Scenario","uz":"vaziyat"},{"en":"Self-directed","uz":"o'zi boshqaradigan"},{"en":"Spontaneity","uz":"tabiiylik"},{"en":"Illuminating","uz":"yorituvchi"},{"en":"Deliberate","uz":"ongli, ataylab"},{"en":"Meaningful","uz":"Ma'noli"},{"en":"Occasion","uz":"Holat, voqea"},{"en":"Snap","uz":"Tezda suratga olish"},{"en":"Outing","uz":"Chiqish, sayr"},{"en":"Enjoyable","uz":"Yoqimli"},{"en":"Special","uz":"maxsus"},{"en":"Contributes","uz":"hissa qo'shadi"},{"en":"Passed down","uz":"avloddan-avlodga o'tgan"},{"en":"Resolutions","uz":"qarorlar"},{"en":"Continuity","uz":"uzluksizlik"},{"en":"Prioritize","uz":"ustuvor qilish"},{"en":"Unity","uz":"birlik"},{"en":"Compelling","uz":"ishontiruvchi"},{"en":"Tackle","uz":"kurashmoq"},{"en":"Obesity crisis","uz":"semizlik inqirozi"},{"en":"Essentially","uz":"asosan"},{"en":"Troubling","uz":"tashvishli"},{"en":"Rely on","uz":"tayanmoq"},{"en":"Impact","uz":"ta'sir"}]},{"id":"b2t7","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":7,"p11":[{"q":"Do you have a pet?","a":"Yes, I have a cat named Luna. She's super affectionate and loves following me around the house like a shadow. Having her around makes my place feel cozy, and honestly, she helps me unwind after a long day. I never thought I'd be a cat person, but now I can't imagine life without her."},{"q":"How often do you read books?","a":"I try to read a few times a week, usually before bed. It helps me relax and disconnect from screens. I'm into self-development and fiction, so I switch between the two depending on my mood. Sometimes I get hooked and finish a book in a couple of days. It really depends on how busy I am."},{"q":"Who is your favourite actor or actress?","a":"I'd say my favourite actor is Leonardo DiCaprio. I admire how he chooses roles that are both intense and meaningful. He's incredibly versatile—from action to drama, he nails every performance. Plus, he's been consistent for years, which is pretty rare in the film industry."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t7_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"I can see two different modes of transportation in these pictures. I guess, in the first image, a man is driving a car with a woman sitting in the back seat, while the second one shows various people riding on public transportation, specifically a bus. The man driving the car appears quite cheerful, with a bright smile as he grips the steering wheel, suggesting he's enjoying the journey or perhaps having a pleasant conversation with his passenger. In the second image, there's a diverse group of passengers on the bus, including elderly people, young adults, and people from different backgrounds, all going about their day."},{"q":"What are the advantages of taking a bus instead of a taxi?","a":"Taking a bus is much more economical, especially if you're traveling a longer distance. It's also more environmentally friendly since it reduces the number of cars on the road. Plus,\n\nbuses usually have dedicated lanes, so they can sometimes avoid traffic jams. It's definitely a more sustainable and budget-friendly option."},{"q":"Do you prefer to travel by bus or by taxi?","a":"I generally prefer taking a bus, especially for short trips. It's more relaxing for me because I don't have to worry about the cost, and I can just enjoy the view or listen to music. Taxis are convenient when I'm in a rush or if the weather's bad, but buses are my go-to for the daily commute."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t7_2.jpg","qs":["Describe a time in your life when you experienced a significant change.","How has this change affected your personal growth or outlook on life?","Why do you think people sometimes struggle with change?"],"a":"One of the most significant changes in my life happened when I moved to a new city for university. I had spent my whole life in a small town, so the idea of moving to a big, bustling city was both exciting and intimidating. I was leaving behind everything I knew—my family, friends, and the familiar routine—and stepping into a completely new environment. The first few months were challenging because I had to adapt to everything: a new lifestyle, new people, and a more fast-paced way of living. I missed home, felt a bit isolated at times, and struggled to find my place. But over time, I began to embrace the change. I started to enjoy the independence, and I learned to navigate the city, make new friends, and manage my time more effectively. I think the experience really pushed me to step out of my comfort zone, and it made me realize how much I could grow when I faced challenges head-on. This change taught me to be more adaptable and open-minded, especially when meeting people from different backgrounds and cultures. It also helped me build confidence in my ability to handle uncertainty and deal with whatever life throws my way. As for why people struggle with change, I think it's often because we get comfortable with the familiar. Change can be unsettling, and when things are uncertain, it's easy to feel anxious or insecure. A lot of people fear the unknown and worry about losing control or making mistakes. But I've learned that change, though difficult at first, is an opportunity for growth and learning. It's how we evolve and move forward in life, and even though it can be uncomfortable, it's something worth embracing. In fact, I think the best things in life often come from the changes we least expect."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t7_3.jpg","topic":"Sports teams should be allowed to pay players based on their performance.","for":["Performance-based pay encourages athletes to give their best and can improve overall team performance.","It rewards hard work and skill, which can inspire other athletes.","It can make teams more competitive and financially efficient."],"against":["This system may lead to unhealthy competition and pressure on players.","It may cause inequality within teams, as some players may not have the same opportunities to showcase their talents.","Performance-based pay could lead to players focusing more on individual success rather than team cooperation."],"a":"So, let's talk about whether sports teams should pay athletes based on how well they perform. This is actually something I've thought about quite a bit as a sports fan.\n\nLooking at the positives first, performance-based pay really does seem to motivate players to give their absolute best on the field or court. I mean, if you know your salary depends on how many goals you score or games you win, you're probably going to push yourself harder, right? This naturally leads to better team performance overall, which benefits everyone - the team, the fans, everybody. Also, this system rewards hard work and skill in a very transparent way. When players see their teammates getting bonuses for exceptional performances, it can create a culture where everyone strives to improve. From a business perspective, it also makes teams more financially efficient since they're investing more in players who actually\n\ndeliver results rather than paying huge salaries to players who might underperform.\n\nHowever, there are some serious downsides to consider. The pressure this system puts on players can become really unhealthy. Imagine knowing that every missed shot or bad game directly affects your ability to pay your bills - that's an enormous mental burden that could actually hurt performance in the long run. There's also the issue of inequality within teams. Not all positions have equal opportunities to shine - a defender rarely scores goals, but that doesn't mean they're not crucial to the team's success. Performance pay might undervalue these less visible but essential roles. Perhaps the biggest concern is how this approach might damage team spirit. If everyone's focused on their individual stats to maximize their own paycheck, the collaborative nature of team sports could suffer dramatically.\n\nIn conclusion, while performance-based pay has clear motivational benefits, the potential damage to player wellbeing and team cohesion suggests that a balanced approach might work better - perhaps a combination of base salary with reasonable performance incentives that reward both individual excellence and team success."},"words":[{"en":"Cheerful","uz":"Xursand"},{"en":"Grip","uz":"Ushlamoq"},{"en":"Journey","uz":"Sayohat"},{"en":"Passenger","uz":"Yo'lovchi"},{"en":"Diverse","uz":"Turli"},{"en":"Economical","uz":"Tejamkor"},{"en":"Environmentally friendly","uz":"Atrof-muhitga foydali"},{"en":"Sustainable","uz":"Barqaror"},{"en":"Budget-friendly","uz":"Arzon narxlarda"},{"en":"Significant","uz":"Muhim"},{"en":"Intimidating","uz":"Qo'rqituvchi, qo'rquv tug'diradigan"},{"en":"Adopt","uz":"Moslashmoq"},{"en":"Isolated","uz":"Yolg'iz, ajratilgan"},{"en":"Step out of the comfort zone","uz":"O'zgacha holatga o'tmoq, qulay hududdan chiqmoq"},{"en":"Navigate","uz":"Yo'l topmoq, boshqarish"},{"en":"Open-minded","uz":"Keng fikrlovchi"},{"en":"Uncertainty","uz":"Noaniqlik"},{"en":"Insecurity","uz":"Xavotir, ishonchsizlik"},{"en":"Evolve","uz":"Rivojlanmoq, o'zgarish"},{"en":"Motivate","uz":"rag'batlantirmoq"},{"en":"Transparent","uz":"shaffof"},{"en":"Exceptional","uz":"ajoyib"},{"en":"Underperform","uz":"kutilganidan past natija ko'rsatmoq"},{"en":"Downsides","uz":"salbiy tomonlar"},{"en":"Enormous","uz":"ulkan"},{"en":"Undervalue","uz":"kam baholamoq"},{"en":"Collaborative","uz":"hamkorlikdagi"},{"en":"Cohesion","uz":"birlashganlik"},{"en":"Incentives","uz":"rag'batlantirish vositalari"}]},{"id":"b2t8","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":8,"p11":[{"q":"What is your town like?","a":"My town is a charming blend of modern amenities and natural beauty. It's not too big, so everything feels pretty cozy. There are parks where you can just relax and enjoy the scenery. The people here are friendly and there's always something happening, like local events or small festivals. Overall, it's a great place to unwind, but it also has a lot of energy."},{"q":"Who is your favourite sports person?","a":"My favourite sports person is Serena Williams. She's not only an incredible tennis player but also a true role model. Her determination and resilience on the court are inspiring, and she's always been outspoken about equality and women's rights. Her success story motivates me to push through challenges, whether in sports or life."},{"q":"How often do you use the internet?","a":"I use the internet daily, mostly for work and staying connected with friends. It's an essential tool for me because I can access information in seconds. I also enjoy watching videos and streaming music when I have some free time. It's hard to imagine life without it nowadays, honestly."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t8_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"In these pictures, we can see people engaged in different types of travel experiences. I guess, in the first image, a young woman with a backpack is boarding a small airplane, looking excited about her journey, while the second image shows three friends or possibly relatives enjoying themselves on what appears to be a train ride. The trio in the second image appears to be sharing a memorable moment together, their genuine smiles and close physical proximity suggesting they have a strong bond and are thoroughly relishing their travel experience."},{"q":"What are some challenges people face while traveling by plane?","a":"Traveling by plane can be really convenient, but it also comes with its fair share of challenges. One of the biggest issues is dealing with long security lines and the constant delays that seem to happen out of nowhere. On top of that, the\n\ncramped space on the plane itself can be uncomfortable, especially during long flights. Another challenge is the jet lag that hits when crossing time zones. It can leave you feeling disoriented and tired for days. Finally, there's always the stress of potential cancellations or lost luggage, which can really throw off your plans."},{"q":"How does traveling benefit people?","a":"Traveling has so many benefits. First and foremost, it opens up new perspectives. When you visit different places, you experience different cultures and ways of life, which helps you understand the world better. It also pushes you out of your comfort zone, which can lead to personal growth and confidence. Traveling is a great way to build memories and spend quality time with friends or family. On top of that, it can be a great stress reliever, giving you the chance to disconnect from daily routines and just recharge."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t8_2.jpg","qs":["Describe the time when you felt happy about something.","Why do you think it was a significant event for you?","To what extent do external factors like wealth, relationships, or achievements contribute to happiness?"],"a":"One time I felt especially happy was when I completed a big project at work that I had been working on for months. I was given full responsibility for it, and there were moments when I felt overwhelmed, unsure if I could finish it. But when I finally saw the results of my hard work—everything falling into place and getting positive feedback—I felt incredibly proud. It wasn't just the accomplishment itself, but the journey and how much I learned along the way that made me really happy. It was a significant event for me because it was a moment where I saw my own growth. There were times when I doubted myself, but pushing through those moments and delivering a successful outcome was a huge boost to my confidence. It\n\nwasn't just about the success itself—it was about realizing I could handle challenges and perform under pressure. That realization made me proud and helped me see my own potential in a new light. I think external factors, like relationships and achievements, definitely contribute to happiness, but they aren't the whole picture. Relationships, for instance, provide support, love, and connection, which are essential for a happy life. Achievements can give us a sense of fulfillment and pride. However, I believe true happiness also comes from within. Personal contentment, being at peace with yourself, and finding joy in the small things are just as important. It's a balance between external factors and how we feel inside that really shapes our happiness."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t8_3.jpg","topic":"Students should be encouraged to participate in extracurricular activities.","for":["Helps in developing soft skills and teamwork","Provides a break from academic pressure","Can improve overall school performance"],"against":["May distract from academic studies","Can be stressful if overcommitted","Not all students have an interest in extracurriculars"],"a":"I think extracurricular activities can play a huge role in student development, but there are definitely two sides to consider here.\n\nIn terms of benefits, extracurricular activities are fantastic for developing critical soft skills that aren't always taught in the classroom. From my experience, joining the debate club really helped me learn how to communicate effectively and work with different personalities. These activities also provide a much-needed mental break from constant academic pressure. When I was overwhelmed with coursework, my football practice became my sanctuary - somewhere I could release stress and return to my studies with a fresher mindset. Research has shown that students who participate in activities outside the classroom often see improvements in their academic performance too, which contradicts what some might expect.\n\nHowever, there are valid concerns about extracurriculars. One major issue is that they can sometimes pull students away from their primary academic responsibilities. I've seen classmates who became so involved in theater productions that their grades began to slip because they simply didn't have enough time for homework. There's also the risk of becoming overcommitted, leading to burnout and excessive stress - I experienced this myself when trying to juggle three different clubs alongside my studies. It's worth noting that not every student has natural inclinations toward extracurricular activities; some prefer to focus solely on academics or pursue interests that aren't formally organized by schools.\n\nTo conclude, while extracurricular activities offer tremendous developmental benefits and stress relief for many students, we need to be mindful about potential academic interference and recognize that they're not universally appealing. The key is finding the right balance and allowing students to make informed choices about their participation rather than making it mandatory."},"words":[{"en":"Charming","uz":"Jozibali"},{"en":"Amenities","uz":"Sharoitlar"},{"en":"Cozy","uz":"Quvnoq"},{"en":"Scenery","uz":"Tabiyat manzarasi"},{"en":"Festivals","uz":"Bayramlar"},{"en":"Resilience","uz":"Bardoshlilik"},{"en":"Outspoken","uz":"Ochiq so'zli"},{"en":"Equality","uz":"Tenglik"},{"en":"Motivates","uz":"Ruhlantiradi"},{"en":"Essential","uz":"Zarur"},{"en":"Convenient","uz":"Qulay"},{"en":"Challenges","uz":"Muammolar"},{"en":"Overcrowded","uz":"Oqibatsiz, gavjum"},{"en":"Patience","uz":"Sabr"},{"en":"Cramped","uz":"Tor"},{"en":"Disoriented","uz":"Buzilgan, yo'nalishini yo'qotgan"},{"en":"Canceled","uz":"Bekor qilingan"},{"en":"Broaden","uz":"Kengaytirish"},{"en":"Horizons","uz":"Ufqlar"},{"en":"Unwind","uz":"Bo'shashmoq, dam olish"},{"en":"Overwhelmed","uz":"Cho'kkan"},{"en":"Feedback","uz":"Fikr-mulohaza"},{"en":"Accomplishment","uz":"Erishish"},{"en":"Prove","uz":"Isbotlamoq"},{"en":"Achievement","uz":"Yutuq"},{"en":"Confidence","uz":"Ishonch"},{"en":"Support","uz":"Yordam"},{"en":"Contentment","uz":"Qoniqish"},{"en":"Developmental","uz":"rivojlantiruvchi"},{"en":"Sanctuary","uz":"boshpana"},{"en":"Contradicts","uz":"zid kelmoq"},{"en":"Valid","uz":"asosli"},{"en":"Primary","uz":"asosiy"},{"en":"Burnout","uz":"toliqish"},{"en":"Inclinations","uz":"moyilliklar"},{"en":"Tremendous","uz":"ulkan"},{"en":"Interference","uz":"aralashuv"},{"en":"Mandatory","uz":"majburiy"}]},{"id":"b2t9","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":9,"p11":[{"q":"Tell me about your house. I live in a cozy apartment in the city. It's not too big, but it's just the right size for me. The living room is spacious, with large windows that let in a lot of natural light, which makes it feel really warm and inviting. I have a small kitchen where I love to","a":"cook, and a comfy bedroom where I can relax after a long day. It's a peaceful place, and I've added some personal touches with artwork and plants that make it feel like home."},{"q":"Do you go to bed early or late?","a":"I tend to go to bed a bit late, especially on weekdays. I usually get caught up in finishing tasks or watching a good show, so I don't end up winding down until around midnight. On weekends, I try to sleep a little earlier, but it's not always easy. I guess I'm more of a night owl than an early riser, but I try to make sure I get enough sleep to stay productive the next day."},{"q":"What is your favorite drink?","a":"My favorite drink would have to be coffee. I love starting my day with a good cup of coffee—it just gives me that boost I need to get going. I enjoy experimenting with different flavors,\n\nbut I usually stick to a strong black coffee or an espresso. On the weekends, I like to treat myself to a cappuccino when I'm out at a café. It's the perfect way to relax and enjoy a quiet moment."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t9_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What can you see in these pictures?","a":"In these pictures, I can see people celebrating different special occasions together. I guess, in the first image, a group of friends are celebrating someone's birthday with a cake and party hats, while the second one shows friends or colleagues enjoying a dinner party at what seems to be an upscale restaurant. The atmosphere in both pictures is incredibly lively, with everyone smiling and seemingly having a wonderful time in each other's company. In the dinner party scene, the friends are engaged in animated conversation over their meal, with elegant wine glasses and beautifully presented food on the table."},{"q":"When was the last time you gathered with family?","a":"The last time I gathered with my family was a couple of months ago, during my cousin's birthday. It was such a warm and cheerful day. We had a big lunch at my grandparents' house, shared stories, and laughed a lot. Even though we're all\n\npretty busy, moments like that bring us closer. It felt really good to disconnect from everything and just enjoy each other's company. Family time like that is something I truly cherish."},{"q":"What are the advantages of celebrating with family over with friends?","a":"Celebrating with family has a different kind of emotional depth. There's a strong bond that makes everything feel more meaningful. With family, there's a sense of tradition, and you often feel more comfortable being yourself. They know your background, your habits—everything—so there's no pressure to impress anyone. Also, family celebrations tend to be more personal and fuller of nostalgia, especially when you're sharing old memories or family recipes. Of course, friends are fun too, but with family, there's a stronger feeling of belonging."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t9_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about the time when you shared a secret with another person.","How did you feel after sharing it?","How important is it to keep other people's secrets?"],"a":"A few years ago, I shared a personal secret with one of my closest friends. I was going through a rough time emotionally, but I kept everything bottled up for months. I didn't want to worry anyone or seem weak. One evening, we were just talking over coffee, and something about the moment felt safe. So, I opened up and told her what I was dealing with. It wasn't easy, but I felt I needed to be honest with someone I trusted deeply. She listened without interrupting, didn't judge me at all, and showed real understanding. Right after I told her, I felt a huge sense of relief—like I could finally breathe. It was emotionally freeing, and honestly, I regretted not doing it sooner. Sharing that secret made me feel lighter, more understood, and it even brought us closer. It reminded me how powerful it is to have someone you can be\n\ncompletely honest with. It gave me a stronger emotional connection to her, and I started feeling more at peace with myself. I think keeping someone's secret is a serious responsibility. When someone chooses to confide in you, they're showing a lot of vulnerability and putting their full trust in you. If you break that trust, it can damage the relationship permanently. I believe being a loyal and respectful friend means protecting their privacy. Everyone deserves a space where they can speak freely without the fear of being judged or exposed. So for me, keeping secrets is not just important—it's part of being a reliable human being."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t9_3.jpg","topic":"Owning a pet improves quality of life.","for":["Provides companionship and emotional support","Encourages a sense of responsibility","Can be beneficial for mental health"],"against":["Pets require time, money, and care","Not suitable for people with allergies or certain lifestyles","Can lead to emotional distress if not managed properly"],"a":"I'd like to talk about whether having a pet actually makes your life better, as there are strong arguments on both sides of this debate.\n\nLet's start with the positives. One of the biggest benefits of pet ownership is the companionship they provide. I've seen firsthand how my grandmother's cat has become her closest companion after my grandfather passed away - pets can truly fill an emotional void in our lives. Having a pet also teaches responsibility in a way few other things can. When I got my first dog as a teenager, I quickly learned that another living being was counting on me for their survival, which was honestly quite transformative. The mental health benefits are substantial too - there's solid research showing that simply petting a dog or cat can lower blood pressure and reduce anxiety. When I'm stressed after a tough day, coming home to my dog's excitement completely shifts my mood.\n\nThat said, pet ownership isn't all cuddles and Instagram moments. The financial commitment can be significant - between food, vet bills, grooming, and unexpected medical emergencies, pets can put a real strain on your budget. My friend recently spent nearly two thousand dollars on emergency surgery for her cat! There's also the lifestyle factor to consider - pets require consistent care and attention, making spontaneous travel or late nights at work much more complicated. And for some people, pet ownership simply isn't feasible due to allergies or housing restrictions. I've known several friends who experienced real emotional distress when they had to rehome pets because they moved to apartments with no-pet policies.\n\nIn conclusion, while pets can bring remarkable joy, companionship and emotional benefits to our lives, they also come with substantial responsibilities and constraints that aren't suitable for everyone. The decision to bring a pet into your life should be carefully considered based on your personal circumstances, lifestyle, and long-term commitment ability."},"words":[{"en":"Cozy","uz":"Qulay"},{"en":"Spacious","uz":"Keng"},{"en":"Bright","uz":"Yorqin"},{"en":"Inviting","uz":"Taklif qiladigan"},{"en":"Comfortable","uz":"Quvnoq"},{"en":"Personal","uz":"Shaxsiy"},{"en":"Caught up","uz":"Band bo'lmoq"},{"en":"Night owl","uz":"Kechqurun uyg'oq bo'ladigan kishi"},{"en":"Productive","uz":"Samarali"},{"en":"Boost","uz":"Rag'bat"},{"en":"Celebrating","uz":"Bayram qilmoq / nishonlamoq"},{"en":"Upscale restaurant","uz":"Qimmatbaho restoran / yuqori darajadagi restoran"},{"en":"Lively atmosphere","uz":"Jonli muhit"},{"en":"Animated conversation","uz":"Jonli suhbat"},{"en":"Beautifully presented food","uz":"Chiroyli tarzda taqdim etilgan ovqat"},{"en":"Cheerful","uz":"Quvnoq, xushchaqchaq"},{"en":"Disconnect from everything","uz":"Hammasidan uzilish / dam olish"},{"en":"Emotional depth","uz":"Hissiy chuqurlik"},{"en":"Sense of tradition","uz":"An'anani his qilish"},{"en":"Feeling of belonging","uz":"Mansublik tuyg'usi"},{"en":"Relief","uz":"Yengillik (ruhiy jihatdan)"},{"en":"Freeing","uz":"Ozod qiluvchi, yengil his qilinadigan"},{"en":"Confide","uz":"Ishonib sir aytmoq"},{"en":"Vulnerability","uz":"Zaiflik, ochiqlik (hissiy)"},{"en":"Trust","uz":"Ishonch"},{"en":"Loyal","uz":"Sodiq"},{"en":"Respectful","uz":"Hurmatli, hurmat ko'rsatadigan"},{"en":"Judged","uz":"Baholangan, tanqid qilingan"},{"en":"Exposed","uz":"Oshkor qilingan, fosh etilgan"},{"en":"Companionship","uz":"hamrohlik"},{"en":"Transformative","uz":"o'zgartiruvchi"},{"en":"Substantial","uz":"sezilarli"},{"en":"Spontaneous","uz":"kutilmagan"},{"en":"Feasible","uz":"amalga oshirishga mumkin"},{"en":"Constraints","uz":"cheklovlar"},{"en":"Remarkable","uz":"ajoyib"},{"en":"Void","uz":"bo'shliq"},{"en":"Commitment","uz":"majburiyat"},{"en":"Rehome","uz":"qayta joylashtirmoq"}]},{"id":"b2t10","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":10,"p11":[{"q":"Tell me about your favorite teacher. My favorite teacher was my English teacher in high school. She had this amazing way of making lessons interesting and fun. She was always very encouraging and made us feel confident, even when we made mistakes. What I liked most was","a":"that she genuinely cared about her students—not just academically, but also personally. She helped me discover my love for reading and speaking in English, and I'm really grateful for that."},{"q":"Do you live in a house or a flat?","a":"Right now, I live in a flat in the city. It's not huge, but it's comfortable and has everything I need. I like it because it's close to public transport, shops, and cafés, which makes daily life a lot easier. The building is quiet, and I've added some small touches to make it feel more like home, like plants and cozy lighting."},{"q":"What do you like to do on weekends?","a":"On weekends, I usually try to unwind and take a break from the busy week. I enjoy meeting up with friends, going for a walk, or watching movies. Sometimes I use the time to catch up on reading or just sleep in. I also love trying out new cafés or\n\ngoing to the market—anything that helps me relax and recharge."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t10_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"Describe these two images. In these pictures, I can see different work environments in the modern world. I guess, in the first image, a group of colleagues are collaborating on a project in what seems to be a creative office space, while the second one shows a woman","a":"working independently at her computer, possibly from home. In contrast, the woman in the second image is focused on her individual task, surrounded by a few books and working in what looks like a more personal space with a quieter ambiance."},{"q":"What are the disadvantages of working in a team?","a":"Working in a team can be great, but it definitely has some downsides. One common issue is poor communication—when people aren't on the same page, things can get confusing. Another problem is dealing with different personalities; sometimes team members clash or don't contribute equally, which can be frustrating. There's also the risk of conflict or\n\ndelays when decisions take too long to make. And if someone doesn't do their part, the whole team can suffer. So, it requires a lot of patience and good coordination to work smoothly."},{"q":"Which one do you prefer; working in a team or alone?","a":"Honestly, it depends on the task, but I usually prefer working alone. I like being in control of my own schedule and having the freedom to make decisions quickly. It helps me stay more focused and productive. That said, teamwork can be very valuable when you need fresh ideas or different perspectives. I just find that I work more efficiently on my own, especially when I have a clear plan and tight deadlines. But I'm flexible—I can adapt to both when needed."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t10_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a time when you disagreed with someone.","How did you handle the disagreement?","Why is it important to learn how to handle conflicts?"],"a":"A time I clearly remember disagreeing with someone was during a group project at work. I was working with a colleague who had a very different approach to solving problems. I wanted to take a creative, slightly risky direction to make our presentation stand out, while he preferred a more traditional, safe route. At first, the situation was a bit tense because we both believed our ideas were better. It was frustrating because we were both passionate, but it started affecting the whole team's mood. Instead of arguing or ignoring each other, I decided to have an honest conversation with him. I explained my point of view clearly and made sure to also listen to his. We realized that both of our ideas had value, so we decided to compromise by blending both approaches. His structured plan gave us a solid\n\nfoundation, and my creative elements added a unique touch. In the end, the project went really well, and we both felt proud of the result. What helped most was staying respectful, keeping an open mind, and focusing on the bigger goal rather than our personal preferences. I believe learning to handle conflict is an essential life skill. Disagreements are bound to happen—whether it's at work, in relationships, or even within families. If we don't know how to manage them, they can easily lead to resentment or broken communication. Handling conflict maturely helps us build stronger connections, improves teamwork, and teaches us to look at things from different perspectives. It also helps you grow emotionally and stay calm under pressure, which is incredibly valuable in any area of life."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t10_3.jpg","topic":"The death penalty is the best way to reduce crime.","for":["Crime rates can be reduced","It is justice for victims' families","It is cheaper than life imprisonment"],"against":["There is a risk of executing the innocent","Application can be unequal and biased","Deterrence effect is limited"],"a":"Well, I'm being asked to discuss whether the death penalty is the best way to reduce crime. This is certainly a complex and sensitive topic that societies have debated for centuries.\n\nOn one hand, supporters argue that the death penalty can help reduce crime rates by serving as the ultimate deterrent. When potential criminals know they might face execution, they might think twice before committing serious offenses. Additionally, many people believe it provides justice for victims' families who have suffered tremendous loss and trauma. Some also point out that it's actually more economical than keeping someone imprisoned for life, which can cost taxpayers millions over decades.\n\nHowever, there are serious concerns about capital punishment. Perhaps the most troubling is the risk of executing innocent people - once carried out, it's irreversible, and sadly, we've seen cases where evidence later proved someone's innocence. There's also the issue of unequal application, with studies showing that factors like race and economic status can\n\ninfluence who receives the death penalty. And despite what many believe, research suggests its deterrence effect is quite limited - countries that have abolished it haven't seen crime spikes.\n\nIn my view, while I understand the emotional appeal of the death penalty, the risk of executing innocent people and its uneven application make me question whether it's truly the best approach to reducing crime. Perhaps focusing on rehabilitation, addressing root causes of criminal behavior, and improving our justice systems would be more effective in the long run."},"words":[{"en":"Encouraging","uz":"Rag'batlantiruvchi"},{"en":"Confident","uz":"Ishonchli"},{"en":"Genuinely","uz":"Chin dildan"},{"en":"Comfortable","uz":"Qulay"},{"en":"Public transport","uz":"Jamoat transporti"},{"en":"Cozy","uz":"Iliq, yoqimli"},{"en":"Unwind","uz":"Bo'shashmoq, dam olmoq"},{"en":"Catch up","uz":"Orqada qolgan narsalarni yetkazib olmoq"},{"en":"Recharge","uz":"Quvvat to'plash, kuch yig'moq"},{"en":"Sleep in","uz":"Kech uyg'onmoq"},{"en":"Collaborating","uz":"Hamkorlik qilmoq"},{"en":"Creative office space","uz":"Ijodiy ish muhiti / ofis maydoni"},{"en":"Independently","uz":"Mustaqil ravishda"},{"en":"Personal space","uz":"Shaxsiy makon"},{"en":"Quiet ambiance","uz":"Tinch muhit"},{"en":"Poor communication","uz":"Zaif muloqot"},{"en":"Clash","uz":"To'qnashmoq / kelishmovchilikka borish"},{"en":"Contribute equally","uz":"Teng darajada hissa qo'shmoq"},{"en":"Tense","uz":"Tarang, asabiy holat"},{"en":"Frustrating","uz":"Jahl chiqarguvchi, ranjituvchi"},{"en":"Compromise","uz":"Murosa"},{"en":"Respectful","uz":"Hurmatli"},{"en":"Open mind","uz":"Ochiq fikrli bo'lish"},{"en":"Foundation","uz":"Asos"},{"en":"Preferences","uz":"Afzalliklar, xohishlar"},{"en":"Deterrent","uz":"to'siq"},{"en":"Irreversible","uz":"qaytarilmas"},{"en":"Application","uz":"qo'llanish"},{"en":"Abolished","uz":"bekor qilingan"},{"en":"Rehabilitation","uz":"qayta tiklash"},{"en":"Complex","uz":"murakkab"},{"en":"Tremendous","uz":"juda katta"},{"en":"Economical","uz":"tejamkor"},{"en":"Uneven","uz":"notekis"}]},{"id":"b2t11","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":11,"p11":[{"q":"What kinds of books do you like to read?","a":"I'm really into psychological thrillers and historical fiction. I find it fascinating how authors weave suspense and rich detail into their stories. Sometimes I also enjoy self-help books—they give me a fresh perspective. I like books that challenge my thinking or transport me to another era. It's like a mini-vacation for the mind."},{"q":"Are there any traditional clothes in your country?","a":"Yes, absolutely. In Uzbekistan, we have beautiful traditional outfits like the atlas or adras dresses for women and chapan for men. They're often handmade with intricate embroidery and vibrant patterns. People still wear them during weddings or cultural festivals. It's a lovely way to celebrate our heritage and keep traditions alive."},{"q":"What colours do you like?","a":"I'm drawn to earthy tones like olive green and terracotta— they feel calming and grounded. But I also like bold colours like royal blue and mustard yellow when I want to make a statement. It really depends on my mood or the season. Colours can say a lot about your vibe without saying a word."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t11_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"Describe these pictures. These images present a contrast between two leisure activities: passive entertainment through television watching and active engagement through reading. I imagine the person watching TV is unwinding after a long day with their favorite","a":"show, while the reader has sought out a tranquil outdoor spot to immerse themselves in a compelling book during the golden hour."},{"q":"What are the advantages of reading books over watching TV?","a":"Reading books has several advantages over watching TV. First, books engage your imagination more, as they allow you to visualize scenes and characters. Additionally, reading improves your focus and concentration, helping you to absorb information better. Books also provide a deeper understanding of topics, offering insights that TV shows may not explore in-depth. Lastly, reading is a quieter activity, which can be relaxing\n\nand more reflective compared to the passive experience of watching TV."},{"q":"When was the last time you watched TV with friends?","a":"The last time I watched TV with friends was last weekend. We gathered at my house and watched a thrilling movie together. It was great to share the experience and discuss the plot and characters afterwards. We had some snacks and enjoyed a fun evening full of laughter and interesting conversation. Watching a movie with friends always makes it more enjoyable, especially when we can react to it together."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t11_2.jpg","qs":["Share an experience where trust played a key role in your relationship with someone.","How did this experience influence your perspective on building and maintaining trust?","What factors contribute to establishing trust between people or groups in society?"],"a":"Yeah, there was a time when trust played a huge role in my life. A couple of years ago, I was working on a group project at university, and honestly, I wasn't sure if we'd all get along — everyone had different ideas, and some of us barely knew each other. But one of the group members, Amina, took the lead and suggested we start by just getting to know each other first. It wasn't just about the project — she wanted us to build some kind of connection. At first, I was skeptical. I mean, most group projects end with one or two people doing all the work. But over time, we started to trust each other. We were honest about what we\n\ncould and couldn't do, and we didn't judge anyone if they were struggling. I remember one time I completely messed up a task, and instead of blaming me, the group helped fix it without making me feel bad. That kind of support really meant a lot. After that experience, I started thinking differently about trust. It's not just something that happens instantly — it takes time, and you have to earn it. But once it's there, it makes everything so much easier. You communicate better, work better, and even enjoy spending time together more. In society, I think trust is built through things like honesty, consistency, and mutual respect. Also, being transparent — like, if something goes wrong, just admit it. When people feel safe and heard, they're more likely to open up, and that's how stronger bonds form, whether it's between friends, coworkers, or even whole communities."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t11_3.jpg","topic":"Artificial intelligence should be used to make hiring decisions.","for":["less bias in the hiring process","fast recruitment by filtering candidates efficiently","processing large volumes of data"],"against":["risk of biases if trained on flawed data","difficult to assess soft skills and cultural fit","can lead to dehumanization in hiring"],"a":"Well, that's quite a thought-provoking question. Should artificial intelligence be used in hiring decisions? Let me share my thoughts on this.\n\nI believe there are both benefits and drawbacks to using AI in the recruitment process. On the positive side, AI systems can significantly reduce human bias in hiring. Traditional interviews often suffer from unconscious prejudices based on gender, ethnicity, or age, while AI can be programmed to focus solely on qualifications and experience.\n\nAnother advantage is the efficiency AI brings to recruitment. Companies today receive hundreds, sometimes thousands of applications for a single position. AI can filter through these applications rapidly, identifying the most suitable candidates based on predetermined criteria.\n\nAI also excels at processing vast amounts of data – far more than any human recruiter could handle. This means it can spot patterns and make connections that might otherwise be missed, potentially identifying promising candidates who might have been overlooked in a traditional screening process.\n\nHowever, there are legitimate concerns about this approach too. Ironically, while AI can reduce bias, it can also perpetuate it if trained on flawed historical data. If past hiring practices were biased, the AI will simply learn and replicate these patterns, potentially exacerbating the problem rather than solving it.\n\nFurthermore, AI struggles with evaluating soft skills and cultural fit. Qualities like creativity, emotional intelligence, and teamwork are crucial in many roles but difficult to quantify in a way that algorithms can accurately assess.\n\nPerhaps my biggest concern is the risk of dehumanization in the hiring process. Job seeking is already an emotionally taxing experience, and the thought of being rejected by an algorithm rather than a person feels particularly disheartening.\n\nIn conclusion, while AI certainly has its place in modernizing and improving hiring processes, I believe it should complement rather than replace human judgment. The ideal approach might be a hybrid system where AI handles initial screening, while human recruiters make final decisions, especially for roles requiring strong interpersonal skills."},"words":[{"en":"Psychological thriller","uz":"Psixologik triller"},{"en":"Intricate","uz":"Murakkab"},{"en":"Vibrant","uz":"Yorqin"},{"en":"Heritage","uz":"Meros"},{"en":"Perspective","uz":"Qarash"},{"en":"Weave (a story)","uz":"To'qimoq"},{"en":"Calming","uz":"Tinchlantiruvchi"},{"en":"Grounded","uz":"Barqaror"},{"en":"Bold (colour)","uz":"Dadil (rang)"},{"en":"Era","uz":"Davr"},{"en":"Leisure","uz":"Bo'sh vaqt"},{"en":"Engagement","uz":"Ishtirok, faol qatnashish"},{"en":"Unwinding","uz":"Dam olish"},{"en":"Immersed","uz":"Botgan, o'rab olgan"},{"en":"Compelling","uz":"Qiziqarli, jalb qiluvchi"},{"en":"Tranquil","uz":"Tinch, sokin"},{"en":"Plush","uz":"Ko'rkam, hashamatli"},{"en":"Climate-controlled","uz":"Iqlimni boshqarilgan"},{"en":"Skeptical","uz":"shubhali"},{"en":"Mess up","uz":"ishni buzmoq, xatoga yo'l qo'ymoq"},{"en":"Support","uz":"qo'llab-quvvatlash"},{"en":"Earn (trust)","uz":"(ishonchni) qozonmoq"},{"en":"Transparent","uz":"ochiq, shaffof"},{"en":"Mutual respect","uz":"o'zaro hurmat"},{"en":"Thought-provoking","uz":"o'ylashga undovchi"},{"en":"Unconscious prejudices","uz":"anglanmagan xusumatlar"},{"en":"Level playing field","uz":"teng imkoniyatlar maydoni"},{"en":"Streamlines","uz":"tartiblashtiradi"},{"en":"Perpetuate","uz":"davom ettirmoq"},{"en":"Exacerbating","uz":"kuchaytirmoq"}]},{"id":"b2t12","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":12,"p11":[{"q":"Do you have many books at home?","a":"Yes, I've got a pretty large collection of books at home. It's my little personal library! I enjoy having books around because they create such a cozy atmosphere. Some are fiction, others are non-fiction, but I've got a few that I return to over and over again. I like to think of them as my mental escape route."},{"q":"Do you like any foreign singers?","a":"Definitely! I really admire artists like Adele and Ed Sheeran. Their voices are so powerful, and I think their songwriting is exceptional. I also enjoy K-pop, like BTS; their performances are always so energetic and visually stunning. It's amazing how music can bring people from all over the world together."},{"q":"What is your favourite item of clothing?","a":"I'd say my favorite item is a well-worn leather jacket. It's classic, versatile, and never goes out of style. It makes me feel confident and it's the perfect piece for any casual outfit. I think it adds a certain edge, whether I'm dressing up or down."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t12_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"Describe these two images. The images depict two different educational settings. The first image shows a student engaged in an online virtual class with a teacher visible on the laptop screen. The second image captures a traditional classroom setting with a teacher standing","a":"in front of a group of students."},{"q":"What are the differences between online education and traditional learning?","a":"Online education is more flexible, allowing students to learn from anywhere at their own pace, while traditional learning often requires a fixed schedule and physical presence in a classroom. In online education, technology plays a major role, with virtual lectures and digital resources, whereas traditional learning focuses more on face-to-face interaction."},{"q":"What are the challenges of online learning?","a":"One major challenge is staying focused, as distractions at home can interrupt the learning process. Technical issues like poor internet connectivity or software problems can also be frustrating. Additionally, the lack of physical interaction can make it harder to build relationships with classmates and teachers, which may affect motivation and engagement. For some, adapting to a self-disciplined study routine can also be quite difficult."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t12_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me when you argued with someone What was the argument about, and who was involved?","How did you feel during the argument?","How did the argument end, and what did you learn from it?"],"a":"Oh, I definitely remember a time when I had a heated argument with my roommate. It was a few months ago, and the argument was actually about something pretty trivial — household chores. At the time, we were both a bit stressed, and she felt like I wasn't doing my fair share of the work around the house. We were both really busy with school, but I didn't realize how much she was doing compared to me. The argument started when she snapped at me one evening, saying, \"You never clean up after yourself!\" I didn't take it well, to be honest, and I got really defensive. I started pointing out all the things I had done, like washing the dishes the day before, and said, \"I do plenty!\" But instead of hearing her out, I was just focused on defending myself. During the argument, I felt a mix of frustration and confusion. I couldn't understand why she was so upset, but at the same time, I was starting to feel guilty because I realized that maybe I hadn't been as attentive to the housework as I thought. We both got pretty emotional and started saying things we didn't mean. But after a while, we both took a step back and started listening to each other more. She explained how she felt overwhelmed because she had been doing most of the chores without any help, and I admitted that I hadn't been as proactive as I should have been. The argument ended on a more positive note — we came up with a solution. We made a schedule for the chores, so we could both see exactly what we were responsible for and when. After that, we didn't argue about it again, and I think it even strengthened our friendship. It was one of those situations where we both realized that communication was key. I learned that it's really important to listen carefully to the other person's feelings, even if you don't agree at first. Also, stepping back from the situation and considering things from their perspective can help avoid misunderstandings. It made me more aware of the small things that can really affect a relationship, even something as simple as housework."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t12_3.jpg","topic":"People should be required to vote in national elections.","for":["Compulsory voting ensures higher participation and a more representative democracy.","It can encourage citizens to be more informed and engaged with political issues.","It prevents the influence of special interest groups from disproportionately affecting the results."],"against":["It violates individual freedom by forcing people to vote. e¢ Some people may vote irresponsibly or without sufficient knowledge of the candidates or issues.","Mandatory voting could lead to an increase in apathy or resentment towards the political system."],"a":"So, should voting be mandatory in national elections? That's actually something I've thought about quite a bit.\n\nPersonally, I can see valid arguments on both sides of this debate. When it comes to the advantages, compulsory voting definitely boosts participation rates and creates a more representative democracy. In countries like Australia where voting is mandatory, they regularly see turnout rates above 90%, which means election results genuinely reflect what the majority of citizens want, not just those who happened to show up.\n\nAnother benefit is that mandatory voting encourages people to become more politically literate. If you know you have to cast a ballot, you're more likely to pay attention to candidates' platforms and current issues. This leads to a more\n\ninformed electorate, which is crucial for a healthy democracy. Instead of just passionate voters showing up, everyone has skin in the game.\n\nHowever, there are significant drawbacks to consider as well. Perhaps the most fundamental concern is that forcing people to vote infringes on individual liberty. In a free society, shouldn't citizens have the right to abstain if they choose?\n\nThen there's the quality of voting decisions. If people who aren't interested in politics are forced to cast ballots, they might make uninformed choices or vote randomly just to avoid penalties.\n\nFinally, mandatory voting might backfire by fostering resentment toward the political system. People don't generally respond well to being forced to do things, and this compulsion could increase political apathy or even rebellion against the system, with people deliberately casting protest votes or spoiling ballots.\n\nIn conclusion, while mandatory voting certainly increases participation and representation, I believe the potential downsides related to personal freedom and voting quality raise serious concerns. Perhaps a better approach might be to focus on removing barriers to voting and improving civic education rather than making it compulsory."},"words":[{"en":"Collection","uz":"To'plam"},{"en":"Cozy","uz":"Qulay, ishonchli"},{"en":"Escape route","uz":"Chiqish yo'li"},{"en":"Admire","uz":"Hurmat qilish"},{"en":"Exceptional","uz":"Ajoyib, noyob"},{"en":"Energetic","uz":"Jonli, faol"},{"en":"Stunning","uz":"Ajoyib, hayratlantiruvchi"},{"en":"Versatile","uz":"Ko'p qirrali"},{"en":"Confident","uz":"O'ziga ishongan"},{"en":"Edge","uz":"O'ziga xoslik, farq"},{"en":"Engaged","uz":"Qiziqqan"},{"en":"Virtual","uz":"Virtual"},{"en":"Flexibility","uz":"Moslashuvchanlik"},{"en":"Presence","uz":"Borlik"},{"en":"Interaction","uz":"O'zaro aloqalar"},{"en":"Motivation","uz":"Motivatsiya"},{"en":"Adapt","uz":"Moslashmoq"},{"en":"Discipline","uz":"Intizom"},{"en":"Connectivity","uz":"Ulanish imkoniyati"},{"en":"Frustrating","uz":"Xafa qiluvchi"},{"en":"Pulling my weight","uz":"o'zimning hissamni berish"},{"en":"Defensive","uz":"himoyachi, mudofaa qiluvchi"},{"en":"Frustration","uz":"norozilik, tushkunlik"},{"en":"Guilty","uz":"aybdor"},{"en":"Attentive","uz":"diqqatli, e'tiborli"},{"en":"Proactive","uz":"oldindan harakat qiluvchi"},{"en":"Step back","uz":"orqaga qadam qo'ymoq"},{"en":"Misunderstanding","uz":"noto'g'ri tushunish"},{"en":"Strengthened","uz":"mustahkamlangan"},{"en":"Perspective","uz":"nuqtai nazar"},{"en":"Compulsory","uz":"majburiy"},{"en":"Disproportionate","uz":"nomutanosib"},{"en":"Electorate","uz":"saylovchilar"},{"en":"Political literacy","uz":"siyosiy savodxonlik"},{"en":"Compelling","uz":"ishontiruvchi"},{"en":"Infringes","uz":"buzmoq"},{"en":"Abstain","uz":"o'zini tiymoq/qatnashmaslik"},{"en":"Fostering","uz":"rivojlantirish"}]},{"id":"b2t13","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":13,"p11":[{"q":"Do you like to wear dark or bright colours?","a":"I tend to lean more towards dark colours like navy blue and charcoal grey. They feel sleek and are easy to pair with almost anything. But I do enjoy bright colours, especially in the summer, like mustard yellow or coral. They bring a burst of energy and can really lift your mood."},{"q":"Are there any photos on the walls of your home?","a":"Yes, I've got quite a few family photos scattered around my home. I love having them on the walls because they remind me of special moments. There are also some beautiful landscape pictures I've collected from my travels. They add personality to the space and make it feel more welcoming."},{"q":"What do you use a computer to do?","a":"I use my computer for a lot of things. Mostly for work, like writing and researching. But I also enjoy watching movies, listening to music, and keeping in touch with friends on social media. It's pretty much my all-in-one tool for entertainment and productivity."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t13_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"Looking at these pictures, I can see two different approaches to physical fitness - outdoor cardiovascular exercise and indoor strength training. I guess, in the first image, a young couple is jogging together along a verdant trail surrounded by trees, while the second one shows seniors working out with dumbbells in what appears to be a modern gym facility. The runners seem completely in sync with each other and their natural surroundings, their expressions revealing both exertion and enjoyment as they engage in this outdoor cardio activity. In contrast, the gym scene depicts focused determination, particularly in the older gentleman's face as he performs bicep curls, demonstrating that fitness pursuits aren't limited by age but can be tailored to individual capabilities and preferences."},{"q":"What are the benefits of doing sports?","a":"Doing sports offers a ton of benefits. First, it's great for your physical health—it keeps your body fit and boosts energy levels. Regular exercise can also improve mental health by reducing stress and boosting mood. Plus, sports teach discipline, teamwork, and perseverance. Whether you're playing individually or with others, it helps build important life skills. Overall, staying active is key to leading a healthy, balanced life."},{"q":"How often do you go hiking?","a":"I try to go hiking at least once a month, usually on weekends. It's a perfect way to escape the city and enjoy the outdoors. I love the feeling of being surrounded by nature, breathing in fresh air, and exploring new trails. Sometimes I go with friends, but I also enjoy solo hikes when I want some quiet time to myself. Hiking is a great way to recharge and clear your mind."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t13_2.jpg","qs":["Describe a moment in your life when you felt genuinely happy.","What do you think contributes the most to your happiness?","In your opinion, what are the main factors that influence people's happiness in society?"],"a":"One moment in my life when I felt genuinely happy was when I found out I got accepted into my dream university. I still remember checking the results online — my hands were literally shaking. I'd been preparing for that exam for months, maybe even a year, and the pressure was intense. I had made so many sacrifices — like missing out on time with friends, giving up weekends, and staying up late studying. So when I finally saw the message saying \"Congratulations,\" I just froze for a second, then started crying and laughing at the same time. My parents were with me, and we all hugged — they were so proud, and I could see how relieved they were too. That day felt like a\n\nturning point in my life — like all the hard work had finally paid off and I was moving toward something I really wanted. For me, what contributes most to my happiness is feeling like I'm making progress in life. When I have goals and I'm working towards them, it gives me a real sense of purpose. I also think that being surrounded by positive, supportive people makes a huge difference. When I'm with people who encourage me and believe in me, it boosts my confidence and just makes life more enjoyable. And honestly, it's also the small things — like a good conversation, a walk outside, or listening to my favorite music — those little moments add up. In my opinion, the main factors that influence happiness in society are financial security, emotional support, and freedom. If people have their basic needs met — like food, a safe place to live, and access to healthcare — they're in a better position to enjoy life. Add strong personal relationships and the freedom to live the way they choose, and that's when real happiness starts to grow. It's not just about money or success — it's more about feeling safe, valued, and connected."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t13_3.jpg","topic":"Cash should be replaced by digital payment.","for":["Environmental impact","Global transactions","Contactless payments"],"against":["Digital divide","Over-reliance on technology","Potential for overspending"],"a":"I think this topic about replacing cash with digital payments has some interesting points on both sides.\n\nFrom what I see, digital payments offer some clear benefits. For one, they're much better for the environment. We don't need to cut down trees for paper money or mine metals for coins, which reduces our environmental footprint significantly.\n\nDigital payments also make global transactions incredibly simple. I can send money to someone on the other side of the world instantly, which wasn't possible before. This has really transformed international business and how families support each other across borders.\n\nPlus, contactless payments are just so convenient. Tapping your card or phone is much quicker than fumbling with cash and coins, which I personally appreciate in my daily life.\n\nBut there are definite drawbacks too. The digital divide is a real issue – many elderly people, rural communities, and those with lower incomes might not have easy access to digital banking tools or reliable internet. Moving completely away from cash could leave these groups behind.\n\nWe're also becoming perhaps too dependent on technology. When systems crash or our devices run out of battery, we can be left in difficult situations if cash isn't an option.\n\nLastly, it's just easier to overspend with digital payments. There's something about physically handing over cash that makes us more aware of what we're spending.\n\nIn conclusion, while I see the benefits of going digital, I think we need a balanced approach that considers everyone's needs."},"words":[{"en":"Lean towards","uz":"Yo'naltirmoq"},{"en":"Sleek","uz":"Yoqimli, silliq"},{"en":"Burst of energy","uz":"Energiya portlashi"},{"en":"Scattered","uz":"Tarqalgan"},{"en":"Landscape","uz":"Landshaft"},{"en":"Collect","uz":"To'plamoq"},{"en":"Personality","uz":"Shaxsiyat"},{"en":"Welcoming","uz":"Mehmondo'st"},{"en":"Researching","uz":"Tadqiqot qilmoq"},{"en":"Productivity","uz":"Ishchanlik"},{"en":"Verdant","uz":"yam-yashil"},{"en":"In sync","uz":"hamohang"},{"en":"Exertion","uz":"zo'riqish"},{"en":"Determination","uz":"qat'iyat"},{"en":"Complementary","uz":"to'ldiruvchi"},{"en":"Perseverance","uz":"Sabrlilik, qat'iyat"},{"en":"Balanced","uz":"Muvozanatli"},{"en":"Escape","uz":"Qochish, chiqib ketish"},{"en":"Recharge","uz":"Tetiklanish, qayta quvvat olish"},{"en":"Trails","uz":"Yo'llar, izlar"},{"en":"Genuinely","uz":"chin dildan, samimiy tarzda"},{"en":"Turning point","uz":"burilish nuqtasi"},{"en":"Sacrifices","uz":"qurbonliklar"},{"en":"Paid off","uz":"o'z samarasini berdi"},{"en":"Sense of purpose","uz":"maqsad hissi"},{"en":"Supportive","uz":"qo'llab-quvvatlovchi"},{"en":"Boosts my confidence","uz":"ishonchimni oshiradi"},{"en":"Add up","uz":"yig'ilmoq, to'planmoq"},{"en":"Financial security","uz":"moliyaviy xavfsizlik"},{"en":"Valued","uz":"qadrlangan"},{"en":"Environmental footprint","uz":"ekologik iz"},{"en":"Digital divide","uz":"raqamli tafovut"},{"en":"Transform","uz":"o'zgartirmoq"},{"en":"Convenient","uz":"qulay"},{"en":"Drawbacks","uz":"kamchiliklar"},{"en":"Dependent","uz":"bog'liq"},{"en":"Fumbling","uz":"paypaslab qidirmoq"},{"en":"Consider","uz":"hisobga olmoq"},{"en":"Approach","uz":"yondashuv"},{"en":"Benefits","uz":"foyda, manfaat"}]},{"id":"b2t14","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":14,"p11":[{"q":"What is the best book you've ever read?","a":"Honestly, the best book I've ever read is To Kill a Mockingbird by Harper Lee. It's incredibly thought-provoking and touches on serious themes like justice and human dignity. The characters felt so real and relatable, especially Atticus Finch—he's kind of a moral compass throughout the story. I was honestly glued to it from the first chapter. It's the kind of book that lingers in your mind long after you finish it."},{"q":"Would you want to be an actor in the future?","a":"Well, acting sounds exciting, but I don't think it's really my cup of tea. I'm a bit camera-shy and I prefer staying behind the scenes. That said, I do admire actors for their creativity and resilience—it's not an easy job. If I ever had the chance, maybe I'd do a small role just for fun, but not as a career. I'm more into creative writing than performing."},{"q":"Where do you usually buy your clothes?","a":"I usually shop online because it's super convenient and I can compare a bunch of styles in one place. Plus, I like unique pieces you don't often find in local stores. Sometimes I visit boutique shops when I'm in the mood for something more\n\nfashionable or trendy. I try to go for quality over quantity. Comfort is key for me, but I still want to look put-together."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t14_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b2t14_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What can you see in these pictures?","a":"Looking at these pictures, I can see families enjoying quality time together in two very different settings. I guess, in the first image, a family is having an exhilarating day at an amusement park with a roller coaster visible in the background. The first picture radiates pure joy and excitement with everyone's faces lit up with genuine laughter, perhaps capturing that thrilling moment right after experiencing the adrenaline rush of the ride. The second image, in contrast, conveys a sense of tranquility and meaningful connection, showcasing how precious moments don't always need to be action-packed to be meaningful."},{"q":"Do you think spending time with parents is important?","a":"Yes, I absolutely believe that spending time with parents is crucial. Not only does it help build a strong bond, but it also allows for meaningful conversations and shared experiences. Parents are often the best source of advice, and spending quality time with them can deepen understanding and respect.\n\nIt's a time to reconnect and show appreciation, which can really strengthen family ties. Plus, the older we get, the more we realize how valuable these moments are. So, I try to make the most of my time with them whenever I can."},{"q":"Will you prefer spending time in the park or in the nature?","a":"I'd definitely lean towards spending time in nature. There's something about being surrounded by trees, fresh air, and natural landscapes that feels so refreshing and peaceful. While parks are great for casual walks and meeting people, nature offers a more serene and rejuvenating experience. It's easier to disconnect from the hustle and bustle of life and find inner calm in the outdoors. The sights, sounds, and even the smells of nature make it a perfect place to relax and recharge."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t14_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a time when you took on a significant responsibility.","How has this experience shaped your views on what it means to be responsible?","Why is taking responsibility important for individuals and society as a whole?"],"a":"I remember a time when I was given the responsibility to lead a major team project at work. It was a significant challenge because the project was crucial for the company, and the deadlines were tight. I had to coordinate with different departments, keep track of the timeline, and make sure everyone was motivated to do their part. At first, I was a bit anxious, but I saw it as an opportunity to grow and prove that I could handle the pressure. This experience really reshaped my views on responsibility. I realized that being responsible is not just about managing tasks, but also about being accountable for the entire team's success. There were times when things didn't go as planned,\n\nand I had to step in and find solutions quickly. I learned how to stay calm under pressure and how important it is to communicate clearly. It wasn't always smooth sailing, but in the end, we finished the project on time, and that gave me a real sense of achievement. Taking responsibility is not only important for personal growth but also for society as a whole. When you take responsibility, you show that people can trust you. This builds relationships and encourages others to be responsible too. On an individual level, it helps you become more reliable and mature. For society, it means people can rely on each other, and things get done more efficiently. Whether it's in a workplace, in the family, or in the community, responsibility is what keeps everything running smoothly."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t14_3.jpg","topic":"All employees should be allowed to work from home permanently.","for":["more flexibility and a better work-life balance","reduces office-related expenses and environmental impact","access to a wider talent pool, regardless of location"],"against":["hinders collaboration and team dynamics","risk of distractions or isolation at home","cannot be implemented in all industries or roles"],"a":"Well, this is definitely a hot topic these days, especially after so many of us got a taste of remote work during the pandemic. I personally think there are strong arguments on both sides of this debate.\n\nTo kick things off, there are some clear advantages to allowing employees to work remotely full-time. First and foremost, the flexibility this offers is incredible for work-life balance. People can organize their day around personal commitments, whether that's picking up kids from school or squeezing in a quick workout during lunch.\n\nAnother major benefit is the reduction in expenses and environmental impact. Without daily commutes, we're looking at significant savings on fuel and public transport costs, not to mention fewer emissions polluting our atmosphere. Companies can also downsize their office spaces, cutting costs on rent and utilities.\n\nThe ability to hire talent from anywhere is another massive advantage. Companies aren't limited to candidates who live\n\nnearby or are willing to relocate. This opens up opportunities for people living in remote areas or different countries altogether, creating a more diverse workforce with broader perspectives.\n\nHowever, there are legitimate concerns about permanent remote work too. One of the biggest issues is how it affects collaboration and team dynamics. Those spontaneous conversations by the coffee machine or quick brainstorming sessions that happen naturally in an office are hard to replicate virtually.\n\nWorking from home also comes with its fair share of distractions and potential isolation. Not everyone has an ideal home setup for productive work, and some people might find themselves dealing with noisy family members or the temptation to do household chores instead of focusing on work tasks.\n\nIt's also worth pointing out that remote work simply isn't feasible for all industries or roles. Healthcare providers, manufacturing workers, and many service industry employees need to be physically present to do their jobs effectively.\n\nIn conclusion, while permanent remote work offers substantial benefits in terms of flexibility, cost savings, and access to talent, it also presents significant challenges related to collaboration, work environment, and implementation across different sectors."},"words":[{"en":"Thought-provoking","uz":"O'ylantiradigan"},{"en":"Moral compass","uz":"Axloqiy yo'lko'rsatkich"},{"en":"Camera-shy","uz":"Kameradan uyalanadigan"},{"en":"Resilience","uz":"Bardoshlilik"},{"en":"Convenient","uz":"Qulay"},{"en":"Unique","uz":"Betakror"},{"en":"Boutique","uz":"Zamonaviy kiyim do'koni"},{"en":"Trendy","uz":"Urfdagi"},{"en":"Put-together","uz":"Yaxshi ko'rinadigan"},{"en":"Relatable","uz":"Oson tushuniladigan"},{"en":"Exhilarating","uz":"hayajonlantiruvchi"},{"en":"Serene","uz":"osoyishta"},{"en":"Tranquility","uz":"tinchlik"},{"en":"Adrenaline rush","uz":"adrenalin toshqini"},{"en":"Nurture","uz":"tarbiyalamoq"},{"en":"Rejuvenating","uz":"Yangilovchi"},{"en":"Hustle and bustle","uz":"Shovqin-suron, hayajon"},{"en":"Refresh","uz":"Yangilanish, tetiklanish"},{"en":"Deepen","uz":"Chuqurlashtirish"},{"en":"Meaningful","uz":"Ma'noli"},{"en":"Reconnect","uz":"Qayta ulanish"},{"en":"Significant","uz":"Muhim"},{"en":"Challenge","uz":"Sinov"},{"en":"Coordinate","uz":"Boshqarish"},{"en":"Motivated","uz":"Rag'batlantirilgan"},{"en":"Anxious","uz":"Xavotirlangan"},{"en":"Opportunity","uz":"Imkoniyat"},{"en":"Accountable","uz":"Javobgar"},{"en":"Sailing","uz":"Sayr qilish"},{"en":"Achievement","uz":"Erishish"},{"en":"Efficiently","uz":"Tez va samarali"},{"en":"Spontaneous","uz":"o'z-o'zidan sodir bo'ladigan"},{"en":"Brainstorming","uz":"g'oyalarni birgalikda o'ylash"},{"en":"Feasible","uz":"amalga oshirilishi mumkin"},{"en":"Downsize","uz":"kichraytirish"},{"en":"Resentment","uz":"norozilik"},{"en":"Implementation","uz":"amalga oshirish"}]},{"id":"b2t15","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":15,"p11":[{"q":"What do you like about living in your hometown?","a":"I really appreciate the sense of community in my hometown. People are friendly and always ready to help, which gives it a cozy, small-town feel. The pace of life is much slower compared to big cities, so I can relax and enjoy my surroundings more. I also love how close it is to nature, with parks and scenic spots all around. It's the kind of place where you can easily escape the hustle and bustle of city life."},{"q":"Do you like to take photographs?","a":"Yes, I enjoy photography a lot! It's a fun way to express creativity and capture moments that mean something to me. I love experimenting with different perspectives and lighting to make ordinary scenes look special. Whether it's a landscape, a portrait, or just an interesting detail, photography lets me freeze time and hold onto memories. It's a hobby I find both relaxing and rewarding."},{"q":"What types of animals do you have in your country?","a":"In my country, there's a huge variety of animals. We have both wild animals like bears, wolves, and deer, especially in the forests and mountains. As for pets, people mostly have cats and dogs, but some families keep more exotic animals like birds or rabbits. The country is also home to a lot of farm animals, such as cows, chickens, and goats. It's amazing how diverse the animal life is here."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t15_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"In these pictures, I can see two contrasting ways people enjoy their leisure time – one in a peaceful outdoor setting and another in an exciting indoor environment. I reckon the first image shows an older woman relaxing in a park with a book and a cup of tea or coffee. The elderly lady seems to be having such a serene moment, sitting on a bench surrounded by lush greenery, perhaps enjoying the tranquility of nature along with her reading. In contrast, the cinema scene captures this intense moment of collective suspense or surprise, with everyone clutching their popcorn and drinks, completely engrossed in whatever is happening on the screen."},{"q":"What are the main differences between reading a book and watching a movie?","a":"One major difference is that reading a book allows you to use your imagination to visualize the story, while a movie shows you everything directly. Books tend to provide more detailed\n\ncharacter development and background information, letting you dive deeper into the plot. On the other hand, movies are much faster-paced and more visually stimulating, which can make them more engaging for some people. In a book, you create your own mental images, but in a movie, everything is laid out for you."},{"q":"Do you prefer reading books or watching movies?","a":"I'd say I prefer reading books. There's something special about diving into a book and really getting lost in the world the author creates. It's more immersive for me, and I enjoy the slower pace, which allows me to think about the story more deeply. While movies are fun, they don't always capture the same depth and detail. That said, I do enjoy watching a good movie every now and then to relax."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t15_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a time when you noticed or experienced inequality.","How did this situation affect your understanding of fairness and justice?","Why is promoting equality important for creating a harmonious society?"],"a":"There was a time when I volunteered at a local community center, and I noticed a clear divide between the children who came from wealthier families and those who didn't. The wealthier kids had access to better resources like books, technology, and even tutors, while the others had to make do with less. I could see that the difference in resources was affecting their confidence and opportunities. It wasn't something I expected, and it really struck me how inequality can shape people's lives. This experience deepened my understanding of fairness and justice. It made me realize that fairness isn't just about treating everyone the same, but about giving each person what they\n\nneed to succeed. Justice means recognizing the obstacles some people face and working to remove them. In this case, it wasn't fair that some kids had advantages while others struggled with basic things. It really made me rethink how society should work to ensure everyone has equal opportunities. Promoting equality is key to building a peaceful and harmonious society because it creates an environment where everyone feels valued. When people are treated equally, they are more likely to contribute positively to their communities. If everyone has the same chance to succeed, society as a whole benefits. Equality isn't just a nice thing to have; it's essential for creating a world where everyone can thrive without barriers based on their background or circumstances."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t15_3.jpg","topic":"Art classes should be mandatory in school.","for":["Boosts creativity","Improves academic performance","Improves problem-solving"],"against":["Time constraints","Lack of interest","Resource limitations"],"a":"Well, this is quite an interesting topic to consider. When we talk about making art classes mandatory in schools, there are several perspectives to consider.\n\nIn my opinion, art education does offer some significant benefits for students. First of all, it really boosts creativity, which is becoming increasingly valuable in today's world. When students engage with different art forms, they learn to think outside the box and express themselves in unique ways.\n\nMoreover, there's growing evidence that art classes actually improve academic performance across the board. It might seem counterintuitive, but studies have shown that students who participate in arts education often perform better in subjects like math and science.\n\nAdditionally, art education significantly improves problem-solving abilities. When creating artwork, students constantly make decisions about colors, composition, and techniques, which develops critical thinking skills that are applicable in many life situations.\n\nOn the flip side, though, there are some valid concerns about making art mandatory. Time constraints are a major issue in many schools. The curriculum is already packed with core subjects, and adding required art classes might put additional pressure on an already tight schedule.\n\nAnother drawback is the simple lack of interest some students might have. Not everyone enjoys or feels comfortable with artistic expression, and forcing these students to take art classes might create negative associations with creativity in general.\n\nLastly, we can't ignore the resource limitations many schools face. Quality art education requires proper materials, dedicated spaces, and qualified teachers – resources that many schools, especially in underfunded areas, simply don't have access to.\n\nIn conclusion, while I see tremendous value in art education, I think we need to find a balanced approach that acknowledges both the benefits and the practical challenges of making it mandatory for all students."},"words":[{"en":"Community","uz":"Jamiyat"},{"en":"Cozy","uz":"Qulay"},{"en":"Pace","uz":"Tizim / tezlik"},{"en":"Escape","uz":"Qochish"},{"en":"Hustle and bustle","uz":"Shovqin-suron"},{"en":"Photography","uz":"Fotografiya"},{"en":"Creativity","uz":"Yaratijonlik"},{"en":"Perspectives","uz":"Perspektivalar"},{"en":"Freeze","uz":"To'xtatmoq"},{"en":"Exotic","uz":"Ekzotik"},{"en":"Imagination","uz":"Tasavvur"},{"en":"Visualize","uz":"Ko'z oldida tasavvur qilish"},{"en":"Character development","uz":"Personajni rivojlantirish"},{"en":"Engaging","uz":"Qiziqarli"},{"en":"Immersive","uz":"Cho'mish"},{"en":"Captured","uz":"Qaytarilgan / tasvirlangan"},{"en":"Lost","uz":"Yo'qolgan"},{"en":"Depth","uz":"Chuqlik"},{"en":"Relax","uz":"Dam olish"},{"en":"Inequality","uz":"Noto'g'ri taqsimlash"},{"en":"Divide","uz":"Ajratish"},{"en":"Resources","uz":"Resurslar"},{"en":"Confidence","uz":"Ishonch"},{"en":"Obstacles","uz":"To'siqlar"},{"en":"Fairness","uz":"Adolat"},{"en":"Justice","uz":"Adolat"},{"en":"Recognizing","uz":"Tan olish"},{"en":"Contribute","uz":"Hissa qo'shish"},{"en":"Thriving","uz":"Taraqqiyot"},{"en":"Counterintuitive","uz":"intuitsiyaga zid"},{"en":"Engaging (to engage)","uz":"jalb qilmoq"},{"en":"Perspective","uz":"nuqtai nazar"},{"en":"Composition","uz":"kompozitsiya"},{"en":"Drawback","uz":"kamchilik"},{"en":"Core subjects","uz":"asosiy fanlar"},{"en":"Applicable","uz":"qo'llaniladigan"},{"en":"Underfunded","uz":"yetarli mablag' ajratilmagan"}]},{"id":"b2t16","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":16,"p11":[{"q":"Please tell me about your best friend. My best friend is someone I've known since childhood, and we've shared so many unforgettable memories. She's incredibly supportive, always knows how to cheer me up, and gives honest advice when I need it. What I admire most is her sense of humor","a":"and the way she stays calm under pressure. We have a lot in common, but we also learn a lot from each other. Spending time with her is always refreshing and meaningful."},{"q":"Tell me about your country. My country is rich in history, culture, and natural beauty. We have stunning landscapes—mountains, deserts, and rivers—all packed into one place. The people are known for being warm and hospitable, and traditional values are still very important","a":"here. Our cuisine is delicious and diverse, full of flavor and spices. There's also a deep respect for art, music, and family life."},{"q":"What do you like to do in your free time?","a":"In my free time, I like to unwind by listening to music or going for a walk. Sometimes I read or try to learn something new online. On weekends, I enjoy hanging out with friends or watching a good movie. I also try to stay active by doing light\n\nexercise or stretching. Free time is really precious, so I try to use it in a way that helps me recharge."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t16_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"In these pictures, I can see two contrasting modes of transportation in urban environments. I'd say the first image shows a man driving alone in what looks like a luxury car with a leather interior. The driver seems quite focused and comfortable in his private vehicle, dressed in a smart blue shirt that suggests he might be commuting to work or heading to a business meeting. Meanwhile, the street scene shows diverse groups of people navigating the city on foot, carrying bags and backpacks as they make their way through what appears to be a major metropolitan area with tall buildings in the background."},{"q":"What are some advantages of walking over driving?","a":"Walking is definitely healthier—it's a great way to stay active without needing any equipment. It also reduces stress and gives you a chance to enjoy your surroundings. Unlike driving, it's free and better for the environment since it doesn't\n\ncreate any pollution. Plus, walking helps clear your mind and can even boost creativity. So, it's a simple habit with a lot of benefits."},{"q":"Why do some people prefer having a car of their own?","a":"I think people prefer having their own car because of the freedom it gives. You can go anywhere, anytime, without relying on public transport. It's especially convenient for families or people with busy schedules. Having a car also feels more private and comfortable. For some, it's even a symbol of independence or success."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t16_2.jpg","qs":["Describe time when you did a project?","How do you handle this?","What do you learn from this experience?"],"a":"One memorable project I worked on was during my final year at university. We were assigned a group task to create a full presentation on environmental sustainability—basically, how small lifestyle changes can make a big impact on the planet. It was a big project with a lot of parts: researching facts and statistics, designing the slides, and preparing the actual speech. I was mainly responsible for gathering the research and making sure our content had a logical flow. At first, I felt a bit stressed because our group had five people, and not everyone was equally motivated. Some teammates didn't respond on time, and that made it harder to move forward. To handle the situation, I decided to take the lead in organizing things. We split the work based on what each person was good at—one was great at design, another at speaking, and so on. I made a timeline with mini-deadlines and set up regular group check-ins. We used a shared document\n\nonline so everyone could edit and see updates in real time, which made collaboration easier. This experience taught me a lot, not just about the topic, but also about working with different personalities and staying calm when things don't go as planned. I realized how important it is to be both organized and flexible—sometimes you have to adjust and help others catch up. I also learned how to step up and take more responsibility when needed. In the end, our presentation went really well, and even our professor said it was one of the most practical and well-prepared ones. What I took away from this experience is that handling a project well isn't just about finishing tasks. It's also about teamwork, communication, and knowing how to motivate people and solve small issues before they become big problems. I definitely gained more confidence, and since then, I've been much more comfortable taking the lead on projects— whether at school or work."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t16_3.jpg","topic":"Libraries are becoming outdated.","for":["Digital resources are more accessible","Fewer people visit physical libraries","High maintenance costs"],"against":["Offer community services and events","Provide access to rare materials","Serve as quiet study spaces"],"a":"This is something I've been wondering about lately, especially seeing how my own library habits have changed over the years.\n\nWhen looking at why libraries might be becoming outdated, there are some convincing points. Digital resources have revolutionized information access – I can find practically any book or article online instantly without leaving my home. This convenience is hard to beat. Library attendance has noticeably dropped in many communities, with fewer people, especially younger generations, visiting physical buildings when they can get information online. There's also the practical issue of costs – maintaining buildings, paying staff, and updating physical collections requires significant funding that many local governments are questioning.\n\nHowever, libraries still offer tremendous value in several ways. They provide essential community services and events that bring people together – from children's programs to job\n\nassistance workshops and technology training. Libraries also house rare materials and special collections that aren't available digitally, preserving important cultural and historical resources. And perhaps most importantly for many people, libraries offer quiet, dedicated spaces for study and work that many don't have access to at home.\n\nIn conclusion, while digital technology has certainly changed our relationship with information, libraries are adapting rather than simply becoming obsolete. They're evolving to meet new community needs while maintaining their core functions. The future probably involves finding balance between digital convenience and the unique social and educational value that physical libraries provide."},"words":[{"en":"Unforgettable","uz":"Unutilmas"},{"en":"Supportive","uz":"Qo'llab-quvvatlovchi"},{"en":"Cheer up","uz":"Kayfiyatni ko'tarish"},{"en":"Calm under pressure","uz":"Bosim ostida xotirjam"},{"en":"Hospitable","uz":"Mehmondo'st"},{"en":"Cuisine","uz":"Oshxona / milliy taomlar"},{"en":"Diverse","uz":"Turli-tuman"},{"en":"Unwind","uz":"Dam olish / erkinlashish"},{"en":"Precious","uz":"Qadrli / qimmatli"},{"en":"Recharge","uz":"Qayta kuch to'plash"},{"en":"Active","uz":"Faol"},{"en":"Surroundings","uz":"Atrof-muhit"},{"en":"Pollution","uz":"Ifloslanish"},{"en":"Clear your mind","uz":"Ongni tozalamoq"},{"en":"Boost","uz":"Oshirmoq / kuchaytirmoq"},{"en":"Freedom","uz":"Erkinlik"},{"en":"Rely","uz":"Ishonmoq"},{"en":"Convenient","uz":"Qulay"},{"en":"Memorable","uz":"Eslanarli, yodda qoladigan"},{"en":"Sustainability","uz":"Barqarorlik (atrof-muhitga zarar yetkazmaslik)"},{"en":"Motivated","uz":"Rag'batlantirilgan"},{"en":"Collaboration","uz":"Hamkorlik"},{"en":"Mini-deadlines","uz":"Kichik muddatlar (vaqtinchalik bosqichlar)"},{"en":"Adjust","uz":"Moslashmoq"},{"en":"Catch up","uz":"Yetib olish, orqada qolmaslik"},{"en":"Step up","uz":"Initsiativani qo'lga olish"},{"en":"Practical","uz":"Amaliy"},{"en":"Solve small issues","uz":"Kichik muammolarni hal qilish"},{"en":"Revolutionized","uz":"tubdan o'zgartirgan"},{"en":"Convincing","uz":"ishonchli"},{"en":"Attendance","uz":"qatnashish"},{"en":"Maintenance","uz":"ta'minlash"},{"en":"Tremendous","uz":"ulkan"},{"en":"Essential","uz":"zaruriy"},{"en":"Preserving","uz":"saqlash"},{"en":"Dedicated","uz":"maxsus mo'ljallangan"},{"en":"Obsolete","uz":"eskirgan"},{"en":"Evolving","uz":"rivojlanayotgan"}]},{"id":"b2t17","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":17,"p11":[{"q":"What do you like about your hometown?","a":"What I like most about my hometown is how peaceful and friendly it feels. People are welcoming, and there's a strong sense of belonging. I also enjoy the natural beauty—it has parks, trees, and fresh air. It's not too crowded, so life feels more relaxed compared to a big city. Everything is close by, which makes daily life really convenient."},{"q":"What is your favourite room in your home?","a":"My favorite room is definitely my bedroom. It's where I can unwind, think, and recharge after a long day. I've decorated it in a way that feels cozy and personal, with soft lighting and a few books. It's also the quietest place in the house, so I can read or listen to music without distractions. It's like my little escape."},{"q":"Do you have a mobile phone?","a":"Yes, of course—I use my mobile phone every day. It's not just for calls and texts; I also use it for studying, taking notes, and even relaxing with music or videos. It helps me stay connected with friends and family. Honestly, it's hard to imagine life without it now. It's such a useful tool for everything."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t17_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"In these pictures, I can see two dramatically different urban street scenes – one extremely crowded and chaotic, and the other peaceful and almost empty. I'd say the first image shows a busy city street during rush hour with masses of pedestrians squeezing between stopped traffic, while the second depicts a tranquil tree-lined avenue with just a single businessman walking along. The congestion in the left image looks absolutely suffocating, with people forced to weave between cars that are completely gridlocked in what appears to be downtown of a major metropolis. In stark contrast, the right image showcases a beautifully maintained pedestrian-friendly street with lush greenery creating a sort of urban oasis away from the typical city chaos."},{"q":"Which Street would you prefer to live on?","a":"I'd prefer to live on a quiet, clean street with lots of trees and friendly neighbors. Somewhere a bit away from the main roads, so it's peaceful but still close to shops and public transport. I like places where kids can play safely, and the air feels fresh. A calm environment really helps me feel relaxed and focused. It doesn't have to be fancy—just safe and comfortable."},{"q":"How does traffic on busy streets influence people's health?","a":"Busy traffic can seriously affect people's health. Constant noise and air pollution can lead to stress, headaches, and even breathing problems over time. It also makes it harder for people to sleep or relax, especially if they live near a main road. Some might even avoid walking or outdoor activities because of the traffic. So, it definitely has a negative impact on both physical and mental well-being."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t17_2.jpg","qs":["Can you describe a time when you had to act courageously?","What do you think gives people the strength to face their fears?","How does society celebrate the act of courage?"],"a":"I remember a time in high school when I had to act courageously. There was a classmate of mine who was constantly being bullied—he was quiet, kept to himself, and some kids thought it was funny to make fun of him. At first, I just ignored it, like a lot of people did. Honestly, I was afraid of becoming a target myself if I said anything. But one day, I saw it happening right in front of me—he was clearly upset, and everyone else just laughed or looked away. That moment really hit me. I couldn't just stand there anymore, so I spoke up and told the others to leave him alone. Then, I went with him to the school counselor to report what had been going on. It wasn't an easy thing to do. My heart was racing, and I was nervous about how others would react. But looking back, I'm\n\nreally glad I didn't stay silent. That experience showed me that courage doesn't always mean doing something dramatic—it can be as simple as standing up for someone when no one else will. It taught me that even small actions can make a big difference in someone's life. I think what gives people the strength to face their fears is a mix of empathy and values. When you really put yourself in someone else's shoes, it's hard to ignore what they're going through. Also, having a strong sense of right and wrong can push you to take action, even if you're scared. Support from others also plays a huge role—knowing someone has your back gives you the extra push you need. Society celebrates courage in different ways. Sometimes it's through awards or media coverage, like when someone saves a life or speaks out about an important issue. But I think everyday courage—like standing up for someone, or being honest when it's difficult—deserves more recognition too. These small acts might not make the headlines, but they help build a kinder, more supportive world."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t17_3.jpg","topic":"Cultural heritage sites should be open to tourists.","for":["Increases awareness of history","Boosts local economy","Provides funding for preservation"],"against":["Damages fragile sites","Adverse impact on environment","Focus shifts to profit over heritage"],"a":"So, the question is whether cultural heritage sites should be open to tourists. This is actually something I've thought about quite a bit during my travels.\n\nTo begin with, I believe there are significant merits to making these sites accessible to visitors. For one thing, allowing tourists to experience cultural landmarks firsthand dramatically increases awareness of history. When people can walk through ancient ruins or historic buildings, they develop a deeper appreciation for different cultures and historical periods than they ever could from simply reading about them in books. Additionally, tourism undeniably boosts local economies. In many regions, heritage sites create jobs and bring in substantial revenue for nearby communities that might otherwise struggle financially. Perhaps most importantly, the money generated from entrance fees and tourism often provides crucial funding for preservation efforts. Without this income stream, many priceless monuments might fall into disrepair due to lack of resources.\n\nHowever, we can't overlook the potential drawbacks. The most pressing concern is the physical damage that can occur when hordes of visitors traipse through fragile sites daily. Even with strict regulations, the cumulative impact of thousands of footsteps, touches, and breaths can deteriorate delicate structures and artifacts. There's also the broader environmental impact to consider, from increased pollution due to transportation to waste management challenges in areas not equipped for large crowds. Furthermore, when heritage sites become popular tourist destinations, there's always the risk that the focus shifts from cultural significance to commercial opportunity. This commercialization can undermine the authentic experience and diminish the site's educational value.\n\nIn conclusion, while opening cultural heritage sites to tourists offers clear benefits for historical awareness and economic development, it must be done thoughtfully to mitigate potential damage. I think the ideal approach involves finding a balance – perhaps through visitor quotas, strategic conservation efforts, and educational initiatives that emphasize respect for these irreplaceable treasures."},"words":[{"en":"Peaceful","uz":"Tinch"},{"en":"Belonging","uz":"Mansublik hissi"},{"en":"Natural beauty","uz":"Tabiiy go'zallik"},{"en":"Convenient","uz":"Qulay"},{"en":"Unwind","uz":"Dam olmoq"},{"en":"Recharge","uz":"Quvvat to'plash"},{"en":"Cozy","uz":"Qulay va yoqimli"},{"en":"Distraction","uz":"Chalg'ituvchi narsa"},{"en":"Escape","uz":"Qochish joyi / panoh"},{"en":"Connected","uz":"Bog'langan / aloqada bo'lgan"},{"en":"Quiet","uz":"Tinch"},{"en":"Fancy","uz":"Dabdabali"},{"en":"Comfortable","uz":"Qulay"},{"en":"Pollution","uz":"Ifloslanish"},{"en":"Stress","uz":"Stress"},{"en":"Breathing problems","uz":"Nafas olish muammolari"},{"en":"Avoid","uz":"Qochmoq"},{"en":"Outdoor","uz":"Tashqaridagi"},{"en":"Well-being","uz":"Farovonlik"},{"en":"Bullied","uz":"Tahqirlangan, bezorilik qurboni"},{"en":"Target","uz":"Nishon, e'tibor markazi (salbiy ma'noda)"},{"en":"Spoke up","uz":"Gapirdi, fikr bildirdi"},{"en":"Racing (heart)","uz":"Tez urayotgan (yurak)"},{"en":"Empathy","uz":"Hamdardlik"},{"en":"Values","uz":"Qadriyatlar"},{"en":"Sense of right and wrong","uz":"To'g'ri va noto'g'rini anglash"},{"en":"Support","uz":"Qo'llab-quvvatlash"},{"en":"Recognition","uz":"Tan olinishi"},{"en":"Deserves","uz":"Loyiq bo'lmoq"},{"en":"Merits","uz":"afzalliklar"},{"en":"Accessible","uz":"foydalanish mumkin bo'lgan"},{"en":"Appreciation","uz":"qadrlash"},{"en":"Undeniably","uz":"shubhasiz"},{"en":"Crucial","uz":"muhim"},{"en":"Priceless","uz":"bebaho"},{"en":"Drawbacks","uz":"kamchiliklar"},{"en":"Deteriorate","uz":"yomonlashmoq"},{"en":"Cumulative","uz":"jamlanuvchi"},{"en":"Mitigate","uz":"kamaytirmoq"}]},{"id":"b2t18","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":18,"p11":[{"q":"Do you like outdoor activities?","a":"Yes, I really enjoy outdoor activities—they help me clear my mind and stay active. I especially like hiking and cycling because they combine exercise with nature. Being outdoors is refreshing, and it's a great break from screens and indoor life. Even a simple walk in the park can boost my mood. It's a healthy habit I try to keep up with regularly."},{"q":"What kinds of public transport do you have in your country?","a":"In my country, we have several types of public transport like buses, trains, and taxis. In bigger cities, there are also metros and trams, which are fast and convenient. Most people rely on buses for daily travel because they're affordable and widely available. Some regions even have ride-sharing services. It's quite a mix, depending on where you live."},{"q":"What is your favourite season?","a":"My favorite season is spring. The weather is perfect—not too hot, not too cold—and everything feels fresh and full of life. Flowers bloom, trees turn green, and the whole atmosphere becomes more cheerful. It's also a great time to spend outdoors without worrying about extreme temperatures. I always feel more energetic and inspired in spring"}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t18_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"The image shows two contrasting transportation options - people cycling in one image versus driving cars in the other. I believe that the first image demonstrates an eco-friendly and health-conscious transportation choice where two individuals are enjoying their bicycle ride through what appears to be an urban residential area, In contrast, driving provides convenience, protection from weather elements, and the ability to travel longer distances more quickly, though at the cost of contributing to traffic congestion and pollution."},{"q":"Which transport do you think is better for short distances?","a":"For short distances, I think a bike is definitely better. It's eco-friendly, keeps you active, and helps avoid traffic. Bikes are also cheaper and easier to park, especially in crowded areas. Of course, a car is more comfortable in bad weather, but for quick trips, cycling just makes more sense. Plus, it's a great way to stay healthy while getting things done."},{"q":"How do transportation choices impact the environment?","a":"Transportation has a huge effect on the environment. Cars and buses release harmful gases that cause air pollution and contribute to climate change. Choosing greener options like bikes, electric vehicles, or public transport can really help reduce our carbon footprint. It's all about making smarter, cleaner choices. Even small changes can make a big difference over time."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t18_2.jpg","qs":["Can you describe a situation where you had to manage your time efficiently?","Why do you think time management is such a valuable skill?","How can schools and workplaces promote better time management practices?"],"a":"One situation that stands out when I had to manage my time efficiently was during my final year of university. I had multiple assignments and exams coming up, and at the same time, I was involved in a group project. It felt like everything was piling up at once, and I was starting to feel overwhelmed. I realized I had to find a way to manage my time better if I wanted to get everything done without burning out. So, I started by creating a detailed schedule. I broke down each task into smaller, more manageable parts, and assigned specific times for each one. I made sure to prioritize the most urgent assignments and set deadlines for each task. I also planned in breaks, so I wouldn't get too tired. To stay on track, I\n\nused reminders on my phone and checked my progress at the end of each day. This helped me stay focused and make steady progress on everything, without feeling too stressed. In the end, I completed everything on time, and it felt really rewarding to see all my hard work pay off. I think time management is such a valuable skill because it helps reduce stress and increases productivity. When you manage your time well, you're not rushing at the last minute or forgetting important things. It also allows you to find time for other activities like exercise or relaxation, which is just as important for maintaining balance in life. Schools and workplaces can promote better time management by encouraging planning and setting clear goals. For instance, schools can teach students how to prioritize tasks and set realistic deadlines for assignments. Workplaces can provide tools or software that help employees organize their tasks and track progress. Also, having a flexible environment where employees or students can manage their own time would allow them to work in a way that suits them best. The key is to help people understand that time management is about balance and making smarter choices rather than just working harder."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t18_3.jpg","topic":"Year-round schooling is better for students.","for":["Reduces summer learning loss","Keeps students engaged consistently","Helps working parents with childcare"],"against":["Lack of time to relax and recharge","Increases stress and burnout","Limits opportunities for summer activities"],"a":"Well, when it comes to year-round schooling, this is definitely a hot topic in education these days. Personally, I think there are compelling arguments on both sides that we need to consider carefully.\n\nOn the positive side, year-round schooling really helps prevent that summer learning loss we often see. You know how students forget so much during those long summer breaks? With more consistent schooling throughout the year, kids retain information better and teachers spend less time reteaching old material in September. Another benefit is that it keeps students consistently engaged with learning. Rather than having this massive three-month gap, shorter but more frequent breaks help maintain academic momentum and student interest in their studies.\n\nI should also mention that year-round schooling is incredibly helpful for working parents. Finding affordable childcare for the entire summer can be an absolute nightmare\n\nfor families where both parents work full-time. Year-round school schedules align much better with typical work schedules, easing this financial and logistical burden on families.\n\nHowever, there are definitely some legitimate concerns with this approach. First, students really do need time to relax and recharge. Those longer summer breaks give kids a chance to decompress from academic pressures, which is important for their mental health. The traditional summer vacation serves an important purpose in giving everyone a proper break.\n\nAlso, year-round schooling can actually increase stress and burnout for both students and teachers. Without that extended period to completely disconnect from school, many might experience heightened anxiety and exhaustion from the constant cycle of classes and shorter breaks.\n\nLastly, year-round school limits opportunities for those enriching summer activities like camps, family vacations, or summer jobs for older students. These experiences provide valuable life skills and memories that can't be replicated in a classroom setting.\n\nSo while I see the benefits of year-round schooling, especially for academic continuity and working families, I'm not entirely convinced it's better for all students. I think we need to find a balance that addresses learning loss while still giving kids the time they need to just be kids."},"words":[{"en":"Clear my mind","uz":"Ongimni tozalamoq"},{"en":"Hiking","uz":"Tog'ga chiqish"},{"en":"Refreshing","uz":"Yangi kuch beradigan"},{"en":"Boost","uz":"Ko'tarish / oshirish"},{"en":"Rely","uz":"Ishonmoq"},{"en":"Affordable","uz":"Arzon / hamyonbop"},{"en":"Widely available","uz":"Keng tarqalgan"},{"en":"Ride-sharing","uz":"Avtomobil ulashish xizmati"},{"en":"Bloom","uz":"Gulli bo'lish / gullamoq"},{"en":"Inspired","uz":"Ilhomlangan"},{"en":"Eco-friendly","uz":"Atrof-muhitga zarar yetkazmaydigan"},{"en":"Active","uz":"Faol"},{"en":"Crowded","uz":"Gavjum"},{"en":"Cycling","uz":"Velosiped haydash"},{"en":"Pollution","uz":"Ifloslanish"},{"en":"Climate change","uz":"Iqlim o'zgarishi"},{"en":"Electric vehicles","uz":"Elektr transport vositalari"},{"en":"Carbon footprint","uz":"Uglerod izlari (tabiatga ta'sir)"},{"en":"Greener","uz":"Ekologik toza"},{"en":"Smarter","uz":"Aqlli / ongli"},{"en":"Overwhelmed","uz":"Haddan tashqari bosim ostida bo'lgan"},{"en":"Schedule","uz":"Jadval"},{"en":"Prioritize","uz":"Ustuvor qilish"},{"en":"Steady progress","uz":"Barqaror taraqqiyot"},{"en":"Productivity","uz":"Ishchanlik"},{"en":"Relaxation","uz":"Dam olish"},{"en":"Balance","uz":"Muvozanat"},{"en":"Realistic","uz":"Haqiqiy"},{"en":"Track progress","uz":"Taraqqiyotni kuzatish"},{"en":"Compelling","uz":"ishontiruvchi"},{"en":"Retain","uz":"saqlab qolmoq"},{"en":"Momentum","uz":"harakat kuchi"},{"en":"Logistical","uz":"tashkiliy"},{"en":"Legitimate","uz":"asosli"},{"en":"Decompress","uz":"bosimdan chiqmoq"},{"en":"Burnout","uz":"toliqish"},{"en":"Enriching","uz":"boyituvchi"}]},{"id":"b2t19","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":19,"p11":[{"q":"What is your favourite song?","a":"One of my favorite songs is Someone Like You by Adele. Her voice is powerful, and the lyrics are really emotional—it always gives me goosebumps. I like songs that tell a story and make you feel something deep. This one reminds me of certain moments in my life, so it feels personal. I never get tired of listening to it."},{"q":"Do you prefer to read local news or international news?","a":"I try to keep a balance, but I usually prefer international news. It helps me stay informed about what's happening around the world, especially with global issues like climate change or politics. Local news is useful too, but international topics feel more relevant sometimes. It also gives me a broader perspective. Still, I check both regularly."},{"q":"Who taught you to be polite?","a":"Definitely my parents. From a young age, they always reminded me to say \"please\" and \"thank you\" and to treat everyone with respect. They led by example, so I learned a lot\n\njust by watching how they spoke to others. Politeness became a natural habit for me over time. I'm really thankful for that."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t19_12_0.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"The image shows contrasting shopping methods with online shopping on the left and in-store shopping on the right. I believe the left image depicts a person shopping on an e-commerce website using a laptop and credit card, while the right image shows a woman browsing through clothing items in a physical retail store. Online shopping offers convenience and the ability to compare prices across multiple stores without leaving home, whereas in-store shopping provides a tactile experience where customers can touch and try products before purchasing. Despite the growing popularity of e-commerce, many consumers still prefer the traditional shopping experience for certain items like clothing where fit and texture matter significantly."},{"q":"Which way of shopping has more advantages?","a":"I think online shopping has more advantages overall. It's super convenient—you can buy anything from the comfort of your home and compare prices easily. There's also a wider selection of products, and you often find better deals online. Of course, in-store shopping is great when you want to try things on, but for saving time and money, online wins for me."},{"q":"How has the Internet changed shopping habits?","a":"The Internet has completely transformed how people shop. Now, most people check reviews, compare prices, and even buy things without ever going to a store. It's faster, more flexible, and available 24/7. Online shopping has made impulse buying more common too. Overall, people are more informed and more used to convenience now."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t19_2.jpg","qs":["Can you describe a teacher who inspired you?","Why do you think education is important for personal growth?","How can education systems adapt to modern challenges?"],"a":"One teacher who really inspired me was my English teacher in high school. Her name was Ms. Safarova, and she had this amazing energy that made every lesson interesting. She didn't just teach us grammar or vocabulary—she encouraged us to express ourselves, think critically, and speak with confidence. What made her stand out was the way she treated every student with respect. Even if someone made a mistake, she never made them feel embarrassed. Instead, she would turn it into a learning moment for the whole class. That positive atmosphere made me feel more confident in myself and actually made me enjoy learning. Thanks to her, I started reading more, improving my speaking, and even joining some school competitions. I think\n\nwhat inspired me most was that she believed in every student's potential, even when we didn't believe in ourselves. That kind of encouragement really sticks with you and pushes you to aim higher. Education, in my opinion, is super important for personal growth. It's not just about learning facts or passing exams—it's about developing your thinking, your values, and how you see the world. A good education teaches you how to solve problems, work with others, and be open to new ideas. It also helps you discover your interests and strengths, which plays a big role in your future. To deal with modern challenges, I think education systems need to become more flexible and updated. For example, there should be more focus on digital skills, emotional intelligence, and creativity—not just memorizing facts. Schools should also offer more real-life learning opportunities, like internships or project-based learning, to prepare students for today's fast-changing world. And of course, mental health support should be part of education too, especially with all the pressure students face nowadays."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t19_3.jpg","topic":"Animals should not be kept in zoos.","for":["Animals can live freely in their natural habitats.","It supports animal rights and prevents mistreatment.","Reduces stress and unnatural behavior caused by captivity."],"against":["Fewer chances to educate people about wildlife.","Harder to protect and breed endangered species.","Less opportunity for scientists to study animals closely."],"a":"Well, this is definitely a topic that gets people fired up these days! Should animals be kept in zoos? It's not a straightforward question, and I can see valid points on both sides.\n\nTo start with the case against zoos, there are several strong arguments. First, animals naturally belong in their native habitats where they can roam freely. When kept in captivity, even in spacious enclosures, they're still confined to areas that are tiny compared to their natural ranges. I've always felt there's something sad about seeing a magnificent creature like a tiger pacing in a limited space.\n\nAnother important consideration is animal welfare. Many zoos have been criticized for mistreating animals or keeping them in poor conditions that lead to stress. You can often observe unnatural behaviors in captive animals - things like\n\nrepetitive movements or self-harm that you'd never see in the wild. This suggests they're suffering psychological distress.\n\nOn the other hand, there are legitimate benefits to zoos. They play a crucial role in educating the public about wildlife conservation. Many people will never have the opportunity to travel to see these animals in their natural habitats, and zoos provide a window into understanding different species and ecosystems.\n\nZoos are also instrumental in protecting endangered species. Many have successful breeding programs that have helped recover populations on the brink of extinction. The California condor is a prime example - it was saved from extinction largely through captive breeding efforts.\n\nAdditionally, zoos enable scientists to study animals up close, which can lead to valuable insights about animal behavior, health, and conservation strategies that might not be possible to obtain in the wild.\n\nIn conclusion, while I personally lean toward thinking animals should ideally live in their natural environments, I recognize that well-run, ethical zoos serve important purposes in education, conservation, and research. Perhaps the solution isn't eliminating zoos entirely but transforming them into more humane sanctuaries and rehabilitation centers focused primarily on conservation rather than entertainment."},"words":[{"en":"Powerful","uz":"Kuchli"},{"en":"Emotional","uz":"Hissiyotli"},{"en":"Goosebumps","uz":"Tovuq terisi (hayajonlanish holati)"},{"en":"Personal","uz":"Shaxsiy"},{"en":"Informed","uz":"Xabardor"},{"en":"Global","uz":"Butunjahon / global"},{"en":"Perspective","uz":"Qarash / nuqtayi nazar"},{"en":"Respect","uz":"Hurmat"},{"en":"Lead by example","uz":"Namuna ko'rsatmoq"},{"en":"Habit","uz":"Odat"},{"en":"Convenient","uz":"Qulay"},{"en":"Compare","uz":"Solishtirmoq"},{"en":"Selection","uz":"Tanlov"},{"en":"Deals","uz":"Chegirmalar / foydali takliflar"},{"en":"Try on","uz":"Kiyp ko'rmoq"},{"en":"Save","uz":"Tejamoq"},{"en":"Transform","uz":"O'zgartirmoq"},{"en":"Flexible","uz":"Moslashuvchan"},{"en":"Impulse buying","uz":"To'satdan xarid qilish"},{"en":"Inspired","uz":"Ilhomlantirgan"},{"en":"Confidence","uz":"O'ziga ishonch"},{"en":"Critically","uz":"Tanqidiy tarzda (fikrlash nuqtai nazarida)"},{"en":"Encouragement","uz":"Rag'bat"},{"en":"Potential","uz":"Salohiyat"},{"en":"Personal growth","uz":"Shaxsiy rivojlanish"},{"en":"Digital skills","uz":"Raqamli ko'nikmalar"},{"en":"Project-based learning","uz":"Loyihaga asoslangan o'rganish"},{"en":"Mental health","uz":"Ruhiy salomatlik"},{"en":"Magnificent","uz":"hashamatli"},{"en":"Confined","uz":"cheklangan"},{"en":"Welfare","uz":"farovonlik"},{"en":"Criticized","uz":"tanqid qilingan"},{"en":"Repetitive","uz":"takroriy"},{"en":"Legitimate","uz":"qonuniy"},{"en":"Instrumental","uz":"muhim rol o'ynovchi"}]},{"id":"b2t20","book":"Speaking 2.0","n":20,"p11":[{"q":"What do you do in the evenings In the evenings, I usually unwind after a hectic day. I often read a book or watch a documentary to relax my mind. Sometimes I catch up with friends online or go for a walk to clear my head. If I feel productive, I might work on personal","a":"projects. It really depends on my mood."},{"q":"Do you live in a house or flat I live in a flat in the city center. It's quite compact but cozy, and it has everything I need. The location is super convenient because it's close to shops, cafés, and public transport. I enjoy the buzz of urban life, though sometimes I do miss the peace of","a":"a house in the suburbs."},{"q":"What do you do when you are bored?","a":"When I'm bored, I try to do something that sparks my creativity. I might listen to music, sketch a bit, or learn something new online. Occasionally, I just daydream or scroll through social media for a while. Boredom can actually be a good trigger for imagination, I think."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b2t20_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b2t20_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"These images contrast fast food with home cooking, highlighting different approaches to meal preparation. I think the first image shows a tempting spread of convenience foods like burgers and fries, while the second depicts someone preparing fresh ingredients, possibly for a healthier, home-cooked meal. The juxtaposition of these images reflects the dilemma many of us face daily: choosing between quick, readily available food and taking time to prepare nutritious meals from scratch. The fast food option offers undeniable convenience but often comes with nutritional drawbacks and excessive packaging waste. Alternatively, home cooking provides nutritional control and can be more economical, though it demands time and culinary skills many busy people struggle to find."},{"q":"What are the advantages of home-made food?","a":"Home-made food is definitely healthier because you know exactly what goes into it. It's usually fresher and free from unnecessary additives or preservatives. Plus, it's budget-friendly and can even be a fun way to bond with family while cooking together. You also have full control over taste and portion size."},{"q":"Which one do you prefer: Fast food or home-made food?","a":"I definitely prefer home-made food. It's not only more nutritious, but also gives a sense of comfort and satisfaction. Fast food is convenient, but it often feels greasy and heavy. With home cooking, I can experiment with recipes and make meals that suit my taste. It just feels more rewarding."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b2t20_2.jpg","qs":["Describe an unforgettable learning experience you have had.","What motivates to learn new things?","How important it is to learn new things?"],"a":"One unforgettable learning experience I had was when I took part in a creative writing workshop during my summer break a couple of years ago. I had always enjoyed writing, but I never really took it seriously until that workshop. The instructor was incredibly inspiring; she made us think outside the box and pushed us to experiment with new writing styles and techniques I'd never considered before. I remember we worked on different writing prompts, and at first, I felt a bit unsure, but as we progressed, I felt more confident in my abilities. By the end of the workshop, I had written a short story that I'm still really proud of, and the feedback I got from my peers was amazing. The experience taught me that learning doesn't always have to be formal – it can be fun, hands-on, and really eye-opening. What motivates me to learn new things is definitely my curiosity and the desire for personal growth. I think it's fascinating to explore different subjects, whether it's something creative like painting or something technical like coding. There's something exciting about discovering how things work and understanding concepts that were once unfamiliar to me. For me, it's not just about gaining new knowledge, but also about challenging myself to improve and broaden my perspective. And, I won't lie, I also love the sense of accomplishment I get when I finally master something I've been working on for a while. Learning new things is incredibly important because it helps us stay sharp and adaptable in a world that's constantly changing. Whether it's new technology, social trends, or even just learning to communicate better, being open to new ideas keeps us relevant. Plus, it's not just about professional growth; learning can enrich our personal lives, too. It helps us connect with others, stay engaged with the world around us, and gives us the tools to make informed decisions. Honestly, I believe it's essential for long-term happiness and success."},"p3":{"card":"img/sp/b2t20_3.jpg","topic":"Public streets should have surveillance cameras.","for":["Increases public safety","Helps solve crimes faster","Acts as a deterrent for illegal behavior"],"against":["Raises privacy concerns","Expensive to install and maintain","Risk of misuse or hacking"],"a":"The question of whether public streets should have surveillance cameras is something I've actually thought about quite a bit recently. It's become such a common sight in most cities these days, and there are definitely strong arguments on both sides of this debate.\n\nWhen it comes to the advantages, public safety is probably the most compelling reason to support surveillance cameras. In high-crime areas especially, having cameras can make people feel much safer when walking around, particularly at night.\n\nThese cameras can also be incredibly valuable for solving crimes. When something happens, having video evidence can dramatically speed up investigations that might otherwise hit dead ends. Police can identify suspects more quickly and gather concrete evidence that holds up in court.\n\nAnother important benefit is the deterrent effect. When potential criminals know they're being watched, they're much less likely to break the law in the first place. It's basic human psychology – most people behave better when they know their actions are being monitored.\n\nHowever, there are legitimate concerns on the other side of this debate. Privacy is a fundamental right that many people feel is being eroded in our digital age. The idea of being constantly recorded while going about your daily business makes many people uncomfortable.\n\nThe financial aspect can't be ignored either. Installing and maintaining a comprehensive camera network across public streets requires significant investment from local governments. This money could potentially be used for other important community needs like education or healthcare.\n\nFinally, there's always the risk of misuse or security breaches. If these systems are hacked or the footage falls into the wrong hands, it could lead to serious privacy violations.\n\nIn conclusion, while I can see both perspectives, I think surveillance cameras in public spaces are probably necessary in today's world – but with strict regulations on how the footage can be used and stored."},"words":[{"en":"Unwind","uz":"Dam olish"},{"en":"Hectic","uz":"Juda band"},{"en":"Compact","uz":"Ixcham"},{"en":"Cozy","uz":"Qulay"},{"en":"Convenient","uz":"Qulay (mos)"},{"en":"Buzz","uz":"Shovqin (shahar hayoti)"},{"en":"Spark","uz":"Ilhomlantirmoq"},{"en":"Sketch","uz":"Chizmoq"},{"en":"Daydream","uz":"Xayol surmoq"},{"en":"Trigger","uz":"Sabab bo'lmoq / Qo'zg'atmoq"},{"en":"Additive","uz":"Qo'shimcha modda"},{"en":"Preservative","uz":"Saqlovchi modda"},{"en":"Budget-friendly","uz":"Hamyonbop"},{"en":"Bond (with someone)","uz":"Yaqinlashmoq, bog'lanmoq"},{"en":"Portion size","uz":"Porsiya hajmi"},{"en":"Nutritious","uz":"Foydali (oziqaviy jihatdan)"},{"en":"Satisfaction","uz":"Qoniqish"},{"en":"Greasy","uz":"Yog'li (ortiqcha)"},{"en":"Experiment (with food)","uz":"Tajriba qilmoq (ovqat bilan)"},{"en":"Rewarding","uz":"Qoniqarli, foydali"},{"en":"Unforgettable","uz":"unutilmas"},{"en":"Inspiring","uz":"ilhomlantiruvchi"},{"en":"Experiment","uz":"tajriba o'tkazish"},{"en":"Techniques","uz":"texnikalar"},{"en":"Proud","uz":"g'ururlanmoq"},{"en":"Formal","uz":"rasmiy"},{"en":"Hands-on","uz":"amaliy"},{"en":"Eye-opening","uz":"ko'z ochuvchi"},{"en":"Curiosity","uz":"qiziqish"},{"en":"Adapt","uz":"moslashmoq"},{"en":"Compelling","uz":"ishontiruvchi"},{"en":"Surveillance","uz":"kuzatuv"},{"en":"Deterrent","uz":"to'sqinlik"},{"en":"Concrete evidence","uz":"aniq dalil"},{"en":"Eroded","uz":"yemirilgan"},{"en":"Perpetual","uz":"doimiy"},{"en":"Oppressive","uz":"ezuvchi"},{"en":"Comprehensive","uz":"keng qamrovli"},{"en":"Breaches","uz":"buzilishlar"}]},{"id":"b3t1","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":1,"p11":[{"q":"What do you usually do in the evening?","a":"In the evening, I usually try to unwind after a long and productive day. I often spend some time reviewing my work or planning what I need to do the next day. After that, I prefer doing something relaxing, like watching an interesting video, listening to music, or occasionally reading a book. These activities help me clear my mind and feel more relaxed before going to sleep."},{"q":"Do you prefer playing sports or watching sports?","a":"I definitely prefer playing sports rather than simply watching them. Being physically active makes me feel more energetic and refreshed. For instance, I sometimes play football with my friends, and it's both fun and a great way to stay healthy. Watching sports can be enjoyable, especially during big tournaments, but in my opinion it's much more exciting to actually take part in the game."},{"q":"Can you describe a park in your city?","a":"Yes, there is a well-known park in my city that many residents like to visit. It's quite spacious and full of trees, which creates a calm and refreshing atmosphere. People often go there to walk, exercise, or simply spend time with their families and friends. There are also benches and small cafés where visitors can relax and enjoy the peaceful environment."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t1_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t1_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"In these pictures, I can see two different ways people pay for goods and services. In the first image, a customer is paying with cash by handing banknotes to a cashier. This is a traditional form of payment that has been used for many years and is still common in many places. Cash payments are simple because they do not require any technology or electronic system. In contrast, the second picture shows a person paying with a card using a payment terminal. This type of payment is much more modern and is widely used today. Card payments are usually quicker and more convenient, especially in busy shops or restaurants. Overall, the pictures illustrate the contrast between traditional cash payments and modern electronic transactions."},{"q":"Which do you think is more convenient: paying with cash or paying with a card?","a":"In my opinion, paying with a card is generally more convenient. It allows people to complete transactions quickly without carrying large amounts of cash. In addition, many cards now support contactless payments, which makes the process even faster. However, cash can still be useful in small shops or in situations where electronic systems are unavailable."},{"q":"Do you think cash will disappear in the future because of card and digital payments?","a":"I do not believe cash will completely disappear in the near future. Although digital and card payments are becoming more common, many people still rely on cash for everyday purchases. In addition, some regions do not have reliable access to electronic payment systems. For this reason, cash will probably continue to exist alongside digital payment methods for quite a long time."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t1_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a moment when you felt truly free.","What made that moment special for you?","How did this experience influence your thoughts or feelings afterward?"],"a":"One moment when I felt truly free was during a quiet evening walk after finishing a very demanding period of study. I had been preparing for several important exams, so my routine had been quite stressful and tightly organized. When everything was finally over, I decided to go for a walk in a nearby park. The weather was calm, the air felt fresh, and there were only a few people around, which created a very peaceful atmosphere. At that moment, I realized that I had no deadlines or pressure, and it gave me a strong sense of freedom. What made that moment especially meaningful was the feeling of relief and calmness I experienced. After weeks of concentrating on my studies, my mind had finally relaxed. I could enjoy simple things such as the cool breeze, the quiet\n\nenvironment, and the beautiful colors of the evening sky. It reminded me that freedom is sometimes found in very ordinary moments. After that experience, my perspective on daily life changed slightly. I began to understand that focusing only on work or study can make people feel exhausted over time. Since then, I have tried to create a healthier balance by taking short breaks and spending time on relaxing activities. This helps me stay more positive, refreshed, and motivated in my daily routine."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"The differences between public and private transportation?","for":["cheaper for individuals and reduces daily travel costs","decreases traffic congestion in cities","more environmentally friendly because fewer cars are used"],"against":["less comfort and privacy compared to private vehicles","limited schedules and routes","often crowded during peak hours"],"a":"The comparison between public transportation and private transportation involves both advantages and disadvantages.\n\nOne clear advantage of public transportation is that it is cheaper for individuals and reduces daily travel costs. Many people can travel using a single bus or train, which allows passengers to spend less money compared to owning and maintaining a private car. In addition, public transportation decreases traffic congestion in cities because fewer private vehicles are used on the roads. When more people rely on shared transport, the number of cars in urban areas becomes lower. Another important benefit is that it is more environmentally friendly since fewer cars are used, which helps reduce pollution and supports a cleaner environment.\n\nHowever, public transportation also has several disadvantages. One of the main drawbacks is that it offers less comfort and privacy compared to private vehicles, where people can travel in a more personal and controlled\n\nspace. Another limitation is that public transport usually has limited schedules and routes, meaning passengers must adjust their plans according to fixed timetables and predetermined paths. Moreover, buses and trains are often crowded during peak hours, especially in busy cities, which can make commuting less convenient and sometimes stressful for daily passengers."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t2","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":2,"p11":[{"q":"Do you live in a house or a flat?","a":"At the moment, I live in a flat. It's not very large, but it's comfortable and convenient for daily life. What I like most is that everything I need is nearby, such as shops and public transport. Although living in a house might offer more space and privacy, a flat is much easier to maintain and manage."},{"q":"Can you tell me about your first teacher?","a":"Yes, I remember my first teacher quite clearly. She was very kind and patient, especially with young students who were just starting school. What I appreciated most was the way she encouraged us to ask questions and stay curious. Because of her supportive attitude, I actually started to enjoy studying and felt more confident in class."},{"q":"Can you describe your house?","a":"My house is fairly simple but very comfortable. It has several rooms, including a living room, a kitchen, and a few bedrooms. The place I like most is the living room because that's where my family usually gathers to talk or relax together. Overall, it's a warm and welcoming place where I feel very comfortable."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t2_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t2_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"In these pictures, I can see two different ways people read books. In the first picture, a person is reading a traditional printed book. This type of reading is very common and many people enjoy it because it creates a more immersive experience. Readers can physically hold the book, turn the pages, and focus without digital distractions.\n\nIn the second picture, someone is reading an e-book on an electronic device such as a tablet or an e-reader. This method is much more modern and convenient because a person can store hundreds of books on a single device. It is also very portable and practical, especially for people who travel frequently. Overall, the pictures show the contrast between traditional reading and digital reading."},{"q":"Which do you think is better: reading printed books or reading e-books?","a":"In my opinion, both options have their own advantages, but I personally prefer printed books. Reading a physical book feels more engaging and immersive because there are fewer distractions compared to electronic devices. In addition, printed books are more comfortable for the eyes during long reading sessions. However, e-books are extremely convenient and portable. You can easily carry many books in one device, which makes them ideal for traveling or commuting."},{"q":"Do you think printed books will disappear in the future?","a":"I do not believe printed books will completely disappear in the future. Although e-books are becoming increasingly popular due to their convenience and accessibility, many people still appreciate the experience of reading a physical book. Printed books provide a sense of authenticity and emotional connection that digital devices often lack.\n\nFor this reason, I think both formats will continue to exist, and people will simply choose the one that best suits their preferences and lifestyle."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t2_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a skill you have learned recently.","How did you learn this skill and what difficulties did you face while learning it?","How do you think this skill will help you in the future or in your daily life?"],"a":"One skill I have learned recently is improving my typing speed on the computer. Because I spend a lot of time working with texts and preparing materials, I realized that typing quickly and accurately is very important. At first, my typing speed was quite slow, so I decided to practice regularly using online typing exercises. Gradually, I noticed that my speed and accuracy started to improve, which made my work much more efficient. I mainly learned this skill through daily practice. I used typing websites and tried to practice for at least fifteen or\n\ntwenty minutes every day. In the beginning, the most difficult part was avoiding mistakes because I often pressed the wrong keys when trying to type faster. Sometimes it was also frustrating to repeat the same exercises many times. However, with patience and consistent practice, I slowly became more comfortable with the keyboard. I believe this skill will be very helpful for me in the future. Since many tasks today involve working on computers, typing quickly can save a lot of time. It also allows me to focus more on ideas instead of worrying about the keyboard. In my daily life, it helps me complete my work faster and communicate more efficiently when writing messages, reports, or other documents"},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"The use of phones should be prohibited in school areas","for":["improves students' concentration and reduces distractions during lessons","prevents cheating and misuse of technology during exams","encourages more face-to-face communication and social interaction"],"against":["phones can be useful educational tools for research and learning","students may need phones for emergencies or communication with parents","banning phones may be difficult to enforce consistently"],"a":"The use of mobile phones in school environments is a topic that generates considerable debate among educators and parents.\n\nOne argument in favour of prohibiting phones in school areas is that such a rule can improve students' concentration and reduce distractions during lessons. Many students tend to check messages or social media instead of paying attention to the teacher, which negatively affects their learning process. In addition, banning phones can help prevent cheating and the misuse of technology during exams, since students would not have the opportunity to access online information or communicate with others. Furthermore, removing phones from classrooms may encourage more face-to-face communication and social interaction among students, helping them develop stronger interpersonal skills and build better relationships with their peers.\n\nOn the other hand, there are also several arguments against banning phones in schools. For example, smartphones can serve as useful educational tools that allow students to quickly search for information, access learning platforms, or use educational applications during lessons. Moreover, many parents prefer their children to carry phones so that they can communicate in case of emergencies or unexpected situations. Another practical concern is that enforcing a complete ban on phones may be difficult for schools to manage consistently, especially in large institutions where monitoring every student at all times can be challenging."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t3","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":3,"p11":[{"q":"What do you usually eat for breakfast?","a":"For breakfast, I usually prefer something simple but filling. Most of the time, I have eggs, bread, and a cup of tea or coffee. Sometimes I also eat fruit because it helps me feel more energetic in the morning. I think breakfast is quite important since it gives me the energy I need to start the day productively."},{"q":"Do you like any sports?","a":"Yes, I do. I particularly enjoy football because it's both exciting and physically demanding. Playing football with friends is a great way to stay active and relieve stress at the same time. I also like the teamwork involved in the game, since it teaches cooperation and quick decision-making."},{"q":"Can you describe your room?","a":"My room is fairly simple but very comfortable. It has a bed, a desk where I usually study or work, and a bookshelf with several books. I try to keep the room tidy because it helps me concentrate better. Overall, it's a quiet and personal space where I can relax, study, and spend time alone."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t3_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t3_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"In these pictures, I can see two different types of activities people usually do in their free time. In the first picture, people are doing an indoor activity, such as reading, studying, or playing games inside a building. Indoor activities are usually done in comfortable environments like homes, libraries, or entertainment centers. They are convenient because people can enjoy them regardless of the weather. In contrast, the second picture shows people participating in outdoor activities, such as walking, playing sports, or spending time in nature. Outdoor activities are often more physically active and allow people to enjoy fresh air and natural surroundings. Overall, the pictures highlight the difference between relaxing indoor activities and more active outdoor experience"},{"q":"Which do you prefer: indoor activities or outdoor activities?","a":"Personally, I prefer outdoor activities because they allow me to stay physically active and spend time in a natural environment. Activities like walking, cycling, or\n\nplaying sports can improve both physical health and mental well-being. However, indoor activities can also be enjoyable, especially when the weather is bad or when someone wants to relax and focus on something calm like reading or watching a movie."},{"q":"Do you think people today spend less time doing outdoor activities?","a":"Yes, I do think that people nowadays tend to spend less time outdoors than they did in the past. A major factor behind this change is the growing influence of technology. Devices such as smartphones, computers, and video games often keep people entertained indoors for long periods of time. Another reason is that modern lifestyles are quite busy, and in many cities there are fewer convenient spaces for outdoor recreation. Nevertheless, awareness about the benefits of physical activity is gradually increasing, so some people are making an effort to spend more time outside and lead a healthier lifestyle."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t3_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a secret you shared with someone.","Who did you share the secret with and why did you trust this person?","How did sharing this secret affect your relationship with that person?"],"a":"One secret I once shared was about an important personal decision I was thinking about. At that time, I felt uncertain and needed someone I could talk to honestly. Instead of keeping everything to myself, I decided to open up about my thoughts and concerns. Sharing the secret helped me feel much lighter because I finally expressed something that had been on my mind for a while. I shared this secret with one of my closest friends because I truly trusted that person. We have known each other for many years and have always supported each other during difficult situations. I knew that my friend would listen carefully and\n\nwould not judge me or tell other people. This sense of trust made it easier for me to speak openly about my feelings and thoughts. After sharing the secret, our relationship actually became stronger. We started to communicate more honestly and support each other more often. It showed me that trust is a very important part of friendship. When people feel safe sharing personal things, it can create a deeper connection and make the relationship more meaningful."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Homework should be abolished at school","for":["reduces academic stress and pressure on students","allows students to spend more time on hobbies, rest, and family","learning can become more efficient during school hours"],"against":["homework helps students reinforce and practice what they learn in class","it develops responsibility and independent learning skills","teachers can evaluate students' understanding through homework"],"a":"The practice of assigning homework in schools is often discussed, with some people supporting it while others believe it should be removed.\n\nOne argument in favour of abolishing homework is that it can reduce academic stress and pressure on students. Many learners already spend long hours at school, and additional assignments at home may make them feel overwhelmed and exhausted. Furthermore, removing homework would allow students to spend more time on hobbies, relaxation, and family activities, which are also important for their personal development and mental well-being. Another possible advantage is that learning could become more efficient during school hours, encouraging teachers and students to focus more actively and productively while they are in the classroom.\n\nHowever, there are also strong arguments against eliminating homework completely. One important reason is that homework helps students reinforce and practice what they learn in class, which can improve their understanding of the\n\nsubject. In addition, completing assignments outside the classroom can develop responsibility and independent learning skills, as students learn how to manage their time and solve problems on their own. Homework also allows teachers to evaluate students' understanding of the material and identify areas where additional support may be needed."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t4","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":4,"p11":[{"q":"How is your room decorated?","a":"My room is decorated in a fairly simple but comfortable style. I prefer a clean and organized environment, so I don't keep too many unnecessary things. There is a desk, a bookshelf, and a few decorations on the wall, such as photos and a small painting. Overall, the room feels calm and cozy, which helps me concentrate and relax."},{"q":"Have you got many books?","a":"Yes, I have quite a lot of books, especially educational and language-learning ones. I enjoy reading because it helps me expand my knowledge and improve my vocabulary. Most of my books are on a small bookshelf in my room, and I try to read at least a few pages whenever I have free time."},{"q":"What is your favorite song?","a":"One of my favorite songs is a calm and emotional track that I often listen to when I want to relax. I really like the melody and the meaningful lyrics because they create a peaceful atmosphere. Music like this helps me focus, especially when I'm studying or thinking about something important."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t4_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t4_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"In these pictures, I can see two different working environments. In the first picture, a person is working outside, possibly in a field, construction site, or another outdoor setting. Outdoor jobs usually involve physical activity and require people to work in different weather conditions. These types of jobs can be physically demanding but also refreshing because workers spend time in the open air.\n\nIn contrast, the second picture shows someone working inside an office or indoor workplace. Indoor jobs are usually more structured and comfortable because people work in controlled environments. These jobs often involve using computers, attending meetings, and performing mental tasks. Overall, the pictures illustrate the contrast between physically active outdoor work and more sedentary indoor work."},{"q":"Which do you think is better: working outside or working inside?","a":"In my opinion, working inside is generally more comfortable and convenient. Indoor workplaces usually provide stable conditions such as air conditioning, proper equipment, and protection from extreme weather. This allows people to focus better on their tasks. However, working outside can also be enjoyable for people who prefer physical activity and do not like sitting for long hours. It often allows workers to stay active and spend more time in fresh air."},{"q":"Do you think more people will work indoors in the future?","a":"Absolutely, I believe more people will work indoors in the future. As technology continues to develop, many jobs are becoming digital and require computers or internet access. This naturally leads to more office-based or remote work.\n\nAt the same time, some professions such as construction, agriculture, and transportation will always require outdoor work. Therefore, while indoor jobs may increase, outdoor occupations will still remain essential."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t4_2.jpg","qs":["Describe a time when you felt confused about something important.","What caused this confusion?","How did you eventually understand the situation?"],"a":"One time when I felt confused about something important was during a period when I had to make a decision related to my academic plans. At that time, I had several possible options, and each one seemed to offer different advantages and opportunities. Because the decision could influence my future studies and long-term goals, I wanted to choose carefully. However, the more I thought about it, the more uncertain I became. I kept comparing the options and imagining different outcomes, which made the situation even more complicated. As a result, I spent a lot of time thinking about the decision\n\nwithout feeling completely confident about which path would be the best one. he confusion was mainly caused by the fact that there were many factors to consider. Each option had both positive and negative aspects, and it was difficult to predict which one would lead to better results in the future. In addition, I received different opinions from people around me. Some suggested that I should follow one direction, while others recommended a different approach. Although their advice was helpful, hearing many different perspectives sometimes made the situation even more confusing. I also felt pressure because I knew the decision was important and could affect my future opportunities. Eventually, I managed to understand the situation more clearly by taking some time to think calmly and analyze my priorities. Instead of focusing only on other people's opinions, I started considering my own interests, strengths, and long-term goals. I also tried to gather more information about each option so that I could evaluate them more realistically. After reflecting carefully and discussing the situation with a few trusted people, I finally felt more confident about my choice. This experience taught me that confusion is sometimes a natural part of making important decisions, and that patience and thoughtful reflection can help people reach a clearer understanding."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Cities should limit cars and promote cycling","for":["reduces traffic congestion in urban areas","improves air quality and reduces pollution","encourages a healthier lifestyle through physical activity"],"against":["cycling infrastructure may be expensive to develop","not all people can cycle due to age, health, or distance","limiting cars may cause inconvenience for commuters and businesses"],"a":"The proposal that cities should limit the use of cars and promote cycling has attracted growing attention in recent years, especially as urban areas face increasing transportation and environmental challenges.\n\nOne argument in favour of this idea is that it can help reduce traffic congestion in urban areas. When a larger number of people choose bicycles instead of cars, the overall number of vehicles on the roads decreases, which can make daily travel more efficient and less stressful. In addition, promoting cycling can improve air quality and reduce pollution because bicycles do not produce harmful emissions that contribute to environmental damage. Another important advantage is that cycling encourages a healthier lifestyle. Regular physical activity such as cycling can improve people's fitness levels, reduce the risk of certain health problems, and promote a more active way of living.\n\nHowever, there are also several concerns related to limiting cars and encouraging cycling. One major issue is that\n\ndeveloping proper cycling infrastructure may be expensive for cities. Governments may need to invest significant financial resources in building safe bike lanes, parking areas, and other facilities for cyclists. Furthermore, not all people can cycle due to factors such as age, health conditions, or long commuting distances. For many individuals, especially those who travel far for work or have physical limitations, cycling may not be a practical option. Finally, limiting cars may cause inconvenience for commuters and businesses that depend on quick and flexible transportation for their daily activities."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t5","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":5,"p11":[{"q":"Do you have a computer?","a":"Actually, I rely on a laptop quite heavily in my daily life. Most of my studying, research, and communication happens through it, so it has become an essential tool for me. Whether I am preparing materials, searching for information, or simply organizing my tasks, my computer makes everything far more efficient. From time to time, I also use it to relax by watching videos or reading interesting articles online."},{"q":"Tell me about your hometown. If I had to describe my hometown in a few words, I would say it is energetic and constantly evolving. Over the years, it has developed significantly, with new buildings, cafés, and public spaces appearing all the time. At the same time, it has managed to","a":"preserve its cultural identity and traditions. What I appreciate most, however, is the sense of community, because people tend to be friendly and supportive toward one another."},{"q":"What do you do with your friends?","a":"Spending time with my friends usually involves simple but enjoyable activities. Quite often, we meet somewhere in the city just to talk and catch up with each other. On other occasions, we might go for a walk, play sports, or watch a film together. What matters most is not the activity itself but the opportunity to relax, share ideas, and strengthen our friendships."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t5_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t5_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"From what I can tell, the two pictures illustrate different ways people relax in their free time. In one of them, several individuals are gathered around a table playing a board game. This type of activity usually involves discussion, decision-making, and sometimes a bit of friendly competition. Because of that, it tends to be quite social and mentally stimulating. By contrast, the other image shows people watching television. Instead of interacting with each other, they are mainly focused on the screen. Watching TV is typically a more passive form of entertainment, but it can still be enjoyable, especially when people want to relax after a long or stressful day."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: playing board games or watching TV?","a":"If I had to choose, I would probably go with board games. What makes them appealing is the interaction they create between people. When playing a board game, you usually have to think strategically and communicate with others, which\n\nmakes the experience more dynamic. That being said, television certainly has its advantages as well. After a tiring day, simply sitting down and watching a good film or an interesting series can be a very relaxing way to unwind."},{"q":"Do you think people today spend too much time watching TV?","a":"To a certain extent, yes. With the huge amount of digital content available today, many people find themselves spending long hours in front of screens. Streaming platforms, TV shows, and online videos are extremely accessible, which can easily turn watching TV into a daily habit. Even so, I do not think television is necessarily harmful if it is consumed in moderation. The key is to maintain a balance between screen-based entertainment and other activities such as socializing or physical exercise."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t5_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a cultural tradition that is important in your country.","Why do people value this tradition?","Do you think it will continue to be important in the future?"],"a":"Why or why not? One cultural tradition that is very important in my country is celebrating Navruz, which marks the beginning of spring and the new year. During this time, families prepare traditional food, visit relatives, and take part in community celebrations. People often clean their homes, cook special dishes such as sumalak, and spend time together outdoors. The atmosphere during Navruz is usually very joyful because it symbolizes renewal, hope, and a fresh start for everyone. People value this tradition because it brings families and communities closer together. It is not only a celebration but also a way of preserving cultural identity and remembering long-\n\nstanding customs. Many people believe that traditions like Navruz help younger generations understand their heritage and respect the history of their country. It also creates an opportunity for people to relax, meet relatives, and enjoy time with loved ones. I believe this tradition will continue to be important in the future. Even though modern lifestyles are changing rapidly, cultural traditions often remain strong because they connect people with their roots. Younger generations still participate in these celebrations, and governments and communities also support them. For these reasons, I think this tradition will remain meaningful for many years."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"A university degree is not necessary for success","for":["many successful entrepreneurs and professionals do not have university degrees","practical skills and experience can be more valuable than academic knowledge","alternative education paths such as vocational training or online courses are growing"],"against":["many careers require formal qualifications and academic training","universities provide structured learning and professional networks","a degree often increases employment opportunities and career stability"],"a":"The idea that a university degree is not necessary for success has become increasingly discussed as different career paths continue to develop in modern society.\n\nOne argument supporting this view is that many successful entrepreneurs and professionals have achieved remarkable success without completing a university degree. Their achievements suggest that determination, creativity, and practical abilities can sometimes be more important than formal education. In addition, practical skills and real-world experience can often be more valuable than purely academic knowledge, particularly in fields that require problem-solving, innovation, or technical abilities. Another important point is that alternative education paths are becoming more popular and accessible. Options such as vocational training programs, professional\n\ncertifications, and online courses allow individuals to develop useful skills without following a traditional university route.\n\nHowever, there are also strong arguments suggesting that a university degree still plays an important role in achieving success. Many careers, such as medicine, engineering, and law, require formal qualifications and specialized academic training that can only be obtained through higher education institutions. Furthermore, universities provide structured learning environments where students can gain deep theoretical knowledge and develop critical thinking skills. They also offer valuable professional networks, allowing students to connect with professors, classmates, and potential employers. Finally, having a university degree often increases employment opportunities and can contribute to greater career stability in the long term."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t6","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":6,"p11":[{"q":"Do you work or are you a student?","a":"At the moment, I'm a student, and most of my time is devoted to studying and improving my skills. I usually attend classes during the day and spend additional time reviewing materials or preparing for exams. Although it can sometimes be demanding, I find it quite rewarding because I feel that I'm gradually developing my knowledge and abilities."},{"q":"Who is your favorite singer?","a":"My favorite singer is someone whose music is both meaningful and inspiring. I really appreciate artists who have a unique voice and strong stage presence. Their songs often have deep lyrics and memorable melodies, which make them enjoyable to listen to repeatedly. Music like this can easily influence my mood and help me relax."},{"q":"What do you usually do at the weekends?","a":"At the weekends, I usually try to relax and recharge after a busy week. Sometimes I spend time with friends or family, and other times I prefer quieter activities like reading, watching films, or going for a walk. Weekends are also a good opportunity for me to catch up on things I didn't have time to do during the week."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t6_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t6_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"At first glance, the images seem to represent two different ways people enjoy their meals. One of the pictures shows people dining in a restaurant. The setting looks quite social, and it seems like they are enjoying a variety of dishes that were prepared by professional chefs. Eating out often creates a pleasant atmosphere because people can relax and focus on conversation rather than cooking.\n\nThe other picture, on the other hand, appears to show someone eating at home. In this case, the food is likely homemade and prepared in a personal kitchen. This type of meal is usually more private and comfortable. Many people also prefer eating at home because it allows them to control the ingredients and prepare healthier food. Overall, the pictures highlight the contrast between restaurant dining and home cooking."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: eating out or eating at home?","a":"If I were asked to choose, I would probably say that eating at home is a better option for everyday life. Preparing meals at home is usually more affordable and healthier since people can select fresh ingredients and cook according to their preferences. Nevertheless, dining out can also be enjoyable from time to time. It gives people the opportunity to try new cuisines and spend quality time with friends or family in a pleasant environment."},{"q":"Do you think people today eat out more often than in the past?","a":"In many cases, yes. Compared with the past, people today seem to eat out much more frequently. One of the main reasons is that modern lifestyles are quite fast-paced, so individuals often prefer quick and convenient meal options. Another contributing factor is the growth of restaurants and food delivery services, which have made prepared meals extremely accessible. As a result, dining out has become a common part of everyday life for many people."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t6_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a time when time seemed to pass very quickly or very slowly.","What were you doing during that moment?","Why do you think time felt different in that situation?"],"a":"One time when time seemed to pass very quickly was during a meeting with some close friends whom I had not seen for a long time. We decided to meet in a small café and simply spend some time talking and catching up with each other. At first, we thought we would only stay there for about an hour, but the conversation became so interesting and enjoyable that we completely lost track of time. We talked about many different topics, including our studies, future plans, and funny memories from the past. During that moment, we were mainly sharing stories and listening to each other's experiences. Everyone had something interesting to say, and the atmosphere was very relaxed and friendly. Because we were fully engaged in the conversation, none of us paid attention to the clock. By the time we realized\n\nhow late it had become, several hours had already passed, which was quite surprising for all of us. I think time felt different in that situation because we were genuinely enjoying ourselves and were completely focused on the moment. When people are interested in what they are doing and feel comfortable with the people around them, they often forget about time completely. On the other hand, when someone is bored or uncomfortable, time tends to feel very slow. This experience reminded me that meaningful conversations and positive emotions can make time seem to move much faster than we expect."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"The government should ban gambling","for":["reduces gambling addiction and protects vulnerable people","prevents financial problems and family conflicts caused by gambling","decreases crime related to illegal betting and debt"],"against":["banning gambling may increase illegal underground gambling","governments would lose significant tax revenue from the gambling industry","people should have the freedom to decide how they spend their money"],"a":"The question of whether the government should ban gambling is widely debated because it involves both social protection and personal freedom.\n\nOne argument in favour of banning gambling is that such a policy could reduce gambling addiction and protect vulnerable people. Many individuals develop serious problems when they become addicted to betting activities, which can negatively affect their mental health and daily lives. In addition, prohibiting gambling could prevent financial problems and family conflicts that often arise when people lose large amounts of money. Another significant benefit is that a ban could decrease crime related to illegal betting and debt, since some individuals may resort to dishonest or illegal actions in order to recover their losses or repay borrowed money.\n\nOn the other hand, banning gambling may also create several challenges. One major concern is that strict prohibition\n\ncould lead to the growth of illegal underground gambling activities that are much harder for authorities to control. Furthermore, governments would lose significant tax revenue that currently comes from the gambling industry, which is often used to fund public services and social programs. Finally, some people argue that individuals should have the freedom to decide how they spend their money, and that responsible adults should be allowed to participate in gambling if they choose to do so."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t7","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":7,"p11":[{"q":"What is your favorite food?","a":"One of my favorite foods is a traditional dish that is both flavorful and satisfying. I enjoy it because it combines different ingredients and spices, which create a rich taste. I usually eat it with my family, especially during special occasions. For me, food like this is not only delicious but also connected with culture and family traditions."},{"q":"How do you use the internet?","a":"I use the internet mainly for learning and communication. For example, I often search for useful information, watch educational videos, or read articles about different topics. I also use it to stay in touch with friends and share ideas. In my opinion, the internet is an essential tool because it provides quick access to knowledge."},{"q":"What famous footballer do you know?","a":"One famous footballer that I know is Cristiano Ronaldo. He is widely recognized for his incredible skills, discipline, and achievements in football. What I admire most about him is his dedication and hard work, which helped him become one of the best players in the world. His career is very inspiring for many young athletes."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t7_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t7_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"These pictures seem to illustrate two different types of markets. In one image, there is likely a large market or supermarket where many products are displayed in an organized way. Such places usually offer a wide range of goods, including food, clothes, and household items. Customers can conveniently find almost everything they need in one location.In contrast, the other picture probably shows a small outdoor market. These markets are often set up in open spaces where local sellers offer fresh fruits, vegetables, and handmade products. The atmosphere in outdoor markets tends to be more lively and traditional because buyers can interact directly with the sellers. Overall, the images highlight the difference between modern, organized shopping environments and more traditional marketplaces."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: shopping in big markets or small outdoor markets?","a":"Personally, I tend to prefer small outdoor markets. One reason is that the products there are often fresher, especially when it comes to fruits and vegetables. In addition, shopping in these markets feels more authentic because people can\n\ncommunicate directly with local sellers. However, large markets also have their advantages. They usually provide a wider variety of products and a more comfortable shopping environment."},{"q":"Do you think big markets will replace small outdoor markets in the future?","a":"Although large supermarkets are becoming increasingly common, I do not think small outdoor markets will disappear completely. Many people still appreciate buying fresh products directly from local farmers and vendors. Furthermore, outdoor markets often represent cultural traditions and community life. For this reason, both types of markets will likely continue to exist and serve different purposes."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t7_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a time when you had to control yourself.","What made the situation difficult for you?","How did you manage to control your emotions or reactions?"],"a":"One situation when I had to control myself happened during a disagreement with someone about an important topic. We were discussing an issue that both of us cared about deeply, and at some point the conversation became quite intense. I started to feel frustrated because the other person did not seem to understand my perspective. For a moment, I felt the urge to respond emotionally and argue more strongly to defend my opinion. The situation was difficult because strong emotions can easily influence how people react. When someone feels misunderstood, it is natural to become defensive or even angry. However, I knew that reacting impulsively could make the situation worse and possibly damage our relationship. Instead\n\nof immediately responding, I tried to pause for a moment and think carefully about my words. I managed to control my emotions by taking a deep breath and focusing on listening rather than reacting. By doing this, I was able to calm down and respond in a more reasonable way. Eventually, the conversation became more balanced and respectful, and we were able to understand each other's opinions better. This experience taught me that self-control and patience are very important when dealing with disagreements."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"The government should limit how much people earn","for":["reduces income inequality between the rich and the poor","allows governments to redistribute wealth for public services like healthcare and education","prevents excessive concentration of wealth and economic power"],"against":["may reduce motivation and ambition to work hard or innovate","could discourage entrepreneurship and investment","wealthy individuals and businesses might move to countries with fewer financial restrictions"],"a":"The idea that the government should limit how much people earn is a controversial topic that raises questions about fairness, economic motivation, and financial freedom.\n\nOne argument in favour of limiting income is that it could reduce income inequality between the rich and the poor. In many countries, wealth is heavily concentrated among a small group of individuals, which can create social and economic imbalance. By introducing limits on extremely high earnings, governments may be able to reduce this gap and create a more equal distribution of wealth. In addition, such policies would allow governments to redistribute financial resources and invest more in essential public services such as healthcare and education. Another important benefit is that income limits could prevent the excessive concentration of wealth and economic power, which sometimes allows a small number of individuals or corporations to influence economic and political decisions.\n\nOn the other hand, there are also strong arguments against limiting how much people can earn. One major concern is that such restrictions may reduce motivation and ambition to work hard or develop innovative ideas. High financial rewards often encourage people to pursue ambitious goals and contribute to economic progress. Furthermore, limiting income could discourage entrepreneurship and investment because individuals might feel that their potential rewards are restricted. Finally, wealthy individuals and businesses might move their activities to countries with fewer financial regulations, which could result in the loss of talent, investment, and economic growth for the country that imposes such limits."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t8","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":8,"p11":[{"q":"What is your favourite TV show?","a":"My favourite TV show is usually something educational or informative. I enjoy programs that explore real-life topics such as science, history, or culture. These kinds of shows are not only entertaining but also very useful because they help me learn new things and broaden my understanding of the world."},{"q":"Do you like animals?","a":"Yes, I do. I think animals are fascinating and important for the natural balance of the environment. Many people enjoy keeping pets because animals can be loyal companions and bring a lot of happiness. Personally, I find it relaxing to spend time with animals or simply observe them in nature."},{"q":"How often do you read?","a":"I try to read quite regularly, usually several times a week. Reading is a great way to expand my knowledge and improve my language skills. I often read articles, books, or online materials about different topics. In my opinion, reading is one of the most effective ways to develop critical thinking and vocabulary."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t8_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t8_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"At first sight, the pictures seem to present two different ways of getting around. In one of them, a person is using a private car to travel. Driving a car is often considered convenient because it allows people to reach their destination quickly and comfortably. It is especially useful when someone needs to travel long distances or carry heavy items. The other picture shows a person walking. Unlike driving, walking is a simple and environmentally friendly way of moving from one place to another. It does not require fuel or special equipment, and it also helps people stay physically active. Overall, the images contrast a fast and comfortable mode of transport with a slower but healthier alternative."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: using a private car or walking?","a":"If the distance is short, I would definitely prefer walking. It is a healthy habit and a great way to stay active. Walking also allows people to enjoy their surroundings and reduce stress. However, when the destination is far away or when time is\n\nlimited, using a private car becomes much more practical. It saves time and makes traveling more comfortable."},{"q":"Do you think people rely too much on private cars today?","a":"To some extent, yes. Many people depend heavily on private cars because they are fast and convenient. In large cities, however, this can create serious problems such as traffic congestion and air pollution. As a result, many governments are encouraging people to walk more or use public transportation. Promoting healthier and more sustainable ways of traveling could improve both environmental conditions and public health."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t8_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a time when you had to be patient after experiencing a failure.","Why was patience important in that situation?","What did this experience teach you about dealing with failure?"],"a":"One time when I had to be patient after experiencing failure was when I did not achieve the result I expected in an important exam. I had spent quite a long time preparing for it, so naturally I hoped to perform very well. When I finally saw the result, I felt disappointed and frustrated because it did not reflect the amount of effort I had put into my preparation. At that moment, it would have been easy to become discouraged or even lose motivation completely. However, I realized that success often requires persistence and patience. Instead of focusing only on the disappointment, I tried to analyze what went wrong. I looked at my preparation methods and identified areas where I could improve, such as time management and practicing more difficult questions. This experience taught me several important lessons about dealing with failure. First, failure does not necessarily mean the end of progress; sometimes it simply shows that we need to change our approach. Second, patience allows people to learn from their mistakes and improve gradually. As a result of this experience, I became more determined to continue working toward my goals and to see challenges as opportunities for growth."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Handwriting is becoming less important in modern education","for":["digital devices have replaced many traditional writing tasks","typing is faster and more efficient for academic and professional work","most communication today happens through digital platforms"],"against":["handwriting helps improve memory and learning retention","it develops fine motor skills and cognitive development","handwritten notes can help students understand information more deeply"],"a":"The idea that handwriting is becoming less important in modern education is often discussed as technology continues to change the way students learn and communicate.\n\nOne argument supporting this view is that digital devices have replaced many traditional writing tasks in schools and universities. Students now frequently use laptops, tablets, or smartphones to complete assignments, take notes, and access learning materials. In addition, typing is generally faster and more efficient than handwriting, especially when students need to produce long pieces of academic work or professional documents. Another important factor is that most communication today takes place through digital platforms such as emails, messaging applications, and online learning systems, which further reduces the need for handwritten communication.\n\nHowever, there are also strong reasons why handwriting should still remain an important part of education. Research suggests that handwriting can help improve memory and learning retention because the physical process of writing encourages deeper mental engagement with the material. Furthermore, practicing handwriting develops fine motor skills and supports cognitive development, particularly for younger students who are still developing coordination and concentration. Another advantage is that handwritten notes often help students understand and organize information more effectively, as writing by hand usually requires them to process ideas more carefully rather than simply typing them quickly."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t9","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":9,"p11":[{"q":"When do you usually get up?","a":"I usually get up quite early in the morning, especially on weekdays. Waking up early helps me start the day in a calm and organized way. After getting up, I normally have breakfast and prepare for the day ahead. I believe having a regular routine in the morning makes the whole day more productive."},{"q":"What do you do to stay healthy?","a":"To stay healthy, I try to maintain a balanced lifestyle. I usually do some physical activities such as walking or playing sports, and I also try to eat nutritious food. In addition, I make sure to get enough rest because sleep is essential for both physical and mental health."},{"q":"Can you describe your room?","a":"My room is quite simple but very comfortable. It has a bed, a desk where I usually study or work, and a small bookshelf. I prefer keeping my room tidy because it helps me concentrate better. Overall, it's a quiet and pleasant place where I can relax and focus on my tasks."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t9_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t9_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"These images seem to contrast two very different types of food. One picture likely shows healthy food such as fruits, vegetables, and other nutritious meals. These foods are usually fresh and contain essential vitamins and nutrients that support a healthy lifestyle. People often choose this type of food when they want to maintain good health and balanced nutrition. The other picture probably represents junk food, which might include items like burgers, fries, or sugary snacks. This type of food is usually very tasty and convenient, but it often contains large amounts of fat, sugar, and salt. As a result, eating too much junk food may negatively affect a person's health. Overall, the pictures highlight the contrast between nutritious meals and less healthy fast food."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: healthy food or junk food?","a":"If I had to choose, I would definitely prefer healthy food. One reason is that it provides the body with important nutrients and helps maintain long-term health. Eating balanced meals\n\ncan improve energy levels and overall well-being. That being said, junk food can still be enjoyable from time to time. Many people occasionally eat fast food because it is quick, convenient, and often very flavorful."},{"q":"Do you think people today eat too much junk food?","a":"In many cases, yes. Modern lifestyles are often very busy, so people tend to choose fast and convenient meals instead of cooking at home. Junk food is also widely available and heavily advertised, which encourages frequent consumption.\n\nHowever, awareness about healthy eating is gradually increasing. Many people are beginning to pay more attention to their diets and try to include more nutritious foods in their daily meals."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t9_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a critical decision you had to make.","What factors did you consider before making this decision?","What was the result of your decision, and how did it affect you?"],"a":"One critical decision I had to make was choosing an important direction for my future studies. At that time, I had several different options, and each of them offered different opportunities and challenges. Because this decision could influence my long-term goals and career path, I wanted to think about it very carefully before making a final choice. Before deciding, I considered a variety of factors. For example, I thought about my personal interests, my strengths, and the kind of work I might want to do in the future. I also tried to evaluate the potential opportunities each option could provide in terms of education and professional development. In addition, I asked for advice from people I trusted, such as\n\nteachers, friends, and family members. Their perspectives helped me see the situation from different angles. In the end, the decision turned out to be very positive for me. It gave me a clearer sense of direction and helped me focus more seriously on my goals. Although making such a decision was not easy, the process taught me the importance of careful thinking and responsibility. It also helped me become more confident in making important choices about my future."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Schools should start later in the morning","for":["students can get enough sleep and feel more rested","better concentration and academic performance during lessons","improved mental health and reduced stress for students"],"against":["later schedules may conflict with parents' work schedules","school activities and sports may finish much later in the day","transportation and school logistics could become more complicated"],"a":"The idea that schools should start later in the morning has received increasing attention in recent years, particularly because of growing concerns about students' health and academic performance.\n\nOne strong argument in favor of later school start times is related to sleep. Many teenagers struggle to get enough rest because their biological sleep patterns tend to shift during adolescence. If schools begin very early in the morning, students may arrive feeling tired and unable to concentrate properly.\n\nAnother benefit is that students may perform better academically when they are well-rested. When individuals have sufficient sleep, their attention span, memory, and overall cognitive performance tend to improve. As a result, lessons may become more productive and effective.\n\nHowever, changing school schedules may also create certain difficulties. For example, later start times could conflict\n\nwith parents' working hours, which might make it harder for families to manage daily routines.\n\nIn addition, extracurricular activities such as sports or clubs could end later in the evening, leaving students with less time for homework or relaxation.\n\nOverall, although starting school later could improve students' health and academic focus, schools would need to carefully consider the practical challenges before implementing such changes."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t10","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":10,"p11":[{"q":"Tell me about your first teacher. When I think back to my early school years, the person who immediately comes to mind is my first teacher. She was extremely patient and supportive, especially because everything at school felt completely new to us at that time.","a":"Instead of simply teaching subjects like reading or mathematics, she also helped us develop confidence and curiosity. Thanks to her encouraging attitude, many of us started to enjoy learning from a very young age."},{"q":"Can you tell me about your typical day?","a":"My daily routine usually begins fairly early in the morning. After getting ready, I normally focus on my main responsibilities, which mostly involve studying and preparing materials. During the day, I spend time working, reading, or organizing different tasks. In the evening, I try to relax a little by talking with friends, going for a walk, or watching something interesting. Overall, my day is usually quite productive but also balanced."},{"q":"Do you have a pet?","a":"At the moment, I do not have a pet, although I have always liked animals. Keeping a pet can be a wonderful experience because animals often bring companionship and\n\npositive emotions into people's lives. However, having a pet also requires responsibility, including proper care, feeding, and regular attention. For that reason, I would probably consider getting one only when Ihave enough time to look after it properly."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t10_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t10_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"These pictures seem to represent two different working situations. In one image, a person is working alone, possibly focusing on a task such as studying, writing, or using a computer. Working individually often allows people to concentrate better because there are fewer distractions. It can also give someone more independence when making decisions. In the other picture, several people appear to be working together as a group. They might be discussing ideas, planning a project, or solving a problem collaboratively. Group work usually involves communication and teamwork, which can help people share different perspectives. Overall, the images highlight the difference between individual work and collaborative effort."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: working alone or working in a group?","a":"If I were given the choice, I would probably lean toward working independently, especially when the task requires deep concentration. Being on my own allows me to organize my\n\nideas clearly and proceed at a pace that suits me. That being said, group work certainly has its strengths. When several people collaborate, they can combine their skills and knowledge, which often leads to more creative and effective outcomes."},{"q":"Do you think teamwork is important in the workplace?","a":"Without a doubt, teamwork plays a crucial role in most workplaces today. Many projects are simply too complex for one person to handle alone, so cooperation becomes essential. Moreover, working in teams encourages people to exchange knowledge and support one another when difficulties arise. As a result, organizations that promote strong teamwork often achieve better productivity and overall success."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t10_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a time when someone gave you useful advice.","Who gave you this advice and why did they give it to you?","How did this advice influence your decisions or behavior?"],"a":"One time when someone gave me very useful advice was during an important period of my studies. I was feeling quite stressed because I had many tasks to complete and several goals that I wanted to achieve. At that time, I sometimes tried to do too many things at once, which made me feel overwhelmed and less productive than I expected. The advice was given to me by one of my teachers. They noticed that I was putting a lot of pressure on myself and trying to finish everything quickly. They told me that instead of\n\nrushing, I should focus on working consistently and improving step by step. Their main advice was to concentrate on small daily progress rather than worrying about big results immediately. This advice influenced my behavior quite a lot. After hearing it, I started organizing my work more carefully and creating a more realistic schedule. Instead of stressing about the final outcome, I began focusing on completing smaller tasks every day. Over time, I noticed that this approach made me feel more confident and productive. It also taught me that steady effort is often more effective than trying to achieve everything at once."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Transportation should be free for everyone","for":["increases accessibility and mobility for low-income citizens","reduces traffic congestion because more people use public transport","helps decrease air pollution and environmental damage"],"against":["governments may struggle to cover the high financial costs","public transport systems could become overcrowded","free services might reduce efficiency and service quality"],"a":"The idea that transportation should be free for everyone is widely discussed as governments try to improve mobility and reduce environmental problems.\n\nOne argument in favour of free transportation is that it would increase accessibility and mobility for low-income citizens. Many people cannot afford daily transport costs, and free public transport would allow them to travel more easily for work, education, and other important activities. In addition, if transportation were free, more people might choose public transport instead of private cars, which could reduce traffic congestion in busy cities. Another important advantage is that increased use of public transport could help decrease air pollution and environmental damage because fewer private vehicles would be on the roads.\n\nHowever, there are also several arguments against making transportation completely free. One major concern is that governments may struggle to cover the high financial costs\n\nof operating and maintaining public transport systems. Without ticket revenue, authorities would need to rely heavily on public funds, which could create pressure on national budgets. Furthermore, free transport might lead to overcrowding, especially during peak hours, since a larger number of people would use buses and trains. Finally, some critics argue that completely free services could reduce efficiency and service quality, as transport providers might have fewer financial incentives to maintain high standards."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t11","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":11,"p11":[{"q":"Do you like watching TV?","a":"Yes, I do, although I don't watch TV very often. When I have some free time, I usually prefer watching documentaries or educational programs because they help me learn something new. In my opinion, TV can be both entertaining and informative if you choose the right type of content."},{"q":"What is a famous food in your country?","a":"One famous food in my country is a traditional dish that many people enjoy during family gatherings or special occasions. It is usually prepared with rice, meat, and different spices, which create a rich and distinctive flavor. This dish is very popular and is often considered an important part of our cultural traditions."},{"q":"Do you usually listen to music?","a":"Yes, I listen to music quite regularly. I often listen to it when I'm studying, relaxing, or traveling somewhere. Music helps me improve my mood and feel more motivated. I particularly enjoy calm or meaningful songs because they create a relaxing atmosphere."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t11_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t11_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"From what I can observe, the images illustrate two different learning environments. One of them appears to show a traditional classroom where students are physically present and listening to a teacher. In such settings, learners usually interact directly with the instructor and their classmates, which can make the learning process more engaging and dynamic.\n\nThe other image seems to represent online learning, where students attend lessons through digital platforms using computers or tablets. In this case, education takes place remotely, which allows learners to study from almost anywhere. Overall, the pictures highlight the contrast between face-to-face education and modern digital learning."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: classroom learning or online learning?","a":"If I had to make a choice, I would probably prefer classroom learning. Being physically present in a class makes it easier to concentrate and participate in discussions. It also allows students to receive immediate feedback from their\n\nteachers. That said, online learning can be extremely convenient. It offers flexibility and allows people to access educational materials from any location."},{"q":"Do you think online education will become more popular in the future?","a":"It seems very likely that online education will continue to grow in popularity. Technological advancements have made digital learning platforms more accessible and effective than before. However, I do not think traditional classrooms will disappear completely. Many students still benefit from direct interaction with teachers and classmates, which is something that online education cannot always fully replicate."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t11_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a moment when you felt truly free.","What made that moment special for you?","How did this experience influence your thoughts or feelings afterward?"],"a":"One moment when I felt truly free happened after I completed a very demanding period of study. For several weeks, I had been preparing for important exams and spending most of my time studying and reviewing materials. Because of this, my daily routine was quite strict and focused mainly on work. When the exams were finally finished, I decided to go for a long walk outside to relax. The weather was calm, the air was fresh, and the environment felt very peaceful. As I walked slowly and looked around, I realized that I no longer had any immediate responsibilities or deadlines. At that moment, I felt a strong sense of relief and freedom. What made that moment special was the realization that I could simply enjoy the present without worrying about tasks or pressure. This experience also influenced my thoughts afterward because it reminded me how important it is to create balance in life. Since then, I have tried to give myself occasional breaks and spend time doing relaxing activities so that I can stay motivated and mentally refreshed."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Keeping domestic pets is beneficial for people","for":["pets provide emotional support and companionship","they can reduce stress and improve mental well-being","taking care of pets teaches responsibility and empathy"],"against":["keeping pets requires time, money, and long-term commitment","some pets may cause allergies or health problems","irresponsible pet ownership can lead to animal neglect"],"a":"The idea that keeping domestic pets is beneficial for people is often discussed because pets can influence both emotional well-being and daily responsibilities.\n\nOne argument in favour of keeping pets is that they provide emotional support and companionship. Many people develop strong bonds with their pets, which can help reduce feelings of loneliness and provide comfort during difficult times. In addition, pets can reduce stress and improve mental well-being. Spending time with animals, such as walking a dog or simply interacting with a pet, can help people relax and improve their mood. Another advantage is that taking care of pets teaches responsibility and empathy. Owners must regularly feed, care for, and pay attention to their animals, which can help them develop discipline and a deeper understanding of others' needs.\n\nHowever, there are also several challenges related to keeping domestic pets. One major concern is that pets require time, money, and long-term commitment. Owners must provide\n\nfood, medical care, and regular attention, which may be difficult for people with busy lifestyles. Furthermore, some pets may cause allergies or health problems, especially for individuals who are sensitive to animal hair or certain bacteria. Finally, irresponsible pet ownership can lead to animal neglect if people are not prepared to ca"},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t12","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":12,"p11":[{"q":"Can you describe your family?","a":"My family is quite close and supportive. We usually try to spend time together whenever we have the opportunity. Each member of my family has a different personality, but we always respect and help each other. I think having a supportive family is very important because it gives people motivation and confidence in life."},{"q":"What place would you like to visit?","a":"One place I would really like to visit is a country with a rich culture and beautiful landscapes. I'm particularly interested in exploring historical landmarks and experiencing different traditions. Traveling to such places would allow me to broaden my perspective and learn more about the world."},{"q":"What do you usually eat for breakfast?","a":"For breakfast, I usually prefer something simple but nutritious. Most of the time, I have eggs, bread, and a cup of tea or coffee. Sometimes I also eat fruit because it helps me feel more energetic in the morning. I believe breakfast is important because it provides energy for the rest of the day."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t12_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t12_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"From what I can observe, the pictures illustrate two different ways of getting around in a city. One of them appears to show people using public transportation, such as a bus, metro, or train. Public transport is commonly used in urban areas because it allows many passengers to travel at the same time. It is often considered a practical option for commuting, especially during busy hours.\n\nThe other image seems to present someone riding a bicycle. Cycling is a more active and environmentally friendly way of traveling. People who cycle not only move from one place to another but also get some physical exercise. Taken together, the pictures show the contrast between shared transportation and a more individual, eco-friendly method of travel."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: using public transport or cycling?","a":"Personally, I would lean toward cycling whenever the distance is not too long. Riding a bicycle is both healthy and refreshing because it allows people to stay physically active while commuting. However, public transport can be much more convenient when traveling longer distances or when the weather conditions are not favorable."},{"q":"Do you think more people will start cycling in the future?","a":"There is a strong possibility that cycling will become more popular in the future. Many cities are already encouraging this habit by building special bicycle lanes and promoting environmentally friendly transportation. In addition, as people become more concerned about their health and the environment, cycling may become an attractive alternative to cars and other motorized vehicles."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t12_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about the most significant challenge you have faced.","Why was this challenge particularly difficult for you?","How did you manage to overcome it, and what did you learn from it?"],"a":"One of the most significant challenges I have faced was working toward an important academic goal that required a great deal of effort and discipline. During that time, I had to study many complicated topics and spend long hours practicing and reviewing information. At the same time, I also had other responsibilities that needed my attention. This challenge was particularly difficult because it required both mental concentration and emotional resilience. Sometimes I felt tired or discouraged, especially when progress seemed slower than I expected. There were moments when I doubted whether I would be able to achieve the result I wanted. In\n\naddition, balancing different tasks at the same time made the situation even more demanding. I managed to overcome this challenge mainly through persistence and better organization. I started creating a clear schedule for my daily activities and setting small, achievable goals for each day. Gradually, I began to see improvement in my performance, which gave me more motivation to continue working. This experience taught me that determination, patience, and consistent effort are essential when dealing with difficult situations, and that even very challenging goals can be achieved step by step."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Zoos should be banned worldwide","for":["keeping animals in captivity may harm their natural behavior","zoos often limit animals' freedom and natural habitats","animals may suffer from stress and poor living conditions"],"against":["zoos help protect endangered species through conservation programs","they provide educational opportunities for the public","zoos support scientific research about animal behavior and biology"],"a":"The idea that zoos should be banned worldwide is widely debated because it raises important questions about animal welfare, conservation, and education.\n\nOne argument in favour of banning zoos is that keeping animals in captivity may harm their natural behavior. Many wild animals are used to living in large natural habitats where they can hunt, explore, and interact freely with other animals. In zoos, however, their movement and activities are often restricted. In addition, zoos frequently limit animals' freedom and natural habitats, which may prevent them from behaving as they normally would in the wild. Another concern is that animals may suffer from stress and poor living conditions, particularly when enclosures are small or do not properly replicate their natural environments.\n\nOn the other hand, there are also strong arguments against banning zoos completely. One important reason is that many zoos help protect endangered species through conservation programs. Some animals that are close to extinction can be bred and protected in controlled environments. Furthermore, zoos provide\n\neducational opportunities for the public, especially for children who can learn about wildlife and environmental protection. Finally, zoos support scientific research about animal behavior and biology, which can help scientists better understand different species and develop more effective strategies for protecting them in the wild."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t13","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":13,"p11":[{"q":"What is a famous food in your country?","a":"One of the most famous foods in my country is a traditional dish made with rice, meat, and vegetables. It is usually prepared during family gatherings and special celebrations. People enjoy it because it has a rich flavor and represents an important part of our national cuisine."},{"q":"Can you describe your dream house?","a":"My dream house would be quite spacious and modern. I would like it to have large windows so that there is plenty of natural light inside. It would also have a small garden where I could relax or spend time with family and friends. Overall, I imagine it as a peaceful and comfortable place to live."},{"q":"Are there many traditional clothes in your country?","a":"Yes, there are several traditional clothes in my country that reflect our culture and history. These clothes are usually worn during festivals, weddings, or other important celebrations. They often include colorful fabrics and unique patterns, which make them both beautiful and meaningful."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t13_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t13_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"At first glance, the pictures seem to portray two different ways people spend their free time. In one of the images, a person appears to be alone, focusing on a hobby such as reading, drawing, or playing a musical instrument. Activities like these often allow individuals to relax and concentrate on something they truly enjoy. Spending time alone can also help people reflect and recharge their energy. The other image likely shows a group of friends spending time together. They might be talking, laughing, or doing some kind of social activity. Hanging out with friends is usually lively and entertaining because people can share experiences and strengthen their relationships. Overall, the pictures highlight the difference between personal hobbies and social interaction."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: spending time alone or hanging out with friends?","a":"If I had to choose, I would probably say that I enjoy a balance of both. Spending time alone helps me focus on my\n\nhobbies and relax without distractions. It can be very refreshing after a busy day. On the other hand, hanging out with friends is equally important because it allows me to socialize, exchange ideas, and create enjoyable memories."},{"q":"Do you think people today spend enough time with their friends In many cases, people nowadays seem to spend less time with friends than before. Busy schedules, work responsibilities, and digital distractions often reduce opportunities for face-to-","a":"face interaction. Nevertheless, many people still make an effort to maintain their friendships by meeting occasionally or staying in touch through social media and messaging platforms."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t13_2.jpg","qs":["Tell me about a time when you forgave someone.","Why was it difficult to forgive that person?","What did this experience teach you about forgiveness?"],"a":"One time when I had to forgive someone happened after a misunderstanding between me and another person. During a conversation, something was said that I felt was unfair and slightly hurtful. At that moment, I believed that my intentions had been misunderstood, and this made me feel disappointed and somewhat frustrated. Because of this misunderstanding, the atmosphere between us became a little tense, and for a short time our communication was not as comfortable as before. Forgiving that person was not easy at first because emotions can sometimes make people focus mainly on negative feelings. For several days, I kept thinking about what had happened and replaying the conversation in my mind. I wondered whether I should have explained myself more clearly or reacted differently at that moment. However, after thinking about the situation more calmly, I realized that misunderstandings can easily happen in everyday communication, especially when people are discussing something important. Eventually, I decided that continuing to feel upset would not improve the situation. Instead, I chose to forgive the person and move forward. I tried to understand that people sometimes say things without fully realizing how their words might affect others. This experience taught me that forgiveness is an important part of maintaining healthy relationships. It also showed me that letting go of negative feelings often helps people communicate more openly and rebuild trust over time."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Everyone should include musical instruments in their life","for":["playing musical instruments improves creativity and cognitive development","music can reduce stress and improve emotional well-being","learning an instrument develops patience, discipline, and focus"],"against":["learning an instrument requires significant time and practice","musical instruments and lessons can be expensive","not everyone has a strong interest or natural ability in music"],"a":"The idea that everyone should include musical instruments in their life is often discussed because music can influence both personal development and emotional well-being.\n\nOne argument in favour of this idea is that playing musical instruments improves creativity and cognitive development. Learning music requires individuals to think carefully about rhythm, melody, and coordination, which can stimulate different areas of the brain. In addition, music can reduce stress and improve emotional well-being. Many people use music as a way to relax, express their emotions, and temporarily escape from daily pressures. Another important benefit is that learning an instrument develops patience, discipline, and focus, since mastering musical skills requires regular practice and long-term dedication.\n\nHowever, there are also several reasons why not everyone may include musical instruments in their life. One major challenge is that learning an instrument requires significant time and consistent practice, which may be difficult for people with busy schedules. Furthermore, musical instruments and lessons can be quite expensive, especially for high-quality instruments or professional training. Finally, not everyone has a strong interest or natural ability in music, and forcing individuals to learn an instrument may reduce their motivation and enjoyment."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t14","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":14,"p11":[{"q":"Can you describe a teacher you disliked?","a":"I once had a teacher who was quite strict and rarely showed patience toward students. The lessons were often stressful because students felt uncomfortable asking questions. I believe a good teacher should be supportive and encouraging, so learning can become a more positive and effective experience."},{"q":"What is your favorite meal?","a":"One of my favorite meals is a traditional dish that is both delicious and satisfying. It usually includes rice, meat, and a variety of spices that create a rich flavor. I particularly enjoy eating it with my family during special occasions because it makes the meal more enjoyable."},{"q":"Is using a mobile phone important for you?","a":"Yes, using a mobile phone is quite important for me. I use it for communication, learning, and staying updated with different information. It also helps me organize my daily\n\nactivities and stay connected with friends and family. However, I try not to rely on it too much."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t14_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t14_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"Judging from the images, they seem to represent two different methods of transportation used for traveling. One of the pictures likely shows people traveling by train. Trains are often associated with long-distance journeys and are commonly used for comfortable and scenic travel. Passengers usually have more space to move around, and they can enjoy the view during the trip. The other image appears to show people traveling by plane. Air travel is usually much faster and is often preferred for international or very long-distance trips. Although flying can sometimes be expensive, it allows passengers to reach their destination in a much shorter time. Overall, the pictures highlight the contrast between a slower but more relaxed journey and a quicker form of transportation."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: traveling by train or by plane?","a":"If I had to choose, I would probably prefer traveling by plane, especially when the destination is far away. Flying saves a significant amount of time and makes long-distance travel much more convenient. However, train journeys can also be very enjoyable. They are often more relaxing and give passengers the opportunity to admire landscapes along the way."},{"q":"Do you think air travel will become more common in the future?","a":"It seems very likely that air travel will become even more popular in the future. As globalization continues to grow, more people need to travel for business, tourism, and education. At the same time, advancements in aviation technology may make flights more efficient and accessible. As a result, flying could become the preferred option for many travelers."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t14_2.jpg","qs":["Describe a time when you worked together with your classmates.","What was the purpose of the activity or project?","How did working together help you complete the task?"],"a":"One time when I worked together with my classmates was during a group project at school. Our teacher asked us to prepare a presentation about a specific topic, and the class was divided into several small groups. Each group had to research the topic, organize the information clearly, and then present it to the rest of the class in an understandable and engaging way. The purpose of this activity was not only to learn new information but also to help students develop teamwork and communication skills. In our group, we divided the responsibilities so that everyone could contribute to the project. For example, some students focused on collecting useful information from books and online resources, while others organized the material and prepared the visual part of the presentation. A few students also practiced explaining the main ideas so that the final presentation would be clear and interesting. Working together helped us complete the project much more effectively than if we had worked individually. We were able to share different ideas and support each other whenever someone faced difficulties. If one person did not understand a certain concept, another member of the group could explain it. In addition, discussing the topic together helped us think more deeply and produce better ideas for the presentation. This experience showed me that teamwork can be very productive and that cooperation often leads to stronger and more creative results than working alone."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Video games are beneficial for children","for":["video games can improve problem-solving and strategic thinking","they develop hand-eye coordination and quick decision-making","some educational games help children learn new skills and knowledge"],"against":["excessive gaming may lead to addiction and reduced physical activity","violent games may negatively influence children's behavior","spending too much time on games can affect academic performance"],"a":"The idea that video games are beneficial for children is often discussed because gaming has become a common part of modern childhood.\n\nOne argument in favour of video games is that they can improve problem-solving and strategic thinking. Many games require players to analyze situations, plan actions, and make decisions in order to progress through different levels or challenges. In addition, video games help develop hand-eye coordination and quick decision-making, since players must react rapidly to visual information on the screen. Another advantage is that some educational games help children learn new skills and knowledge, such as mathematics, language, or logical reasoning, while still keeping the learning process engaging and enjoyable.\n\nHowever, there are also concerns about the negative effects of video games on children. One major issue is that excessive gaming may lead to addiction and reduced physical activity, which can negatively affect children's health and lifestyle. Furthermore, violent games may influence children's behavior, particularly if they are exposed to aggressive content at a young age. Finally, spending too much time playing games can affect academic performance, as children may devote less time to studying, homework, and other educational responsibilities."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t15","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":15,"p11":[{"q":"Do you play or watch any sport?","a":"Yes, I both play and watch sports occasionally. In terms of playing, I particularly enjoy football because it is both entertaining and physically beneficial. I usually play it with my friends, which makes the experience even more enjoyable. As for watching sports, I tend to follow major football tournaments or important matches since they are often exciting and highly competitive. Overall, sports are a great way to relax, stay healthy, and spend quality time with others."},{"q":"Tell me about the park in your city. There are several parks in my city where people can relax and enjoy outdoor activities. One of the most popular parks is located near the city center and attracts many visitors, especially in the evening. The park is filled with green trees and","a":"has walking paths as well as benches where people can sit and enjoy the peaceful atmosphere. Families often bring their children there, while others go for walks, exercise, or simply enjoy the fresh air. Overall, it is an important place for both recreation and social interaction."},{"q":"What do you do in the evenings?","a":"In the evenings, I usually try to relax after a long day while still doing something productive. Quite often, I spend some time studying or reviewing the material I learned earlier in the day. On other days, I prefer quieter activities such as reading, watching educational videos, or going for a short walk to clear my mind. Occasionally, I also meet friends or have conversations with family members. Overall, the evening is the time when I reflect on the day and prepare for the next one."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t15_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t15_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"At first glance, the pictures seem to depict two very different leisure activities. In one of them, people are enjoying time at the beach. The environment appears warm and sunny, and individuals might be swimming, relaxing on the sand, or engaging in various recreational activities. Spending time at the beach is often associated with relaxation and enjoying natural scenery. In contrast, the other image likely shows people playing in the snow. This activity usually takes place in cold, snowy environments where individuals participate in winter sports or simply have fun building snowmen or having snowball fights. Altogether, the pictures highlight the contrast between summer leisure activities and winter recreation."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: going to the beach or playing in the snow?","a":"If I had the option, I would probably choose going to the beach. Warm weather, fresh sea air, and the relaxing atmosphere make it a very pleasant experience. It is also a\n\ngreat opportunity to swim or spend time outdoors. That being said, winter activities in the snow can also be extremely exciting, especially when people take part in sports like skiing or snowboarding."},{"q":"Do you think people prefer summer holidays or winter holidays?","a":"In general, it seems that many people prefer summer holidays. Warm temperatures allow people to travel, swim, and participate in a wide range of outdoor activities. Nevertheless, winter holidays also have their own charm. For some individuals, snowy landscapes and winter sports create a unique and memorable travel experience."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t15_2.jpg","qs":["What is your favorite movie?","What is the movie about?","Why do you like this movie so much?"],"a":"One of my favorite movies is a film that tells an inspiring story about determination, ambition, and personal growth. The movie focuses on a main character who faces many difficulties in life but continues to pursue an important goal despite numerous obstacles. Throughout the story, the character encounters situations that test their patience, confidence, and resilience. The movie follows the character's journey as they experience both success and failure while trying to achieve their dream. Along the way, the character meets different\n\npeople who influence their decisions and provide guidance or support during challenging moments. Some situations in the film are emotionally powerful because they show how difficult it can be to stay motivated when things do not go as planned. However, the character continues to move forward and learn from each experience. I like this movie very much because it is not only entertaining but also meaningful. The story reminds viewers that success usually requires persistence, effort, and belief in oneself. In addition, the message of the movie is very motivating because it shows that challenges are a natural part of personal growth. Whenever I watch this film, it encourages me to stay determined and keep working toward my goals even when I face difficulties. For these reasons, the movie has left a very strong and lasting impression on me."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Tourism should be limited","for":["excessive tourism can damage natural environments and ecosystems","large numbers of tourists may cause overcrowding in popular destinations","limiting tourism can help preserve local culture and historical sites"],"against":["tourism generates significant income for local economies","it creates employment opportunities in many industries tourism promotes cultural exchange and international understanding"],"a":"The idea that tourism should be limited is widely debated because tourism brings both economic benefits and environmental challenges.\n\nOne argument in favour of limiting tourism is that excessive tourism can damage natural environments and ecosystems. When large numbers of visitors travel to the same destinations, they may harm wildlife habitats, increase pollution, and place pressure on natural resources. In addition, popular tourist destinations often become overcrowded, which can reduce the quality of life for local residents and make the experience less enjoyable for visitors. Another important reason is that limiting tourism can help preserve local culture and historical sites, as too many tourists may lead to the commercialization or gradual loss of traditional practices and heritage.\n\nHowever, there are also strong arguments against restricting tourism. Tourism generates significant income for\n\nlocal economies, particularly in regions that rely heavily on visitors for economic growth. It also creates employment opportunities in many industries, including hospitality, transportation, and entertainment. Furthermore, tourism promotes cultural exchange and international understanding, as people from different countries have the chance to learn about new cultures, traditions, and ways of life."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t16","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":16,"p11":[{"q":"What place do you like to visit?","a":"One place I really enjoy visiting is a quiet park or a peaceful natural area. Such places help me relax and escape from the busy city environment. I especially like walking there, enjoying the fresh air, and spending some time thinking or listening to music. In my opinion, visiting calm places like this is a great way to refresh your mind."},{"q":"Where do you go in your free time?","a":"In my free time, I usually go to places where I can relax or spend time with friends. For example, I sometimes visit a park, a café, or a quiet place where I can read or think. These places give me an opportunity to take a break from daily responsibilities and enjoy some peaceful moments."},{"q":"What time do you usually get up?","a":"I usually get up quite early in the morning, especially on weekdays. Waking up early helps me start the day in a calm and organized way. After getting up, I normally have breakfast and prepare for the day ahead. I believe that starting the day early makes it easier to stay productive."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t16_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t16_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"From what I can tell, the pictures present two very different travel experiences. One of them seems to show people camping outdoors, possibly in a forest or near a lake. Camping usually involves staying in a tent and spending time in nature. People often choose this activity because it gives them an opportunity to escape from busy city life and enjoy peaceful surroundings. The other image likely shows people staying at a hotel. In this case, travelers can enjoy a comfortable room along with various facilities such as restaurants, room service, and other services. Staying at a hotel is generally more convenient and luxurious compared to camping. Overall, the pictures highlight the contrast between a natural outdoor adventure and a comfortable indoor stay."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: camping or staying at a hotel?","a":"From my point of view, I would probably prefer staying at a hotel. One reason is that hotels usually provide a high level of comfort and convenience. After a long day of traveling, it is nice to have a comfortable bed and access to different facilities.That being said, camping can also be an exciting experience. It allows people to connect with nature and enjoy a peaceful environment away from crowded cities."},{"q":"Do you think camping will become more popular in the future?","a":"There is a strong possibility that camping will become more popular in the future. Many people today are looking for ways to relax and escape from stressful urban lifestyles. Spending time in nature can be refreshing and beneficial for both mental and physical well-being. For this reason, outdoor activities such as camping may attract more travelers in the coming years."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t16_2.jpg","qs":["Describe a situation when justice was important.","Why was fairness necessary in that situation?","What can happen when justice is not respected?"],"a":"One situation where justice was very important happened during a group activity at school. Our class was working together on a project, and every student had a specific role and responsibility. However, when the project was finished, there was some disagreement about how the work should be evaluated. A few students felt that their efforts were not being recognized fairly, while others believed that everyone had contributed equally. Fairness was necessary in that situation because the final result depended on the effort of the whole group. If some students received more credit than they deserved while others were ignored, it could create frustration and reduce motivation. Our teacher carefully reviewed the work that each student had done and tried to evaluate everyone's contribution objectively. By doing this, the teacher made sure that the final evaluation was balanced and fair for all members of the group. This situation showed me why justice is very important in everyday life. When fairness is respected, people feel valued and respected for their efforts. On the other hand, when justice is ignored, it can create conflict, disappointment, and even distrust between people. For this reason, fairness is essential for maintaining positive relationships and cooperation in any community."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Education should be free","for":["free education ensures equal access to learning opportunities","it can reduce social inequality and improve social mobility","educated populations contribute to economic and national development"],"against":["providing free education requires significant government funding","education systems may become overcrowded and less efficient","students may not fully appreciate education if it is completely free"],"a":"The idea that education should be free is frequently debated because it involves both social equality and financial responsibility.\n\nOne argument in favour of free education is that it ensures equal access to learning opportunities for people from different economic backgrounds. When education is free, students from low-income families have the same chances to study and develop their abilities as those from wealthier families. In addition, free education can reduce social inequality and improve social mobility, since individuals can achieve better careers and living conditions through learning. Another important benefit is that educated populations contribute to economic and national development. When more people receive quality education, they can develop valuable skills and knowledge that help strengthen the workforce and support long-term progress.\n\nHowever, there are also several arguments against completely free education. One major concern is that providing free education requires significant government funding, which may place heavy pressure on national budgets. Governments would need to allocate large financial resources to maintain schools, universities, and teaching staff. Furthermore, education systems might become overcrowded and less efficient if a large number of students enroll without sufficient infrastructure or resources. Finally, some people argue that students may not fully appreciate education if it is completely free, since they might take learning opportunities for granted and show less motivation to work hard."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t17","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":17,"p11":[{"q":"What is your favorite room at school?","a":"My favorite room at school is the library. I like it because it is quiet and provides a comfortable environment for studying and reading. The library also contains many useful books and learning materials. Whenever I have free time at school, I often go there to read, study, or simply relax in a peaceful atmosphere."},{"q":"What day do you dislike the most?","a":"The day I dislike the most is usually Monday. After the weekend, it can be difficult to return to a busy routine and start working again. Mondays often feel more demanding because there are many tasks and responsibilities waiting. However, once the day begins, I usually adapt and focus on my work."},{"q":"Can you describe your typical day at school?","a":"A typical day at school usually starts with morning classes, where students learn different subjects and participate in discussions. During breaks, students often talk with their friends or relax for a short time. After several lessons, the school day ends, and students either go home or continue with other activities such as studying or sports. Overall, school days are usually structured and productive."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t17_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t17_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"At first glance, the images seem to illustrate two contrasting leisure activities. In one of them, a person appears to be sitting alone in a park, possibly enjoying the quiet atmosphere and natural surroundings. Spending time alone in such a peaceful place often allows people to relax, think, or simply appreciate the environment around them.\n\nIn contrast, the other picture likely shows a large number of people watching a movie in a cinema. This setting is usually lively and full of energy because many individuals are sharing the same entertainment experience. Going to the cinema is often considered a social activity where people gather to enjoy films together. Overall, the pictures highlight the difference between solitude and group entertainment."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: sitting alone in the park or watching a movie in the cinema?","a":"To be honest, quiet places like parks appeal to me much more than crowded entertainment venues. Whenever I sit in a calm natural setting, it becomes much easier to disconnect\n\nfrom daily pressures and simply enjoy the moment. The presence of trees, fresh air, and open space often creates a sense of peace that is difficult to find elsewhere. That said, cinemas can still be enjoyable, particularly when the film is interesting and the experience is shared with close friends."},{"q":"Do you think people today spend enough time relaxing outdoors?","a":"From my perspective, outdoor relaxation has become less common in recent years. Many people are now surrounded by technology throughout the day, whether it is for work, study, or entertainment, which naturally keeps them indoors most of the time. However, there has recently been a growing interest in healthier lifestyles. Because of this shift, some individuals are starting to prioritize activities like walking in parks or spending time in natural environments."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t17_2.jpg","qs":["Describe a trip you took to a particular destination.","Why did you choose to visit this place?","What did you enjoy the most about this trip?"],"a":"One memorable trip I took was to a historical city in my country that is well known for its beautiful architecture and cultural heritage. I had heard many interesting things about this place before, especially about its ancient buildings, traditional markets, and historical monuments. Because of this, I decided to visit the city during a holiday in order to explore it personally. I chose this destination mainly because I am very interested in history and culture. I wanted to see the famous historical sites and learn more about the traditions and lifestyle of people who lived there in the past. In addition, many people had recommended the city as a peaceful and inspiring place to visit. What I enjoyed the most about the trip was walking through the old streets and observing the unique architectural style of the buildings. The atmosphere felt very special because the city seemed to combine history with everyday life. I also enjoyed trying traditional food and interacting with local people. Overall, the trip was both relaxing and educational, and it helped me appreciate the cultural richness of my country even more."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Social media should be banned for individuals under 16","for":["young teenagers may be exposed to harmful or inappropriate content","social media can negatively affect mental health and self-esteem","limiting social media may help students focus more on studies and real-life interaction"],"against":["social media can be useful for communication and learning","banning it may limit digital literacy and technological skills","strict restrictions may be difficult to enforce"],"a":"The idea that social media should be banned for individuals under the age of sixteen has become an important topic of discussion in modern society.\n\nOne argument in favour of such a ban is that young teenagers may be exposed to harmful or inappropriate content on social media platforms. Since many online spaces are difficult to control, children may encounter material that is not suitable for their age. In addition, social media can negatively affect mental health and self-esteem, especially when teenagers constantly compare themselves with others or face online criticism. Another advantage of limiting social media use is that it may help students focus more on their studies and encourage more real-life interaction with friends and family.\n\nHowever, there are also arguments against banning social media for young people. Social media can be useful for communication and learning, as students can share information, collaborate on projects, and stay connected with\n\nclassmates. Moreover, banning social media may limit the development of digital literacy and technological skills, which are increasingly important in modern education and future careers. Finally, strict restrictions may be difficult to enforce, since many teenagers might still find ways to access social media through different devices or accounts."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t18","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":18,"p11":[{"q":"Can you tell me about your hometown?","a":"My hometown is a lively place with a mix of modern buildings and traditional culture. It has several parks, schools, and markets where people spend their daily lives. What I like most about my hometown is the friendly atmosphere and the sense of community among residents. Overall, it is a comfortable place to live and grow up."},{"q":"What do you usually do with your friends?","a":"When I spend time with my friends, we usually do simple but enjoyable activities. Sometimes we go for a walk, play sports, or visit a café to talk and relax. These moments are important because they help us strengthen our friendship and take a break from our daily routines."},{"q":"Do you have a favorite hobby?","a":"Yes, I do. One of my favorite hobbies is reading because it helps me learn new ideas and improve my knowledge. I especially enjoy reading educational books or articles about different topics. In my opinion, hobbies like reading are very useful because they help people develop their thinking and creativity."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t18_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t18_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"The pictures appear to present two distinct ways people communicate. In one of them, individuals seem to be interacting online, possibly through smartphones or laptops. This type of communication usually takes place through social media, messaging apps, or video calls. One advantage of online interaction is that people can stay connected even when they are physically far apart.\n\nBy contrast, the other image likely shows people talking face-to-face. In this situation, individuals can see each other's expressions and body language, which often makes communication more natural and meaningful. Overall, the pictures highlight the difference between digital communication and direct personal interaction."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: online communication or face-to-face communication?","a":"If I had to choose, I would probably prefer face-to-face communication. Speaking directly with someone allows you to understand their emotions and reactions more\n\nclearly. It also makes conversations feel more genuine and engaging. However, online communication is extremely convenient, especially when people need to communicate quickly or when they live far away from each other."},{"q":"Do you think online communication will replace face-to-face communication in the future?","a":"Although digital communication has become extremely common, I do not think it will completely replace face-to-face interaction. Human communication often depends on emotional connection, body language, and personal presence. Online platforms will certainly continue to grow, but direct communication will remain important because it helps build stronger relationships and deeper understanding between people."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t18_2.jpg","qs":["Describe a goal that you achieved.","What motivated you to pursue this goal?","How did achieving this goal affect you?"],"a":"One important goal that I managed to achieve was improving my skills in a particular academic area that required consistent effort and discipline. At the beginning, it seemed quite challenging because I needed to dedicate a lot of time and concentration to practicing and learning new concepts. What motivated me to pursue this goal was my desire to improve myself and reach a higher level of knowledge. I knew that achieving this goal could open new opportunities for me in the future. In addition, I wanted to prove to myself that with enough effort and persistence, it is possible to overcome difficult challenges. Achieving this goal had a very positive effect on me. It increased my confidence and made me realize the value of hard work and patience. The experience also taught me that progress often happens gradually rather than suddenly. Because of this achievement, I now feel more motivated to set new goals and continue improving myself in different areas."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Nature documentaries have a positive impact on environmental","for":["documentaries educate people about wildlife and environmental issues","they raise awareness about climate change and conservation","they encourage viewers to protect nature and support environmental organizations"],"against":["watching documentaries does not always lead to real action","some documentaries may exaggerate problems for dramatic effect","people may feel temporarily emotional but quickly forget the message"],"a":"The idea that nature documentaries have a positive impact on environmental awareness is often discussed in relation to education and public attitudes toward nature.\n\nOne argument in favour of nature documentaries is that they educate people about wildlife and environmental issues. By showing different ecosystems and animal species, these films help viewers understand how nature functions and why it should be protected. In addition, documentaries raise awareness about climate change and conservation by presenting scientific information in a way that is accessible and engaging for the public. Another important benefit is that they can encourage viewers to protect nature and support environmental organizations, as many people feel inspired to take action after seeing the beauty and vulnerability of the natural world.\n\nHowever, there are also some arguments suggesting that the impact of documentaries may be limited. Watching documentaries does not always lead to real action, as many viewers simply enjoy the content without changing their behavior. Furthermore, some documentaries may exaggerate environmental problems for dramatic effect in order to capture the audience's attention. Finally, people may feel emotional while watching such films, but these feelings can disappear quickly, and the message of environmental protection may soon be forgotten."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t19","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":19,"p11":[{"q":"Why is sport important?","a":"To begin with, sport plays a crucial role in maintaining a healthy lifestyle. Regular physical exercise strengthens the body and improves mental well-being. Moreover, participating in sports allows people to develop important qualities such as discipline, perseverance, and teamwork. For these reasons, sport is considered an essential part of everyday life."},{"q":"Should everyone do sports?","a":"From my perspective, it would be beneficial for everyone to take part in some form of physical activity. It does not always have to involve intense training; even light activities like walking, jogging, or cycling can have a positive effect on health. Engaging in regular exercise helps individuals stay energetic and maintain a balanced lifestyle."},{"q":"Where is your favorite place in your home?","a":"As for my home, the place I enjoy the most is my personal room. It is a calm and comfortable space where I can focus on studying or simply relax after a busy day. I keep it organized so that the environment remains peaceful and suitable for concentration. Overall, it is the place where I feel the most comfortable."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t19_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t19_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"The images seem to present two different ways people obtain vegetables. In one of the pictures, someone appears to be growing vegetables in a garden. This activity usually involves planting seeds, watering plants, and taking care of them until they are ready to harvest. Many people enjoy gardening because it allows them to produce fresh and organic food.\n\nThe other image likely shows a person buying vegetables from a store or market. In this case, vegetables are already prepared for sale and customers can simply choose what they need. This option is often more convenient because it saves time and effort. Overall, the pictures highlight the contrast between producing food independently and purchasing it from shops."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: growing vegetables yourself or buying them from the store?","a":"If I had enough space and time, I would probably prefer growing my own vegetables. Producing food yourself can be very satisfying, and it also allows people to know exactly how their food is grown. However, buying vegetables from a store is usually much more practical for people with busy lifestyles. It provides quick access to a wide variety of fresh products."},{"q":"Do you think more people will start growing their own food in the future?","a":"There is a possibility that more people will become interested in growing their own food in the future. Many individuals today are becoming more concerned about healthy eating and sustainable living. As a result, activities like home gardening may become increasingly popular, especially among people who want fresh and natural ingredients."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t19_2.jpg","qs":["Describe a situation when you felt uncertain about something.","Why did you feel unsure in that situation?","How did you deal with this uncertainty?"],"a":"One situation when I felt uncertain happened when I had to make an important choice about something that could influence my future plans. At that moment, I had several different options, and each one seemed to have both advantages and disadvantages. I felt unsure mainly because I did not want to make the wrong decision. When a decision has long-term consequences, it is natural to think carefully about every possibility. I also considered how each option might affect my future opportunities, which made the situation even more complicated. To deal with this uncertainty, I decided to gather more information and think about the situation more calmly. I spoke\n\nwith people whose opinions I trusted and considered their advice carefully. After reflecting on all the factors, I finally made a decision that felt right for me. This experience helped me understand that uncertainty is a normal part of decision-making and that thoughtful reflection can help people make better choices."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Online privacy is more important than national security","for":["protecting personal data is essential for individual freedom and civil rights","excessive surveillance can lead to misuse of personal information","strong privacy protections help prevent abuse of power by authorities"],"against":["governments need access to certain data to prevent crime and terrorism","national security measures can protect citizens from serious threats","some level of surveillance may be necessary to maintain public safety"],"a":"The idea that online privacy is more important than national security is widely debated because it involves balancing individual rights with collective safety.\n\nOne argument in favour of prioritizing online privacy is that protecting personal data is essential for individual freedom and civil rights. When people feel that their personal information is secure, they are more likely to express their opinions and communicate freely. In addition, excessive surveillance can lead to the misuse of personal information, especially if authorities collect large amounts of data without strict regulation. Another important reason is that strong privacy protections help prevent the abuse of power by authorities, ensuring that governments cannot monitor citizens without proper justification or legal oversight.\n\nOn the other hand, there are also strong arguments supporting the importance of national security. Governments often need access to certain data in order to prevent crime and terrorism, particularly in cases that involve organized criminal networks or\n\npotential security threats. Furthermore, national security measures can protect citizens from serious dangers by allowing authorities to detect suspicious activities before they lead to harmful events. Finally, some level of surveillance may be necessary to maintain public safety, as modern threats often involve digital communication that requires monitoring to ensure effective protection of society."},"words":[]},{"id":"b3t20","book":"Speaking Book 3.0","n":20,"p11":[{"q":"Tell me about your work or study At present, I am mainly focused on my studies. My daily routine usually involves attending classes, reviewing lessons, and preparing for exams. Studying allows me to develop new skills and expand my knowledge in different areas. Although it","a":"can sometimes be challenging, I believe that education plays a vital role in shaping a successful future."},{"q":"Who is your favorite singer?","a":"When it comes to music, I admire singers who have a distinctive voice and meaningful songs. My favorite singer is someone whose music is both emotional and inspiring. Their lyrics often convey deep messages, which makes the songs more memorable. Listening to such music helps me relax and sometimes reflect on different aspects of life."},{"q":"What role does the internet play in your life?","a":"In today's world, the internet plays a significant role in my daily life. I frequently use it to search for information, watch educational content, and communicate with others. It also provides quick access to a wide range of knowledge. In many ways, the internet has become an essential tool for learning and staying connected."}],"p12":{"img":["img/sp/b3t20_12_0.jpg","img/sp/b3t20_12_1.jpg"],"qs":[{"q":"What do you see in these pictures?","a":"The two images seem to portray different approaches to writing. In one of them, an individual is writing with a pen on paper, which suggests a more traditional and personal form of communication. This method is commonly used in situations like note-taking, journaling, or completing written assignments. The other picture appears to involve someone using a computer keyboard to type text. This approach reflects the influence of modern technology on the way people produce written content today. Typing allows individuals to compose, revise, and store information digitally. Taken together, the images illustrate the contrast between manual writing and technology-based text production."},{"q":"Which do you prefer: handwriting or typing?","a":"If I were asked to choose between the two, I would probably favor typing. Using a keyboard enables people to write much more quickly and organize their ideas efficiently, particularly when producing longer texts. Even so, handwriting still has certain advantages. For instance, writing things down\n\nmanually can sometimes improve concentration and make it easier to retain information."},{"q":"Do you think handwriting will disappear in the future?","a":"Despite the rapid growth of digital technology, it seems unlikely that handwriting will vanish entirely. In many educational contexts, students are still encouraged to write by hand in order to develop fundamental writing skills. Furthermore, handwritten notes can feel more personal and meaningful, which is why this form of writing will probably remain relevant even in a highly digital world."}]},"p2":{"img":"img/sp/b3t20_2.jpg","qs":["Describe a decision that changed your perspective.","What made this decision important for you?","How did it influence the way you think now?"],"a":"One decision that changed my perspective was choosing to approach challenges with a more positive and patient mindset. In the past, whenever I faced difficulties, I sometimes felt frustrated if progress was slow. However, after reflecting on my experiences, I realized that challenges are often valuable opportunities for learning and growth. This decision became important for me because it influenced the way I respond to difficult situations. Instead of focusing only on problems, I started looking for ways to learn from them. I began to see obstacles not as failures but as steps that can help me improve my skills and understanding. As a result, this change in perspective influenced the way I think about both success and failure. I now understand that progress usually takes time and consistent effort. This mindset\n\nhas helped me remain more patient and determined when working toward my goals. It also encourages me to continue learning from every experience, whether it is positive or challenging."},"p3":{"card":null,"topic":"Standardized testing should be removed from school systems","for":["standardized tests do not always reflect students' true abilities","they can create excessive stress and pressure for students","education may become too focused on memorization instead of real understanding"],"against":["standardized tests provide a clear and consistent way to evaluate students","they help schools and governments measure educational performance","universities often rely on standardized results for fair admissions decisions"],"a":"The idea that standardized testing should be removed from school systems is widely debated because such tests influence both educational evaluation and student experience.\n\nOne argument in favour of removing standardized testing is that these exams do not always reflect students' true abilities. Many students may perform poorly in exam situations despite having a good understanding of the subject. In addition, standardized tests can create excessive stress and pressure, especially when students believe that their future academic opportunities depend on a single exam. Another concern is that education may become too focused on memorization rather than genuine understanding, as teachers sometimes prioritize preparing students for tests instead of encouraging critical thinking and deeper learning.\n\nHowever, there are also strong arguments against eliminating standardized testing entirely. These exams provide\n\na clear and consistent way to evaluate students from different schools and regions using the same criteria. This allows educational institutions and governments to measure educational performance and identify areas that require improvement. Furthermore, universities often rely on standardized test results when making admission decisions because they provide a relatively fair method of comparing applicants from different educational backgrounds.\n\nCAMBRIDGESCHOOL– NATI\n\nJAGAI\n\nSHLAYDI\n\nGAN MAKTAB\n\nI ELTS9.\n\n0gachat\n\najr\n\nibal\n\nius\n\ntoz\n\nlar\n\n;\n\nHaryi\n\nl\n\niko'\n\npl\n\nabyuqor\n\ninat\n\nij\n\nal\n\nar;\n\nO'\n\nquv\n\nchi\n\nl\n\naruchunavt\n\nobusxi\n\nzmat\n\ni;\n\n5mahal\n\nto'\n\nl\n\niqv\n\nasog'\n\nl\n\nomov\n\nqat\n\nlani\n\nsh;\n\nO'\n\nrgani\n\nsh,\n\nyashas\n\nhvar\n\nivoj\n\nl\n\nani\n\nshuchun mukammalj\n\noy;\n\nHarbi\n\nro'\n\nquv\n\nchi\n\nust\n\nidannaz\n\norat\n\n;\n\nQul\n\nayv\n\naxavf\n\nsi\n\nzyot\n\noqx\n\nona."},"words":[]}]};
